1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hrómundar saga Gripssonar or The Saga of Hromund Gripsson is a legendary saga from Iceland. The original version has been lost, but its content has been preserved in the rímur of Hrómundr Gripsson, known as Griplur
2 CONC , which were probably composed in the first half of the 14th century, but appeared in print in 1896 in Fernir forníslenzkar rímnaflokkar, edited by Finnur Jónsson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is probably not a historic account of real events since it was remarked by king Sverre of Norway, who heard it, that it was an amusing "lying tale" (lygisaga). Nonetheless, according to Landnámabók, Hrómundr Gripsson was the pa
2 CONC ternal great-grandfather of Ingolfr Arnarson, the first settler in Iceland. This means that he would have lived in Norway in the first half of the 8th century, and it's not impossible that stories about an ancestor who did exist w
2 CONC ere handed down by his Icelandic descendants (probably becoming increasingly embellished as time passed).
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hr%C3%B3mundar_saga_Gripssonar
