1 NOTE "HJORT"; KING OF RINGERIKE
1 NOTE Kong Harald Granraude  Konge i Agder på 800-tallet. Far til dronning Åsa. Da sendemenne til Gudrød Veidekonge kom for å fri til datteren hans, Åsa, sa han nei. Dette likte ikke Gødrød og dro til Agder med en stor hær, kringsatte h
2 CONC uset til Harald Granraude. Det ble kamp og Harald Granraude falt. Gudrød Veidekonge tok stort hærfang og datteren til Harald, Åsa, med seg hjem og tok henne til ektemake. Granraude betyr "han med rødt skjegg".
1 NOTE Cause of his death was he was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Halvdan Svarte [Halfdan the Black] Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "5. HALFDAN'S MARRIAGE WITH HJORT'S DAUGHTER.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigurd Hjort was the name of a king in Ringerike, who was stouter and stronger than any other man, and his equal could not be seen for a handsome appearance. His father was Helge Hvasse (the Sharp); and his mother was Aslaug, a da
2 CONC ughter of Sigurd the worm- eyed, who again was a son of Ragnar Lodbrok. It is told of Sigurd that when he was only twelve years old he killed in single combat the berserk Hildebrand, and eleven others of his comrades; and many are
2 CONC  the deeds of manhood told of him in a long saga about his feats. Sigurd had two children, one of whom was a daughter, called Ragnhild, then twenty years of age, and an excellent brisk girl. Her brother Guthorm was a youth. It is 
2 CONC related in regard to Sigurd's death that he had a custom of riding out quite alone in the uninhabited forest to hunt the wild beasts that are hurtful to man, and he was always very eager at this sport. One day he rode out into the
2 CONC  forest as usual, and when he had ridden a long way he came out at a piece of cleared land near to Hadeland. There the berserk Hake came against him with thirty men, and they fought. Sigurd Hjort fell there, after killing twelve o
2 CONC f Hake's men; and Hake himself lost one hand, and had three other wounds."
1 NOTE OCCUPATION: Konge på Ringerike
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH: Hadeland 
1 NOTE SOURCE NOTES:
2 CONT Snorre 45 http://home.sol.no/~nermo/slekt/d0009/g0000041.html#I1520 +
2 CONT http://www.northvegr.org/lore/oldheathen/056.php
1 NOTE Sigurd (Hjort) HELGESSON Antavla
2 CONT Yrke: Kung i Ringerike och Oplandene, Norge
2 CONT Far: Helge den HVASSE (780 - )
2 CONT Mor: Aslug SIGURDSDOTTER (780 - )
2 CONT
2 CONT Händelse Datum Plats Källa
2 CONT Födelse omkr 810 Norge, Buskerud, Ringerike Egen beräkning
2 CONT Död efter 840 Norge, Buskerud, Ringerike Egen beräkning
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Tyrne HARALDSDOTTER (812 - 840)
2 CONT Barn: Ragnhild SIGURDSDOTTER (840 - 858)
2 CONT
2 CONT Det står og om han i Snorre:
2 CONT Halvdan Svartes saga:
2 CONT "Sigurd Hjort het en konge på Ringerike Far hans var Helge den
2 CONT Kvasse og mor hans var Åslaug, datter til Sigurd Orm-i-auga, Ragnar Lodbroks
2 CONT sønn".
2 CONT
2 CONT 887309914. Kong Sigurd Hiort HELGISSON på Romerike (22185) was a Konge in Romerike. (22186) Han var større og sterkere enn alle andre. Det sies at han bare 12 år gammel drepte berserken Hildebrand og 11 av hans menn i enekamp. S
2 CONC igurd øvet mange storverk, men en dag han red på jakt efter storvildt, vlev han nær Hadeland drept av Hake berserk med 30 menn. Hake førte Sigurds datter Ragnhild til sin gård på Hadeland og holdt henne der, men måtte senere g
2 CONC i henne til Halvdan Svarte. He was married to Thorny KLACKSDOTTIR
1 NOTE Saga1, 43.
1 NOTE RESEARCH NOTES:
2 CONT King of Ringerike, Norway
2 CONT Of all the men ever seen, he was the fairest, and the biggest, and the
2 CONT strongest. When Sigurd was twelve, he killed the berserk Hildibrand in a duel,
2 CONT and he single-handedly slew twelve men in that fight. After that Klakk-Harald
2 CONT gave him his daughter, who was called Ingibjorg. They had two children:
2 CONT Gudthorm and Ragnhild.
2 CONT
2 CONT Then Sigurd learnt that King Frodi, his father's brother, was dead. He went
2 CONT north to Norway and became king over Ringerike, his inheritance.
