1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tyrne Haraldsdotter (Þórný Haraldsdóttir)
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English: Thorny Haraldsdotter)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=nor&person=Tyrne%20Haraldsdotter
2 CONT
2 CONT B.Brox: Since to many mix Tyrne with her sister Thyra Dannebod and some sources also operates with the name Ingeborg on her we have decided to use both names and keep Ingeborg as her first name.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Halvdan Svarte [Halfdan the Black] Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "5. HALFDAN'S MARRIAGE WITH HJORT'S DAUGHTER.
2 CONT
2 CONT ... Ragnhild's mother was Thorny, a daughter of Klakharald king in Jutland, and a sister of Thrye Dannebod who was married to the Danish king, Gorm the Old, who then ruled over the Danish dominions."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the assumed chronology makes it impossible to have a daughter of Harald be identical to [http://www.geni.com/people/Thyra-Danebod-Dronning-af-Vest-Danmark/5473900875460120094 Thyra Danebod], so this statement is likely f
2 CONC alse.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Tyrne married Sigurd "Hjort" Helgasson, son of Helge den Kvasse and Åslaug Sigurdsdatter. (Sigurd "Hjort" Helgasson was born between 810 & 815 in Ringerike, Norway and died in 856 in Ringerike, Norway.) The cause of his death was 
2 CONC he was killed.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 0820 - ____
2 CONT
