1 NOTE Harald Klak of Denmark fled his country, and went to the Frankish court of Louis the Pious, where Harald was convinced to convert and was baptised about 826.  He returned to Denmark the next year, and took with him the Frankish mo
2 CONC nk Ansgar to preach Christianity in Denmark.  But Klak's authority at home was disregarded and short lived, he was driven out again by Haarik.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 824 Harald I Klak of Denmark became the first known of the Danish Kings.  He was driven out by Haarik Godfredsson in 826, and Harald fled to France.  He returned about 827 and resumed his throne, but was again driven out by 
2 CONC Haarik in 828 or 829.
