1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Siggeir''' is named in ''Hversu Noregr byggðist''. He corresponds to [https://www.geni.com/people/Siggeir-king-of-Gautland-Volsunga-saga/6000000056317905874 Siggeir, king of Gautland] in ''Volsunga saga''.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Ættartolur", the genealogies appended to the ''Hversu Noregr byggdist'':
2 CONT
2 CONT >"''Sigarr was the father of '''Siggeir''', who married Signy, the daughter of the king of the Volsungs. Sigarr was also the father of Sigmund, who married Hilda, daughter of Grjotgard, King of Maeri. His son was named Sigarr, fat
2 CONC her of Signy. He had Hagbard hanged. That is the dynasty of the Siklings.''"
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikipedia ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Siggeir is the king of Gautland (i.e. Götaland/Geatland, but in some translations also rendered as Gothland), in the ''Völsunga saga''. In ''Skáldskaparmál'' he is given as a Sikling and a relative of Sigar who killed the hero Hag
2 CONC bard. ''Hversu Noregr byggðist'' specifies that the last Sigar was Siggeir's nephew.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/FraFornjotiHardman.html
2 CONT * http://www.norsesaga.no/hvorledes-norge-ble-bosatt.html
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siggeir
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigar var far til Siggeir, som var gift med Signyju, datter til kong Volsung. Sigar var også far til Sigmund, gift med Hild, datter til kong Grjotgard av Møre. Hans sønn het Sigar, far til Signyju. Han lot henge Hagbard. Dette het
2 CONC er Siklingeætten.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kilde:''' 
