2 ADDR
3 CTRY France
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1155
1 OCCU seigneur de Wavrin Saint Venant & Malanoy, Sieur, de Wavrin, Sénéchal, de Flandre
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please read .......
2 CONT  Maison de Wavrin
2 CONT
2 CONT http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Wavrin.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfranord.htm#RogerIIWavrindiedbefore1107<br/>
2 CONT 1.         ROGER [II] de Wavrin (-before 1107).  He is named in his wife’s 1107 donation but no primary source has been identified which names him in his own capacity.  Dereine suggests that Roger died during the First Crusade[652
2 CONC ], but if that is correct it is surprising that his widow would have waited until 1107 before making a donation for his soul (see below).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' as her first husband, EMMISSA “comitissa” [de Valenciennes], daughter of ISAAC [de Valenciennes] & his wife Mathilde --- (-after 1143).  Her parentage and first two marriages are confirmed by the charter dated 1107 under w
2 CONC hich "Emmissa quæ cognominor comitissa, Isaac et Maltheldis filia, Fastrei de Fossato conjunx" granted revenue rights to the church of Saint-Jean-Baptiste de Valenciennes, for the souls of "patris et matris [et] domini mei…Rogeri…
2 CONC de Wavring", signed by "Godefridi, Hugonis, castellanorum de Valentianis, Godzewini de Avesnes…"[653].   She married secondly Fastré de Fossé and thirdly Godfried [I] van Aarschot.  Her third marriage is confirmed by the charter d
2 CONC ated 1139 under which "Emeza, quæ cognominor comitissa, Ysaac et Mathildis filia, uxor Godefridi de Arescot" donated revenue rights to the abbey of Liessies, with the consent of "Balduino Montensi comite"[654].  Baudouin IV Comte 
2 CONC de Hainaut confirmed that "comitissa, uxor Godefridi de Arscoth" renounced her rights in the forest of Vicogne in favour of the abbey of Vicogne by charter dated 1143[655]. 
