1 NAME Thrand Norsson, king of Trondheim
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 PLAC Raumsdal, Norway
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Norway
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thránd ruled Trondheim (Þrándheimr) which was named after him and refers approximately to present day county of Sør-Trøndelag and the southern parts of Nord-Trøndelag, rather than to the city now called Trondheim.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Hversu Noregr byggdist'' ('How Norway was Settled') says he was a son of [http://www.geni.com/people/Norr-Thorrasson-King-in-Alfheim/6000000005946368472 Nórr], legendary founder of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Eireks saga víðförla'' ('The Saga of Eirek the Traveller') also brings in Thrand as the first king to reign in Trondheim. Thrand's ancestry is not given here, but he is the father of Eirek the Traveller (Eirekr inn víðfǫrli) the
2 CONC  hero of the saga.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Hálfdanar saga Eysteinssonar'' ('Saga of Halfdan Eystein's son', early 14th century) states instead that Trondheim was named from King Thránd, the father of Eirek the Traveller, but also states that Thrand was son of King [http:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/people/Saemingr-Odinsson/6000000006271194025 Sæmingr of Hálogaland], son of [http://www.geni.com/people/%C3%93%C3%B0inn-Woden-Woutan/6000000001169221592 Odin], and that Thránd's mother and Sæmingr's wife was [http:/
2 CONC /www.geni.com/people/Nauma/6000000000462674113 Nauma] after whom Naumu Dale was named. For more on Sæmingr see Sons of Odin. Thrand's wife is here said to be Dagmær sister of Svanhvít the wife of Hrómund Grip's son, the protagonis
2 CONC t of Hrómundar saga Gripssonar. The saga says that Eystein, son of Thrand and Dagmær, married Ása, a daughter of Sigurd Hart (the maternal grandfather of Harald Fairhair), and she bore him Halfdan, the hero of the saga. This place
2 CONC s Thrand just three generations back from Harald Fairhair. But this saga seems to be a late and untraditional creation, dating only to the early 14th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Primary Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/HversuNoregrDasent.html How Norway was Settled]
2 CONT * [http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/HalfdanEysteinssonHardman.html Saga of Halfdan Eysteinsson]
2 CONT * [http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/EireksSagaVidforlaTunstall.html The Tale of Eirek the Traveller]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Secondary Sources ==
2 CONT
