1 OCCU King of Kvenland, Konge av Kvenland, Kung av Kvenland, Myth King of Finland
1 TITL King
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thorri var en navngjeten konge som rådde over Gotland, Kvenland og Finland. Til ham blotet kvenene for å få snø og godt skiføre. Dette var deres beste tid. Blotet skulle være midt på vinteren, og derfor kalles det 
2 CONC siden Thorremåned.  Kong Thorri hadde tre barn; sønnene hans het Nor og Gor, og datteren Goi. Goi ble borte og Thorri blotet da en måned senere enn han pleide å blote, og siden kalte de denne måneden de da hadde framfor seg for Go
2 CONC i. Nor og Gor lette etter søsteren sin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Legendary king in part of Sveden.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N%C3%B3r he is described in two quite similiar stories of the "Flateyarbok" (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flatey_Book) as the king of Götaland, Finland and Kvenland, and the father of Nor 
2 CONC the founder of Norway and Gorr, the founder of Dennmark, as well as a daughter, Goi.
2 CONT
2 CONT The two accounts (Fundinn Noregr and Hversu Noregr Bygddist) differ on some points.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorri was a great sacrificer, he had a sacrifice every year at midwinter; that they called Thorri’s sacrifice; from that the month took its name. One winter there were these tidings at Thorri’s sacrifice, that Goi was lost and go
2 CONC ne, and they set out to search for her, but she was not found. And when that month passed away Thorri made them take to sacrifice, and sacrifice for this, that they might know surely where Goi was hidden away. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorri was also 12th great grandfather to legendary Viking, Ragnar Sigurdson Lodbrok. https://www.geni.com/people/Ragnar-Lodbrok-Sigurdsson/5604233735830047570 
2 CONT
