2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Granraude was a king of the district Agder, Norway, and lived in the 9th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Gunhild Ragnvaldsdatter, daughter of Ragnvald Sigurdsson, Lord of Huseby on Lista. He was father to Åsa Haraldsdatter and Gyrd Haraldsson, and great-grandfather of Harald Hårfagre, the first king of Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the king of Vestfold, Gudrød the Hunter, sent men to propose to Haralds daughter Åsa, Harald answered no. This made Gudrød angry and he sailed with his ships the king's farm on Tromøy. He arrived at night and attacked Harald'
2 CONC s farm in a surprise attack. When Harald saw an army was coming he retaliated with all his men. It was a hard battle, and Harald lost. He and his son were killed. King Gudrød looted Harald's treasure, and took and married Åsa.
2 CONT
2 CONT A local legend says that Harald Granraude hid in an underground tunnel with his daughter Åsa during the attack, but was found and beheaded.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harald_Granraude
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Granraude was a king of the district Agder, Norway, and lived in the 9th century.
