1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Eylimi''' is named in the ''Ættartolur'', the genealogy section of ''Hversum Noreg byggdist''. He corresponds to the fictional [https://www.geni.com/people/King-Eylimi-Volsunga-saga/6000000003796287385 King Eyli
2 CONC mi] in the ''Volsunga saga''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ættartolur: "Lofdi was a great king. The troops, which he commanded, are called Lofdar. He plundered in Reidgotaland and became king there. His sons were Skekkill the Sea-king, and Skyli, father of Egdis, father of Hjalmthes, fat
2 CONC her of '''Eylima''', father of Hjordi, mother of Sigurdar Fafnisbana, father of Aslaug, mother of Sigurd Serpent-Eye, father of Aslaug, mother of Sigurd Hjarta, father of Ragnhild, mother of Harald Fair-haired. These relatives of 
2 CONC Harald are called Lofdungs."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lofdungs ''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lofdi was a great king who raided Reidgotaland (Reiðgotaland) and became king there. Lofdi's sons were Skekkil Sea-king (Skekkill sækonungr) and Skyli. Skyli was father of Egdir (Egðir), the father of Hjálmthér (Hjálmþér), the fat
2 CONC her of '''Eylimi''', the father of Hjördís (Hjǫrdís), the mother of Sigurd Fáfnir's-bane, father of Áslaug (Áslaugr) by Brynhild whose ancestry appears below in the Budling discussion. This Áslaug was a wife of Ragnar Lodbrok and 
2 CONC by him the mother of Sigurd Snake-in-the-Eye (Sigurðr ormr í auga) who was father of a second Áslaug who was mother of Sigurd Hart. Sigurd Hart was father of Ragnhild (Ragnhildr), mother of Harald Fairhair as already stated.
2 CONT
2 CONT But stanza 26 of the ''Hyndluljód'' identifies Eylimi the father of Hjördís as an Ödling.
2 CONT
