2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT In Norse mythology, Aurboða (Old Norse "gravel-bidder" or "gravel-offerer"[1]) is a mountain jötunn, wife to the jötunn Gymir, and mother of Gerðr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attestations
2 CONT
2 CONT Aurboða is attested in the Poetic Edda; compiled in the 13th century from earlier traditional sources, and the Prose Edda written in the 13th century by Snorri Sturluson. Aurboða is also the name of one of nine maidens who sit at 
2 CONC the knees of Menglöd in the poem Svipdagsmál. Aurboða is sometimes anglicized as Aurboda.
2 CONT
