1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mythology.
2 CONT
2 CONT Driva norr. Drífa Snæsdóttir, datter av Snø den gamle og søster til Torre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT    http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr%C3%ADfa_Sn%C3%A6sd%C3%B3ttir
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vanlandi or Vanlande was a Swedish king at Uppsala of the House of Yngling in Norse mythology. He was the son of Sveigðir whom he succeeded as king. He married a girl from Finnland (territories inhabited by Finno-Ugric peoples), b
2 CONC ut forgot about her. In revenge, the girl arranged so that Vanlandi was hag ridden to death. He was succeeded by his son Visbur. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vanlande, Swegde's son, succeeded his father, and ruled over the Upsal domain. He was a great warrior, and went far around in different lands. Once he took up his winter abode in Finland with Snae the Old, and got his daughter Dri
2 CONC va in marriage; but in spring he set out leaving Driva behind, and although he had promised to return within three years he did not come back for ten. Then Driva sent a message to the witch Huld; and sent Visbur, her son by Vanlan
2 CONC de, to Sweden. Driva bribed the witch- wife Huld, either that she should bewitch Vanlande to return to Finland, or kill him. When this witch-work was going on Vanlande was at Upsal, and a great desire came over him to go to Finlan
2 CONC d; but his friends and counsellors advised him against it, and said the witchcraft of the Finn people showed itself in this desire of his to go there. He then became very drowsy, and laid himself down to sleep; but when he had sle
2 CONC pt but a little while he cried out, saying that the Mara was treading upon him. His men hastened to him to help him; but when they took hold of his head she trod on his legs, and when they laid hold of his legs she pressed upon hi
2 CONC s head; and it was his death. The Swedes took his body and burnt it at a river called Skytaa, where a standing stone was raised over him
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Driva norr. Drífa Snæsdóttir, datter av Snø den gamle og søster til Torre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilder:
2 CONT
2 CONT   http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr%C3%ADfa_Sn%C3%A6sd%C3%B3ttir
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Vanlandi or Vanlande was a Swedish king at Uppsala of the House of Yngling in Norse mythology. He was the son of Sveigðir whom he succeeded as king. He married a girl from Finnland (territories inhabited by Finno-Ugric peoples), b
2 CONC ut forgot about her. In revenge, the girl arranged so that Vanlandi was hag ridden to death. He was succeeded by his son Visbur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vanlande, Swegde's son, succeeded his father, and ruled over the Upsal domain. He was a great warrior, and went far around in different lands. Once he took up his winter abode in Finland with Snae the Old, and got his daughter Dri
2 CONC va in marriage; but in spring he set out leaving Driva behind, and although he had promised to return within three years he did not come back for ten. Then Driva sent a message to the witch Huld; and sent Visbur, her son by Vanlan
2 CONC de, to Sweden. Driva bribed the witch- wife Huld, either that she should bewitch Vanlande to return to Finland, or kill him. When this witch-work was going on Vanlande was at Upsal, and a great desire came over him to go to Finlan
2 CONC d; but his friends and counsellors advised him against it, and said the witchcraft of the Finn people showed itself in this desire of his to go there. He then became very drowsy, and laid himself down to sleep; but when he had sle
2 CONC pt but a little while he cried out, saying that the Mara was treading upon him. His men hastened to him to help him; but when they took hold of his head she trod on his legs, and when they laid hold of his legs she pressed upon hi
2 CONC s head; and it was his death. The Swedes took his body and burnt it at a river called Skytaa, where a standing stone was raised over him
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Driva var gift med Vanlande och bodde i Finland. Vanlande hade lovat att åtevända till Finland efter tre år men det gick tio år utan att han kom. Driva skickade då iväg deras son till sin far och hoppas att han skulle förmå sin fa
2 CONC r att antigen återvända eller att han skulle hjälpa till med att döda sin far. Vanlande dog av Mara.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.genealogieonline.nl/en/stamboom-homs/I5622011688610034767.php
2 CONT
2 CONT Suomennos:
2 CONT Vanlandi eli Vanlande oli ruotsalainen kuningas Uppsalassa, joka kuului pohjoismaisessa mytologiassa Ynglingin sukuun. Hän oli Sveigðirin poika, jonka hän seurasi kuninkaana. Hän meni naimisiin Suomesta (suomalais-ugrilaisten kans
2 CONC ojen asuttama alue) kotoisin olevan tytön kanssa, mutta unohti hänet. Kostoksi tyttö järjesti niin, että Vanlandin noita ratsastettiin kuoliaaksi. Hänen seuraajakseen tuli hänen poikansa Visbur.
2 CONT
2 CONT Swegden poika Vanlande seurasi isäänsä ja hallitsi Upsalin aluetta. Hän oli suuri soturi ja matkusti kauas eri maihin. Kerran hän asettui talviasunnolle Suomeen Vanhan Snaein luokse ja otti tyttärensä Drivan vaimoksi. Keväällä hän
2 CONC  kuitenkin lähti matkaan jättäen Drivan taakseen, ja vaikka hän oli luvannut palata kolmen vuoden kuluessa, hän ei palannut kymmeneen vuoteen. Sitten Driva lähetti viestin noita Huldille ja lähetti Visburin, hänen ja Vanlanden poj
2 CONC an, Ruotsiin. Driva lahjoi noitavaimo Huldin joko lumoamaan Vanlanden palaamaan Suomeen tai tappamaan hänet. Kun tämä noituutta harjoitettiin, Vanlande oli Upsalissa, ja häneen valtasi suuri halu mennä Suomeen; mutta hänen ystävän
2 CONC sä ja neuvonantajansa neuvoivat häntä olemaan tekemättä sitä ja sanoivat, että suomalaisten noituus ilmeni tässä hänen halussaan mennä sinne. Sitten hänestä tuli hyvin unelias ja hän kävi nukkumaan; mutta nukuttuaan vain hetken hä
2 CONC n huusi ja sanoi, että Mara tallasi häntä. Hänen miehensä kiiruhtivat hänen luokseen auttamaan häntä; mutta kun he tarttuivat hänen päähänsä, Mara tallasi hänen jalkojaan, ja kun he tarttuivat hänen jalkoihinsa, hän painoi hänen p
2 CONC äätään; ja se oli hänen kuolemansa. Ruotsalaiset ottivat hänen ruumiinsa ja polttivat sen Skytaa-nimisessä joessa, jossa hänen päälleen pystytettiin seisova kivi.
