2 CONT
2 CONT An elegant and slender ship. The wood carvings of the stave friezes (loops of very high artistic quality. In this ship, Queen Åsa, King Harald (Hårfager's) grandmother may have been buried during the latter half of the ninth centu
2 CONC ry.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Oseberg ship was found in 1903 in a burial mound on the west side of the Oslo Fjord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Vikangatiden mythology and reality" by Nils Erik Hennix and Lennaart Denne.
