1 NOTE Visbur was a Swedish King who was killed by his sons from his first wife. After Visbur sent away his first wife and two sons in order to take another wife, the first wife sent the two sons back to Visbur to ask him to return their
2 CONC  mother’s dowry - three large farms and a gold ornament. Visbur refused to return anything to them. During the night they gathered a group of men and went to Visbur’s house where they burned the house with Visbur in it.
1 NOTE G6SX-VP
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. The Viking Age, Gen. Hist. 19, v. 1, p. 67
2 CONT     2. Attarskra Bjarni Thorsteinsson, Ice FH 1, p. 433
