1 OCCU Konge i Vestfold og Romerike, Rey en Vestfold, Konge, Roi, de Danemark, Konge først på 800-tallet, King of Vestfold and Romerike, Kung av Vestfold och Romerike, Kung 760-826 i Vestfold, Rusled 800-10, Kung, Konge av Vestfold, Kong
2 CONC e først på 800 tallet
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.friesian.com/germania.htm#orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.friesian.com/germania.htm#norse
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød the Hunter (Old Norse: Guðrǫðr veiðikonungr, Norwegian: Gudrød Veidekonge) was a semi-legendary king in south-east Norway, during the early Viking Age. He is mentioned in the skaldic poem Ynglingatal. Snorri Sturluson elabo
2 CONC rates on Gudrød's story in Heimskringla, written c. 1230; however, this is not considered to be a historical account by modern historians. The following account is taken from Heimskringla - Ynglingesoga section 48:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød was the son of Halfdan the Mild of the House of Yngling and Liv Dagsdotter of Vestmar. He married Alfhild, a daughter of Alfarin the king of Alfheim (Bohuslän), which was the name of the area between Glomma and Göta älv, an
2 CONC d inherited half the province of Vingulmark. They had a son, Olaf Gudrødsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Alfhild died, Gudrød sent his warriors to Agder and its king, Harald, to propose a marriage with his daughter Åsa. However, Harald Granraude declined, so Gudrød decided to take his daughter by force.
2 CONT
2 CONT They arrived at night. When Harald realised that he was being attacked, he assembled his men and fought well, but died together with his son Gyrd. Gudrød carried away Åsa and married her. He raped her and she gave him a son named 
2 CONC Halfdan who would be called Halfdan the Black.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fall, when Halfdan was a year old, Gudrød was having at a feast in Stiflesund. He was very drunk and in the evening, as he was walking on the gangway to leave the ship, an assassin thrust a spear through Gudrød, killing him
2 CONC . Gudrød's men instantly killed the assassin, who turned out to be Åsa's page-boy. Åsa admitted that the page-boy had acted on her behalf.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT GENI NOTE: There is another Gudrød son of Halfdan, who is not the same as this one. This one is Gudrød son of Halfdan son of Eyvind; the other one is Gudrød son of Halfdan "Kvitbein" son of Olaf.
2 CONT
2 CONT Take care!
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød Veidekonge (Halvdansson) (Guðröður veiðikonung)
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English: Gudrod the Hunter)
2 CONT
2 CONT King in part of Norway: Vestfold / Vingulmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternative fødselsår: 738, 765, 780
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternative dødsår: 810, 821
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.snl.no/.nbl_biografi/Gudr%C3%B8d_Veidekonge/utdypning
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gudr%C3%B8d_Halvdansson_Veidekonge
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gudr%C3%B8d_the_Hunter
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=no&emne=asatru&person=Gudr%F8d%20Veidekonge%20%28Halvdansson%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Mens skipet hans lå i “Stivlesund” (et ukjent sted), ble han offer for et snikmord. Morderen var Åsas skosvein, og det ble ikke lagt skjul på at hun stod bak. Hva som skjedde med Åsa etterpå, sies det ingenting om i sagaene.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød Veidekonge – og for så vidt også Åsa (men ikke nødvendigvis under dette navnet) – må oppfattes som gamle sagnskikkelser i skandinavisk/nordeuropeisk sammenheng. Gudrød svarer som skikkelse i noen grad til en legendarisk dan
2 CONC sk konge, Godofridus, som regjerte på begynnelsen av 800-tallet og er nevnt i frankiske kilder. Men han har også lånt trekk fra andre “Gudrød”-skikkelser (blant dem en norsk Dublin-konge). Ifølge en av de frankiske kildene ble God
2 CONC ofridus drept i et familiedrama, og hustruen stod bak drapet.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød the Hunter (Old Norse: Guðrǫðr veiðikonungr, Norwegian: Gudrød Veidekonge) was a semi-legendary king in south-east Norway, during the early Viking Age. He is mentioned in the skaldic poem Ynglingatal. Snorri Sturluson elabo
2 CONC rates on Gudrød's story in Heimskringla, written c. 1230; however, this is not considered to be a historical account by modern historians.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Konge først på 800-tallet
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød Veidekonge
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød Veidekonge (dvs. jegeren, av gn. veidr, jakt) ifølge Snorre konge over Vestfold og Romerike. Gudrød drepte Agderkongen, hærtok og ektet hans datter Åsa, som fødte han sønnen:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Halvdan Svarte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød ble drept av Åsas trell. 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Gyldendals Store Konversasjonsleksikon (1965) D-G, sid. 3271.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød Halvdansson Veidekonge (født ca. 780 død ca. 821) var konge over Vestfold, Romerike og halve Vingulmark (omtrent dagens Østfold). Gudrød var Halvdan Øysteinsson den gavmilde og Liv Dagsdotters sønn, og far til Halvdan Svart
2 CONC e og Olav Geirstadalv Gudrødsson. Frem til ca. 815 var han gift med Alvhild Alfarinsdatter, og deretter med Åsa Haraldsdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød fikk halve Vingulmark som medgifte da han giftet seg med Alvhild, datter av kong Alvarin Alvheim fra Alvheim (Bohuslän).
2 CONT
2 CONT Etter Alfhilds tidlige død, la Gudrød ut på frierferd til Agder, etter datteren til kong Harald Granraude, Åsa. Harald avviste ham og Gudrød svarte med å ta livet av ham og hans sønn Gyrd, for så å røve med seg Åsa og ta henne til
2 CONC  ektemake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød ble myrdet i 821, på ordre fra Åsa, for mordet på hennes far og bror, og for å ha voldtatt henne.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Forgjenger:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Halvdan Øysteinsson den gavmilde  Konge av Vestfold (ca. 800–821) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Etterfølger:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Olav Geirstadalv Gudrødsson 
2 CONT
2 CONT Forgjenger:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Harald Granraude  Konge av Agder (ca. 815–ca. 821) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Etterfølger:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Åsa Haraldsdotter  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Han var Veidekonge. (Den stormodige) 2. gang gift med Åsa Haraldsdtr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 53. OF GUDROD THE HUNTER.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrod, Halfdan's son, succeeded. He was called Gudrod the Magnificent, and also Gudrod the Hunter. He was married to Alfhild, a daughter of King Alfarin of Alfheim, and got with her half the district of Vingulmark. Their son Olaf
2 CONC  was afterwards called Geirstad-Alf. Alfheim, at that time, was the name of the land between the Glommen and Gotha rivers. Now when Alfhild died, King Gudrod sent his men west to Agder to the king who ruled there, and who was call
2 CONC ed Harald Redbeard. They were to make proposals to his daughter Aasa upon the king's account; but Harald declined the match, and the ambassadors returned to the king, and told him the result of their errand. Soon after King
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrod hove down his ships into the water, and proceeded with a great force in them to Agder. He immediately landed, and came altogether unexpectedly at night to King Harald's house. When Harald was aware that an army was at hand,
2 CONC  he went out with the
2 CONT
2 CONT men he had about him, and there was a great battle, although he wanted men so much. King Harald and his son Gyrd fell, and King Gudrod took a great booty. He carried away with him Aasa, King Harald's daughter, and had a wedding wi
2 CONC th her. They had a son by their marriage called Halfdan; and the autumn that Halfdan was a year old Gudrod went upon a round of feasts. He lay with his ship in Stiflesund, where they had been drinking hard, so that the king was ve
2 CONC ry tipsy. In the evening, about dark, the king left the ship; and when he had got to the end of the gangway from the ship to the shore, a man ran against him, thrust a spear through him, and killed him. The man was instantly put t
2 CONC o death, and in the morning when it was light the man was discovered to be Aasa's page-boy: nor did she conceal that it was done by her orders. Thus tells Thjodolf of it: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "Gudrod is gone to his long rest,
2 CONT
2 CONT Despite of all his haughty pride --
2 CONT
2 CONT A traitor's spear has pierced his side:
2 CONT
2 CONT For Aasa cherished in her breast
2 CONT
2 CONT Revenge; and as, by wine opprest,
2 CONT
2 CONT The hero staggered from his ship,
2 CONT
2 CONT The cruel queen her thrall let slip
2 CONT
2 CONT To do the deed of which I sing:
2 CONT
2 CONT And now the far-descended king,
2 CONT
2 CONT At Stiflesund, in the old bed
2 CONT
2 CONT Of the old Gudrod race, lies dead."
2 CONT
2 CONT 54. OF KING OLAF'S DEATH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf came to the kingdom after his father. He was a great warrior, and an able man; and was besides remarkably handsome, very strong and large of growth. He had Westfold; for King Alfgeir took all Vingulmark to himself, and placed
2 CONC  his son Gandalf over it. Both father and son made war on Raumarike, and subdued the greater part of that land and district. Hogne was the name of a son of the Upland king, Eystein the Great, who subdued for himself the whole of H
2 CONC edemark, Toten, and Hadeland. Then Vermeland fell off from Gudrod's sons, and turned itself, with its payment of scatt, to the Swedish king. Olaf was about twenty years old when Gudrod died; and as his brother Halfdan now had the 
2 CONC kingdom with him, they divided it between them; so that Olaf got the eastern and Halfdan the southern part. King Olaf had his main residence at Geirstad. There he died of a disease in his foot, and was laid under a mound at Geirst
2 CONC ad. So sings Thjodolf: --
2 CONT
2 CONT "Long while this branch of Odin's stem
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the stout prop of Norway's realm;
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while King Olaf with just pride
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruled over Westfold far and wide.
2 CONT
2 CONT At length by cruel gout oppressed,
2 CONT
2 CONT The good King Olaf sank to rest:
2 CONT
2 CONT His body now lies under ground,
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at Geirstad, in the mound."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Alvhild ALVARINDOTTER (765 - 819)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigsel: omkring 780 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik GUDRÖDSSON (782 - 854)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnvald GUDRÖDSSON (801 - 836)
2 CONT
2 CONT Familj med Åsa HARALDSDOTTER (800 - 834)
2 CONT
2 CONT Vigsel: omkring 820 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn:
2 CONT
2 CONT Halvdan (den svarte) GUDRÖDSSON (825 - 867)
2 CONT
2 CONT Men när Alfhild var död sände kung Gudröd sina män västerut till Agder, där det härskade en kung som är nämnd Harald den munskäggsröde. De hade i uppdrag att fria till hans dotter Åsa på kungens vägnar, men Harald sade nej. Sändem
2 CONC ännen kom tillbaka och förtalte kungen om utgången av ärendet. Något senare sköt kung Gudröds skepp i vattnet och for med en stor här till Agder, dit han kom helt oväntat och företog landgång och överföll kung Haralds gård om natt
2 CONC en. Men när denne blev varse att en här kom emot honom, då gick han ut med så mycket manskap han hade. Det vart strid, men skillnaden i styrka var stor och Harald stupade jämte sin son Gyrd. Kung Gudröd tog stort byte och förde me
2 CONC d sig hem kung Haralds dotter Åsa och höll bröllop med henne. De fick en enda son, som hette Halfdan. Samma höst som Halfdan blev en vinter gammal for kung Gudröd på gillen och låg med sitt i Stivlusund. Där var mycket drickande o
2 CONC ch kungen var svårt drucken, och på kvällen när det blev mörkt gick kungen ned ifrån skeppet. Men när han nådde landgångens ände lopp en man emot honom och rände ett spjut igenom honom, och det vart hans bane. Mannen dräptes på fl
2 CONC äcken, men om morgonen när det blev ljust kändes han igen, och det befanns vara drottning Åsas skosven. Hon förnekade då heller inte att rådet var hennes.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Källa: Vikingen, Nordbok 1975)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunröd den ädle. Gift först med Alfhild som var dotter till kung Alvarin från Alvhem.Med henne får han sonen Olof som blir kung i Vestvold. Efter Alfhilds död gifter han sig med Åsa som var dotter till kungen Harald den rödskäggie
2 CONC  i Agder och får med henne sonen Halfdan. Gunröd övertog kungadömet efter sin far.
2 CONT
2 CONT Se Ynglingasagan (YS) i Snorre Sturlassons kungasagor, sid 71-74. 
2 CONT
