2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gudr%C3%B8d_Halvdansson_Veidekonge
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudröd the Hunter was the son of Halfdan the Mild of the House of Yngling, according to Heimskringla, a collection of sagas from thirteenth century Iceland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudröd married Alfhild, a daughter of Alfarin the king of Alfheim (Bohuslän), which was the name of the area between Glomma and Göta älv, and inherited half the province of Vingulmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Alfhild died, Gudröd sent his warriors to Agder and its king Harald to propose a marriage with his daughter Åsa. However, Harald declined so Gudröd decided to take his daughter by force.
2 CONT
2 CONT They arrived at night time and when Harald realised that he was attacked he assembled his men and fought well, but died together with his son Gyrd. Gudröd carried away Åsa and married her. He raped her and she gave him a son named
2 CONC  Halfdan who would be called Halfdan the Black.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fall when Halfdan was a year old, Gudröd was having at a feast in Stiflesund. He was very drunk and in the evening as he was walking on the gangway to leave the ship, an assassin thrust a spear trough Gudröd and he was kill
2 CONC ed. Gudröd's men instantly killed the assassin who turned out to be Åsa's page-boy. Åsa admitted that the page-boy had acted on her behalf.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • He was a King from 00 0780 to 820 in Vestfold, Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudröd married Alfhild Alfarinsdatter, daughter of Alfarin of Alfheim and Unknown. (Alfhild Alfarinsdatter died before 820.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudröd next married Åsa Haraldsdatter, daughter of Harald Granraude and Unknown, circa 810. (Åsa Haraldsdatter was born circa 780 in Agder, Norway and died circa 840 in Norway.)
2 CONT
