2 DATE 1201
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted and translated from “Charles Poplimont. La Belgique héraldique : recueil historique, chronologique, généalogique et biographique complet de toutes les maisons nobles, T. 5-9.” Bruxelles: G. Adriaens, 1863-1867. Page 19-2
2 CONC 0. [https://books.google.com/books?id=mIFCAAAAcAAJ&lpg=PA23&ots=ka_bjedf6L&dq=Alix%20d%E2%80%99Aire%2C%20dame%20de%20Thiembronne&pg=PA19#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT II. GODEFROY DE NEDONCHEL [Geoffroi de Nédonchel], knight, Lord of Nedonchel, de Nedon, d'Estrées Blanches, etc., high baron of Boulonnais, witness in 1150, to the charter of an endowment made by Jean d'Humières and Richilde de Fo
2 CONC sseux at the Abbey of Mont Saint Martin, married Alette d'Humières, sister of Jean d'Humières, governor of the province of Artois in 1199, who married Agnès de Renty, ei d'Hugues d'Humières, lord of Cauchie, daughter of John, Lord
2 CONC  of Humieres of Huméreuil and of Millefau and of Richilde of Fosseux. He had by his marriage a son, Gilles, 1st  of the name, which follows, III.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. GILLES DE NEDONCHEL, ['''Gilles 1er de Nédonchel'''] lord of Nedonchel, de Nedon, de Ligny, etc., died around 1220, qualified in a charter of 1201, nephew of the lords of Bailleul and Thiem bronne, married, around 1175, Alis 
2 CONC or Adelis d ' Aire , daughter of Gislebert, Viscount of Aire and of Cassine of Saint Omer, which is proven by a donation to the religious of Clairmarais, of tithes and other feudal dues owed annually to the lord of Saint Omer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilles I of Nedonchel had seven children by his marriage, namely:
2 CONT
2 CONT * A. Berthold or Barthélemy, who follows, IV, after his brother Jean.
2 CONT * B. Guillaume DE NEDONCHEL, knight, mentioned in a role among several gentlemen following Eustache de Cbastillon, at the host of Bouvines, July 27, 1214.
2 CONT * C. John, which follows, IV.
2 CONT * D. Aelide, designated as sister of Lady Mathilde de Cresecques, in the obituary of the priory of Saint André, where she is recalled on the calendar day of June (1).
2 CONT * E. Mathilde, married Robert, Lord of Cresecques, whom she survived.
2 CONT * F. Helyide, died before 1220. 
2 CONT * G. Anne, living without marriage in 1220.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Nedonchel.pdf
