2 CONC rowned head, where battle plain, Was miry red with the blood-rain. But Domald dies by bloody arms, Raised not by foes in war's alarms Raised by his Swedish liegemen's hand, To bring good seasons to the land.[7][8] The Historia Nor
2 CONC wegiæ presents a Latin summary of Ynglingatal, older than Snorri's quotation:
