1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted and translated from “Charles Poplimont. La Belgique héraldique : recueil historique, chronologique, généalogique et biographique complet de toutes les maisons nobles, T. 5-9.” Bruxelles: G. Adriaens, 1863-1867. Page 21-2
2 CONC 3 [https://books.google.com/books?id=mIFCAAAAcAAJ&lpg=PA23&ots=ka_bjedf6L&dq=Alix%20d%E2%80%99Aire%2C%20dame%20de%20Thiembronne&pg=PA21#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT III. GILLES (er DE NEDONCHEL, lord of Nedonchel, de Nedon, de Ligny, etc., died around 1220, qualified in a charter of 1201, nephew of the lords of Bailleul and Thiem bronne, married, around 1175, Alis or Adelis d ' Aire , daughte
2 CONC r of Gislebert, Viscount of Aire and of Cassine of Saint Omer, which is proven by a donation to the religious of Clairmarais, of tithes and other feudal dues owed annually to the lord of Saint Omer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilles I of Nedonchel had seven children by his marriage, namely:
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Berthold or Barthélemy, who follows, IV, after his brother Jean.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. '''BERTHOLD or BARTHÉLEMI DE NEDONCHEL''', knight, sire and baron of Nedonchel, lord of Ligny, de Nedon, d'Auchel, de Liettres, etc., died around October 1249, took part, with other Flemish lords and artesians, at the fifth cr
2 CONC usade, in 1217. To meet the expenses of this expedition, he contracted, with another knight, named Hugues de Dona, a loan of one hundred and eighty pounds tournaments. It is probable that it was because of this expedition and to b
2 CONC ear the costs that Berthold de Nedonchel sold Nedon to the house ofMailly, who owns ELGIQUE HÉRALDIQUE, VIII. this land since that time. He found himself at the siege of Damietta, in the month of September 1218 and he was to retur
2 CONC n in the month of March 1225, shows that a donation he made at that time to the monastery of Saint Andrew. His seal, with the band, on horseback, sword high, is affixed to the loan contract that he concludes with Hugues de Dona, a
2 CONC nd it is according to the production of this title that his name and his arms can be found in the second crusades room at the Musée de Versailles.
2 CONT
2 CONT By letters of June 1246, he confirmed, with the consent of Gilles, his eldest son, a sale made to the monastery of Saint André of the goods located in his fief, at Westrehem, in the tenement of Girard de Chastel, his liege man. , 
2 CONC subject to the usufruct for his daughter Béatrix (2).
2 CONT
2 CONT He had married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 ° Marie d'Ollehain, daughter of Guillaume, Lord of Ollehain, and of Ursule of Colemberg, for whom he founded an obit in the monastery of Saint André; 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 ° Alix , lady of Thiembronne , daughter of Gilbert, lord of Aire .
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two children from the first lady, namely: 
2 CONT *A. Gilles, II of the name, which follows, V.
2 CONT *B. Beatrix, died before the month of October 1249, which is proved by the confirmation of Alix , Lady of Thiembronne , her mother-in-law, in favor of the monks of the monastery of Saint André of the goods of which Béatrix de Nedo
2 CONC nchel was the usufructuary, by virtue of the deed of gift of Barthélemi Nedonchel and his son, Gilles, knight, of the month of June 1246 (3).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://racineshistoire.free.fr/LGN/PDF/Nedonchel.pdf
2 CONT * Genealogie de la maison de Nedonchel en Artois et en Flandre. Publ. par ---By Louis Laine.  Page 10.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=zF9lAAAAcAAJ&lpg=PA14&ots=KAnGnf2pXd&dq=Alix%20d%E2%80%99Aire%2C%20dame%20de%20Thiembronne&
2 CONC pg=PA10#v=onepage&q=Alix%20d%E2%80%99Aire,%20dame%20de%20Thiembronne&f=false GoogleBooks] “Berthold de Nedonchel had them, among other children: to Gilles, 2nd of the name, which follows;  2 Béatrix de Nedonchel, died before Octob
2 CONC er 1249. At that time , Alix, lady Thiembronne , confirmed in favor of the religious of St. Andrew, property held viagèrement by said Beatrix , such as fire had granted Bartholomew of Nedonchel and Gilles, his eldest son, chevalie
2 CONC rs. ( Cartul . De Saint . André , part 2, Priviléges 45, page 18).“
2 CONT * “Charles Poplimont. La Belgique héraldique : recueil historique, chronologique, généalogique et biographique complet de toutes les maisons nobles, T. 5-9.” Bruxelles: G. Adriaens, 1863-1867.  Page 22-23. [https://www.ancestry.co
