2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan Haraldsson of Lethra King in Sweden & Denmark born Abt 0590 Of Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT died Abt 0650
2 CONT
2 CONT father:
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Valdarsson born Abt 0568 Of Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT mother:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hildur "Hildis" "Hervor" Heidreksdatter born Abt 0572 Of Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT married Abt 0589 Of, Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrud (Gudrod) Haraldsson born Abt 0592 Of Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT spouse:
2 CONT
2 CONT Moalda "Digri" Kinriksdatter born Abt 0594 Of Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT married Abt 0611 Of Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT (end of information)
2 CONT
2 CONT children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ivar "Vidfame" Halfdansson King in Sweden born Abt 0612 Of Denmark died 0647
2 CONT
2 CONT Hraeric of Lethra biographical and/or anecdotal:
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan was killed by his brother, Gudrod, "whom he also killed." The question is, were they dueling?
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Haldan the Valiant (Hálfdan snjalli) (7th century) was the legendary father of Ivar Vidfamne according to Hervarar saga, the Ynglinga saga, Njal's Saga and Hversu Noregr byggdist. The genealogical work Hversu Noregr byggdist gives
2 CONC  his father as Harald the Old, his grandfather as Valdar and his great-grandfather as Hróarr (i.e. the Hroðgar of Beowulf). Snorri Sturluson related that the Swedish king Ingjald Ill-ruler married his daughter Åsa to king Guðröðr 
2 CONC of Scania. Åsa was her father's daughter and made Guðröðr murder his own brother Halfdan, the father of Ivar Vidfamne. Later, she was the cause behind Guðröðr's death as well, and had to escape back to her father. People afterward
2 CONC s called her Åsa Ill-ruler like her father Ingjald. Ivar Vidfamne mustered a large army and besieged Ingjald and his daughter at Ræning, whereupon the two committed suicide by burning themselves to death inside the hall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Whereas Hversu and Ynglinga saga don't inform about Halfdan's mother, Hervarar saga provides the information that she was Hild, the daughter of the Gothic king Heiðrekr Ulfhamr, the son of Angantyr who defeated the Huns. It then t
2 CONC ells that Halfdan had the son Ivar Vidfamne, who attacked Ingjald Ill-ruler, which led to Ingjald's suicide by burning down his own hall at Ræning together with all his retinue. After this, Ivar Vidfamne conquered Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halfdan_the_Valiant"
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
