2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "A Guide to Irish Roots," William & Mary Durning (La Mesa, CA: Irish Family Names Society, 1995), p. II-112, gives this ancestry of Halfdan (backwards in time): Heiti, Gor, Snow ("The Old One"), Frosti, Karl, Fornjot of Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Halfdan and brother Gudrud reportedly killed each other
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan's ancestry on his father's and mother's side is elsewhere in this chart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan's father was Harald Valdarsson and his mother was Hildur (Hildis, Hervor) Heidreksdottir. His paternal
2 CONT
2 CONT grandparents were Valdar Hroarsson and Hildis Vandals.
2 CONT
2 CONT his maternal grandparents were Heidrek (Ulfhamr) Angantyrsson and Arnfleda (The Younger).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdan Snälle Haraldsson, King of Roeskilde1,2,3
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdan Snälle Haraldsson, King of Roeskilde||p278.htm#i9379|Haraldr Valdarsson, King of Roeskilde||p78.htm#i10098||||Valdar H., King of Roeskilde||p78.htm#i10099|Hildis|b. b 530\nd. c 572|p293.htm#i10100|||||||
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Haraldr Valdarsson, King of Roeskilde4
2 CONT
2 CONT Hálfdan Snälle Haraldsson, King of Roeskilde died. Killed by his brother, Gudrod, who did it at the urging of his wife, Aasa, daughter of Ingjald "the Evil-Advisor."5 He was born at Jutland, Denmark. He was the son of Haraldr Vald
2 CONC arsson, King of Roeskilde.4 Hálfdan Snälle Haraldsson, King of Roeskilde married Maolda (?) before 612. Family
2 CONT
