1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''This Ivar is son of Halvdan 'Gamle' Sveidasson. He is NOT the son of Harald Eivindsson or Halvdan Eysteinsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This Ivar is the same as:
2 CONT * '''https://www.geni.com/people/Ivar-Halfdansson-Opplendingejarl/6000000002889226416
2 CONT * '''https://www.geni.com/people/Ivar-Halfdansson-Opplendingejarl/6000000026962286560
2 CONT * '''https://www.geni.com/people/Ivar-Opplendingejarl/6000000137515951821
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZGL-BFY
2 CONT ==brief biography==
2 CONT * Father: Halvdan 'Gamle' Sveidasson, born 0758, died 0834 (according to Orkney Saga)
2 CONT * Mother: Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Jarl of Oppland ("the Uplands"), Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT ==family==
2 CONT * Spouse: Unknown
2 CONT * Documented child: Eystein Ivarsson "Glumra", father of Ragnvald Eysteinsson Mørejarl
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT Quoting from
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivar_Halfdan#Halfdan_the_Old_of_G.C3.B3r.27s_lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT Halfdan the Old of Gór's lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT The Orkneying saga does not speak at all of Nór's descendants, but introduces instead a figure named Halfdan the Old as the son of Sveidi (Sveiði) the Sea-king, who is called Svadi (Svaði) in the Ættartolur. Sveidi/Svadi in both t
2 CONC exts was son of Heiti, son of Gór who was Nór's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT This second Halfdan the Old is father of Jarl Ívar of the Uplands who married a daughter of a certain Eistein and so became father of Eystein the Clatterer (Eysteinn Glumra) who was father of Jarl Rögnvald of Møre and of Rögnvald'
2 CONC s brother Sigurd, and also of two daughters: Svanhild who was one of King Harald Fairhair's wives and another daughter named Malahule. According to various sources, Jarl Rögnvald had three illegitimate sons: Hallad (Hallaðr), Hrol
2 CONC laug (Hrollaugr), and Torf-Einarr. Later, by his wife Ragnhild (Ragnhildr) daughter of Hrólf Nose (Hrólf Nefja), Rögnvald was father of three legitimate sons: Hrólf, Ívar, and Thórir (Þórir) the Silent. Hrólf, also called Ganger-H
2 CONC rólf (Gǫngu-Hrólfr 'Hrólf the walker'), Icelandic/Norwegian historians identify him as the Rollo who conquered Neustria which was then renamed as Normandy, but that identification seems very doubtful. Thórir inherited his father's
2 CONC  lands. The first four Jarls of Orkney were successively Rögnvald's brother Sigurd, Sigurd's son Guthorm (Guttormr), Rögnvald's son Hallad, and Rögnvald's son Turf-Einar. From Turf-Einar the later Jarls descended. Hrollaug and his
2 CONC  wife and sons settled in Iceland.
