2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Chassé d'Uppland, il crée son royaume de Vestfold en Norvège
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olaf Tree Feller (Old Norse: Óláfr trételgja, Swedish: Olof Trätälja, Norwegian: Olav Tretelgja, all meaning Olaf Woodwhittler) was the son of the Swedish king Ingjald Ill-ruler of the House of Yngling according to Ynglingatal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heimskringla
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother was Gauthild, a princess of West Götaland, whose maternal grandfather was Olof the Sharp-sighted, the king of Nerike.
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother sent him to his foster-father Bove in West Götaland, where he grew up with his foster-brother Saxe who was surnamed Flette.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Olof heard of his father's death, he assembled the men who were willing to follow him and went to his kinsmen in Nerike, because after his father's atrocities, the Swedes had grown hostile towards the Ynglings.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Swedes learnt that Olof and his kin had sought refuge in Nerike, they were attacked and had to head west through deep and mountainous forests (Kilsbergen) to Lake Vänern and the estuary of Klarälven (where Karlstad is pre
2 CONC sently situated). Here, they settled and cleared land. Soon they had created a whole province called Värmland, where they could make good living.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the Swedes learnt that Olof was clearing land, they were amused and called him the Tree-feller. Olof married a woman named Solveig who was a daughter of Halfdan Guldtand of Soleyar. Olof and Solveigh had two sons, Ingjald Olo
2 CONC fsson and Halfdan Hvitbeinn, who were brought up in Soleyar in the house of his mother's uncle Sölve.
2 CONT
2 CONT Because of king Ivar Vidfamne and his harsh rule many Swedes emigrated to Värmland, and they became so numerous that the province could not sustain them. The land was afflicted by famine of which the Swedes accused the king. It wa
2 CONC s an old tradition in Sweden of holding the king responsible for the wealth of the land (see Domalde). The Swedes accused Olof of neglecting his sacrifices to the gods and believed that this was the cause of the famine.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Swedish settlers thus rebelled against Olof, surrounded his house on the shores of lake Vänern and burnt him inside it. Thus he was sacrificed to Odin, like his ancestor Domalde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ynglingatal and Historia Norwegiae
2 CONT
2 CONT However, Historia Norwegiae says that Olof succeeded his father and ruled as the king of Sweden in peace until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ejus filius Olavus cognomento tretelgia diu et pacifice functus regno plenus dierum obiit in Swethia.[1] 	
2 CONT
2 CONT His son, Olav, known as Tretelgje, accomplished a long and peaceful reign, and died in Sweden, replete in years.[2] 	
2 CONT
2 CONT The lines of Ynglingatal appear to say that he was a Swedish prince (svía jöfri), and that he was burnt inside his hall and disappeared from Gamla Uppsala.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ok við vág,
2 CONT     viðar (telgju)
2 CONT     hræ Ólafs
2 CONT     hofgyldir svalg,
2 CONT     ok glóðfjálgr
2 CONT     gervar leysti
2 CONT     sonr Fornjóts
2 CONT     af Svía jöfri.
2 CONT     Sá áttkonr
2 CONT     frá Uppsölum
2 CONT     Lofða kyns
2 CONT     fyrir löngu hvarf.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Archaelogy
2 CONT
2 CONT Along the lower parts of the river Byälven in Värmland, there are three large barrows, which legend attributes to Olof Trätälja. Moreover, there are many hillforts near this river and the northern shore of Lake Vänern testifying t
2 CONC o a violent period. Archaeological excavations from one of the hillforts, Villkorsberget, show that it was burnt in a period corresponding to Olof (510–680).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olof Trätälja, var en kung av Ynglingaätten. Han omtalas i Snorre Sturlassons Ynglingasaga i Heimskringla och då som son till Ingjald Illråde. Han uppfostrades i Västergötland hos sin fosterfar. Han bosätter sig i Värmland där han
2 CONC  bryter mark och skapar sig ett välde. Efter en hungersnöd offras han till Oden och bränns inne i sitt hus. En annan version är att han for till Norge. Han ska ha varit gift med Solveig.
2 CONT
2 CONT Säffle har Olof Trätälja i sitt vapen och en gravhög kallas Olof Trätäljas hög.
2 CONT
2 CONT Varken Olof Trätälja eller Ynglingaätten är historiskt säkerställda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olof trätälja
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Ur Snorre Sturlasons Heims-Kringla, Ynglingasagan, kapitel 45, citeras följande (översättning av Emanuel S Ekman 1765): "Nu som Olof, Konung Ingjalds
2 CONC  Son, fick höra sin Faders frånfälle, drog han af med det folk, som honom följa wille; ty at all den gemene man gorde endräkteliga upror, til at förderfwa hela Kung Ingjalds släckt och alla hans wänner. Olof reste först up til Ner
2 CONC ike, men så snart som de swenske fingo det weta, fick han icke längre där wara. Sedan drog han wäster öfwer marken, til den ån, som rinner nordan ifrån uti Wänern, och kallas elfwen (fellur i vöni oc Elfur heitir). Ther dwaldes th
2 CONC e, och begynte at rödja marken, hugga skogen, bränna och bygga, hwaraf innom en liten tid blefwo stora härader, som kallades Wärmeland, som blef et godt och fruktsamt landskap. Men som det spordes til Swrie om bemälte Olof, at han
2 CONC  uthögg skogen och rögde markena, tå kallade de honom Trätelja, och tyckte hans förehafwande wara mycket förakteligt."
2 CONT
