2 CONT
2 CONT After a season of bad harvests, the woodcutting king [Olof Ingjaldsson] was sacrificed to Odin so that his people might have good crops. He was succeeded by his son Halfdan Whiteleg, who is said to have extended his rule over much
2 CONC  of southern Norway. Halfdan died at a ripe old age, was duly placed in a burial mound, and his deeds were sun by the bards.
