1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALFHILD 'ALOF' GANDALFSSDOTTIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT King Gandalf Alfgeirsson was the father of Alfhild Gandalfsdottir, who was the mother of 
2 CONT Ragnar 'Lodbrok' Sigurdsson who was the father of Alof Ragnarsdottir who was the mother of 
2 CONT Bjorn Hunda-Steinarson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''NOTE: "Sagas" are NOT fairytales, the term is related to the Swedish word "utsaga", meaning 'statement' ''outsayings'' or ''tellings'' in English. While the average Medieval People were not literate, the oral tradition was in pr
2 CONC actice over all with tellings by elders and traders around a bonfire with gathered families. People in the Sagas are generally believed to have genuinely existed; in some cases the events attributed to them, especially those of an
2 CONC  extravagant nature, are considered by skeptical historians to be embellished or invented until further sources can be found to confirm them, and they are therefore dubbed 'legendary'. The 'legendary' moniker does not imply their 
2 CONC historic non-existence; you can believe they existed, just take any information about them with a healthy (not cynical) dose of suspicion.''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfhild was the wife of Sigurd Ring (a ''legendary'' king in Sweden and Denmark) and she was mother of the equally ''legendary'' Ragnar "Lodbrok" Sigurdsson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Up until recently, there was some confusion as to whether Ragnar's mother was Alfhild, or Alof. Alfhild has a clear parentage, while Alof's parentage is wholly confused. However, it has been historically determined that the confus
2 CONC ion arose because Alfhild and Alof are one and the same person, with "Alof" being a nickname or term of endearment for Alfhild; this explains why her son Ragnar named his daughter 'Alof', likely in his mother's honor.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources cited==
2 CONT -Abbrev: Stuart (1992) Title: Royalty for Commoners Author: Stuart, R. W. Publication: Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2nd. Ed. 1992 (firstEd. 1988). Page: pp. 175-176 (Line 240) 00
2 CONT -Google Gemini 3 AI
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT '''Alfhild 'Alof' Gandalfsdattir:'''  
2 CONT She was married to Sigurd Ring (the ''legendary'' king of Sweden), mother of Ragnar 'Lodbrok' Sigurdsson. Snorri Sturluson writes in the Ynglinga Saga, the first saga in the saga collection Heimskringla, that Alvheim (Alfheim) was
2 CONC  what they called the land between the Rauma River and Göta River at the time. His use of the expression ''they called it then'' suggests that the name was out of use in the 13th century when Snorri wrote. 
2 CONT Snorri tells of a king Alv (Alf), father of Alvhild (Alfhild) [grandmother of our Alfhild 'Alof' Gandofsdattir], who married Gudrød the Hunter King of Vestmar and brought with her half of Vingulmark as a dowry. Alv's (Alf's) son, 
2 CONC Alvgeir (Alfgeir), took possession of all of Vingulmark and placed his son, Gandalv (Gandalf), as king there. Since this Gandalv (Gandalf) was a contemporary elder of Harald Fairhair, and since the sons of Ragnar Lodbrok in some t
2 CONC raditions are said to have been contemporaries of Fairhair, it is possible that Alvhild (Alfhild), mother of Ragnar Lodbrok, was the daughter of this Gandalv (Gandalf).
2 CONT In other Norse sources, Gandalv (Gandalf) was called King Alvarin of Alvheim (Alfarin of Alfheim). What is recounted in Heimskringla is that after many indecisive battles between Gandalv (Gandalf) and Halvdan (Halfdan) the Black, 
2 CONC the two kings agreed to divide Vingulmark, Halvdan (Halfdan) regaining the part that his grandfather had received as a dowry with his first wife Alvhild (Alfhild). Two sons of Gandalv (Gandalf), Hysing and Helsing, later led an ar
2 CONC my against Halvdan (Halfdan), but fell in battle, and a third brother, Hake, fled back to Alvheim (Alfheim). After Halvdan’s (Halfdan’s) son Harald Fairhair succeeded his father as king of Vestfold, both Gandalv (Gandalf) and his 
2 CONC son Hake joined an alliance that attacked Harald. Hake fell, but Gandalv (Gandalf) escaped. There would come more wars between Gandalv (Gandalf) and Harald, and in the end Gandalv (Gandalf) fell in battle and Harald took over the 
2 CONC entire country up to the Raumelv. Alvheim was now conquered by King Erik Anundsson of Uppsala, but Harald soon gained control over the area and Alvheim (Alfheim) was incorporated into Norway.
2 CONT https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alvheim 
2 CONT
2 CONT Norwegian:
2 CONT Alfhild 'Alof' Gangalfdattir:  Hun var gift med til Sigurd Ring (legendariske kongen i Sweden), mor av Ragnar "Lodbrok" Sigurdsson.  Snorre Sturlason skriver i Ynglingesaga, den første sagaen i sagasamlingen Heimskringla: at Alvhe
2 CONC im (Alfheim) kalte de den gang landet mellom Raumelv og Göta älv. Bruken av uttrykket «kalte de dengang» vil tilsi at navnet var ute av bruk på 1200-tallet, da Snorre skrev. Snorre forteller om en kong Alv (Alf), far til Alvhild (
2 CONC Alfhild) som giftet seg med Gudrød Veidekonge av Vestmar, og brakte med seg halve Vingulmark som medgifte. Alvs (Alf's) sønn, Alvgeir (Alfgeir), la igjen under seg hele Vingulmark og plasserte sin sønn, Gandalv (Gandalf), som kong
2 CONC e der. Siden denne Gandalv (Gandalf) var en eldre samtidig av Harald Hårfagre og siden sønnene til Ragnar Lodbrok i noen tradisjoner skal ha vært samtidige med Håfagre, er det mulig at Alvhild (Alfhild), mor til Ragnar Lodbrok, va
2 CONC r datter av denne Gandalv (Gandalf).  
2 CONT I andre norrøne kilder ble Gandalv (Gandalf) kalt for kong Alvarin av Alvheim (Alfarin av Alfheim). Hva som blir fortalt i Heimskringla er at etter mange uavgjørende slag mellom Gandalv (Gandalf) og Halvdan (Halfdan) Svarte ble de
2 CONC  to kongene enige om å dele Vingulmarken, Halvdan (Halfdan) fikk tilbake den delen som han bestefar hadde fått som medgifte med sin første kone Alvhild (Alfhild).  To sønner av Gandalv (Gandalf), Hysing og Helsing førte senere en 
2 CONC hær mot Halvdan (Halfdan), men falt i slag, og en tredje bror, Hake flyktet tilbake til Alvheim (Alfheim). Etter at Halvdans (Halfdans) sønn Harald Hårfagre etterfulgte sin far som konge av Vestfold var både Gandalv (Gandalf) og h
2 CONC ans sønn Hake med på en allianse som angrep Harald. Hake falt, men Gandalv (Gandalf) unnslapp. Det skulle komme flere kriger mellom Gandalv (Gandalf) og Harald, og til slutt falt Gandalv (Gandalf) i slag og Harald overtok hele lan
2 CONC det til Raumelv. Alvheim ble nå erobret av kong Erik Anundsson av Uppsala, men Harald vant snart kontroll over området og Alvheim (Alfheim) ble innlemmet i Norge.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alvheim 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Enligt Norska dokument avled Alfhild när Ragnar var pojke ca 10 år gammal omkr. 803. Han sändes då till sin mors släktingar i Ringerike i Norge för att fostras och växa upp. Där fick han god kännedom om segelleder och maktcentra. 
2 CONC Ragnar blev i tonåren av hövdingar och jarlar utsedd kung efter sin far Sigurd 'Ring' Randversson. Som nybliven Kung mötte Ragnar den lika gamla Gerda Hålgadottir, Ladgerda, från Gaulardal nära Lade dagens Trondheim. De fick tills
2 CONC ammans tre dokumenterade barn . En son Fridleif och två ej namngivna döttrar.
