1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Critisk Historie af Danmark, udi den hedenske Tid, fra Odin ... https://books.google.com › books - Translate this page 1781 Hans Moder Hildur VIII, 144. Alf, han somastede Ivars Dotter, anseet för valdar, hvilken M
2 CONC eeningsrafaldes VIII, 257. . . . -''' Alfarin, Gandalfs Son'''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfarin (Alfarin Gandolfsson) or Álf was a leader Viking king of Alvheim (today Bohuslän , Sweden ). Son of King Gandalf Alfgeirsson . His daughter married King Alfhild Norwegian , Gudrød the Hunter of the kingdom of Romerike and 
2 CONC Vestfold , a marriage which extended its influence to half the kingdom of Vingulmark , territory Gudrød received as dowry . Therefore Álf is grandfather of King Olaf Geirstad-Alf who was brother of Halfdan the Black .
2 CONT
2 CONT King Álf appears in several Nordic sagas as Ynglinga saga , Hálfdanar svarta saga and saga of Haralds saga ins hárfagra , the three works are part of the compendium of XIII century Heimskringla the skald Icelandic Snorri Sturluson
2 CONC  .
2 CONT
2 CONT References [ edit ]↑ Norsk Adel, Heber, Gustav, (Oslo: Trykt I Centraltrykkeriet, 1949), TNB book Hlex 929.7, p.. 73-74. References [ edit ]Sturluson, Snorri Heimskringla. History of the Kings of Norway, trans. Lee M. Hollander. R
2 CONC eprinted University of Texas Press , Austin, 1992. ISBN 0-292-73061-6
