1 NOTE {geni:about_me} EUSTACHE [IV] "Campulus" du Rœulx, son of EUSTACHE [III] Seigneur du Rœulx & his wife Marie de Tournai ([1190/1205]-after Mar 1274).  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis names “filium unum [...E
2 CONC ustachius] et filiam unam” as the children of “Eustachius dictus Kanivet” and his wife “filiam Balduini de Mortania castellani Tornacensis”[339].  Seigneur du Rœulx.  “Eustache seigneur de Rœulx” confirmed the foundation of a chap
2 CONC el at Sart by “Gilles chevalier de Sart” by charter dated 1234[340].  Under a codicil dated Aug 1242, “Arnould d’Audenarde” appointed as his executors “Eustache de Rœux chevalier son cousin, Bauduin de Mervenghien, Alix sa femme, 
2 CONC Robert de Saint-Jacques et Eustache de Gand, frère cordeliers”[341].  The family relationship between Eustache [IV] and Arnoud [IV] Heer van Oudenarde was that Richilde de Tournai, mother of Arnoud [IV], was the paternal aunt of E
2 CONC ustache [IV]’s mother --- de Tournai.  It has not proved possible to assess with any certainty the date of death of Eustache [IV].  His son was named in sources as “seigneur de Trazegnies”, without reference to “seigneur du Rœulx”
2 CONC , until Mar 1274.  It is a reasonable assumption therefore that his father Eustache [IV] was still alive at that date and continued to hold the seigneurie du Rœulx. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m MARIE de Trith, daughter and heiress of GILLES de Trith {Trith St Léger, Nord} & his wife ---.  The late 13th century genealogy by Balduinus de Avennis records that “Eustachius”, son of “Eustachius dictus Kanivet” and his wife “
2 CONC filiam Balduini de Mortania castellani Tornacensis”, married “filiam domini Ægidii de Tryt, sororem domini Theodorici de Bevre ex parte matris”[342].  It is difficult to identify with certainty the relevant “van Beveren” (see the 
2 CONC document FLANDERS NOBILITY) to whom the wife of Gilles de Trith was married as her first/second husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eustache [IV] & his wife had [eight] children: 
