1 NAME Siger IV /van Gent/
2 GIVN Siger IV
2 SURN van Gent
2 _MARNM van Gent
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Medlands: http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Second child of Seger III  Entry in Medlands:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         SIGER .  "Sigerus castellanus Gandensis" donated property to Affleghem, for the anniversaries of "meum et matris mæ Petronillæ et uxoris meæ Beatricis", with the consent of “Hugo primogenitus filius meus, Sigerus filius
2 CONC  meus”, by charter dated 1218[709]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Entry in Medlands of family:
2 CONT
2 CONT SIGER [III] van Gent, son of SIGER [II] Châtelain de Gand & his wife Petronille de Courtrai (-1227 or after).  "Sigerus castellanus de Gandavo" donated property to Los abbey near Lille, in the presence of "uxore nostra Petronilla 
2 CONC et filiis nostris...Sigero et Daniele", for the soul of “filii nostri Arnulfi”, by charter dated 1190, witnessed by “...Egidii castellani...”[690].  “Willelmus Attrebatensis advocatus Bethuniæ et Thenremundiæ dominus et Mathildis 
2 CONC uxor mea” donated property to Clermarest abbey, for the souls of “Roberti advocati et Adelidis matris meæ, Roberti fratris mei et Walteri de Thenremunda”, by undated charter witnessed by “Anselmus frater meus...Sigerus castellanus
2 CONC  de Gant, Sigerus et Daniel filii eius...”[691].  “Sigerus castellanus Gandensis et uxor mea Petronilla” donated property to Afflighem abbey, with the consent of "Sigero filio nostro et reliquis filiis nostris", by charter dated 1
2 CONC 198[692].  Châtelain de Gand.  "Sigerus castellanus Gandensis" donated property to Affleghem, for the anniversaries of "meum et matris mæ Petronillæ et uxoris meæ Beatricis", with the consent of “Hugo primogenitus filius meus, Sig
2 CONC erus filius meus”, by charter dated 1218[693].  1227.  m BEATRIX de Houdain, daughter of HUGUES de Houdain & his wife ---.  "Sigerus castellanus Gandensis" donated property to Affleghem, for the anniversaries of "meum et matris mæ
2 CONC  Petronillæ et uxoris meæ Beatricis", with the consent of “Hugo primogenitus filius meus, Sigerus filius meus”, by charter dated 1218[694].  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.
2 CONC   Du Chesne names “Beatrix Dame de Houdain mariée avec Siger II Chastellain de Gand” as the child of “Hugues Seigneur de Houdain” but he does not cite the corresponding primary source[695].  Siger [III] & his wife had children:  1
2 CONC .         HUGO [II] (-[Sep/26 Nov] 1232).  "Sigerus castellanus Gandensis" donated property to Affleghem, for the anniversaries of "meum et matris mæ Petronillæ et uxoris meæ Beatricis", with the consent of “Hugo primogenitus fili
2 CONC us meus, Sigerus filius meus”, by charter dated 1218[696].  Châtelain de Gand.  “Hugo Gandensis castellanus uxorque mea Oda filiusque meis Hugo primogenitus” granted privileges to the church of Sainte-Marie de Baserode by charter 
2 CONC dated 1228[697].  "Hugo castellanus Gandensis" confirmed the donation to the abbey of Byloka made by "Giselbertus de Sottenghem miles" with the consent of "Mathildis uxoris suæ" by charter dated May 1230[698].  "Hugo castellanus G
2 CONC andensis dominus de Hosdain" confirmed the donation to the abbey of Gent St Marie made by "Bernardus de Vennebrechies" by charter dated 1232[699].  m EUDETTE [Oda] de Champlitte, daughter of EUDES de Champlitte Vicomte de Dijon & 
2 CONC his first wife [--- de Mont-Saint-Jean] (-after 1228).  The contract of divorce between "Erardus dominus Chascegnay" and "Emeline uxoris mee", with the consent of "Elisabeth domine Castri Villani et Simonis filii sui", is dated Se
2 CONC p 1224, names "Oda dicta Emeline primogenita" and provides for the dowry of "M. filiam meam" on her marriage to "comiti Gigeti"[700].  Dame de Champlitte until 1228.  “Guillaume de Vergy frere d´Alix de Vergy duchesse de Bourgongn
2 CONC e” bought “la ville de Champlite” from “Hugues Chastellain de Gand et de Oede sa femme” by charter dated 1228[701].  “Hugo Gandensis castellanus uxorque mea Oda filiusque meis Hugo primogenitus” granted privileges to the church of
2 CONC  Sainte-Marie de Baserode by charter dated 1228[702].  Hugo & his wife had two children:  a)         HUGO [III] (-[Dec 1264/Apr 1265]).  “Hugo Gandensis castellanus uxorque mea Oda filiusque meis Hugo primogenitus” granted privile
2 CONC ges to the church of Sainte-Marie de Baserode by charter dated 1228[703].  Châtelain de Gand.  -        see below.  b)         VILAIN (-before 1262).  “Hugo castellanus Gandensis et dominus Hosdino” confirmed the donation of prope
2 CONC rty held from "domino Villano milite fratre nostro" to Baudeloo abbey, granting powers to "dominæ Avezoetæ relictæ prædicti domini Villani et Alexandro primogenito eius", by charter dated 1262[704].  m AVEZOTA, daughter of --- (-[
2 CONC 1262/Aug 1279]).  “Hugo castellanus Gandensis et dominus Hosdino” confirmed the donation of property held from "domino Villano milite fratre nostro" to Baudeloo abbey, granting powers to "dominæ Avezoetæ relictæ prædicti domini Vi
2 CONC llani et Alexandro primogenito eius", by charter dated 1262[705].  Villan & his wife had one child:  i)          ALEXANDER (-after Aug 1279).  “Hugo castellanus Gandensis et dominus Hosdino” confirmed the donation of property held
2 CONC  from "domino Villano milite fratre nostro" to Baudeloo abbey, granting powers to "dominæ Avezoetæ relictæ prædicti domini Villani et Alexandro primogenito eius", by charter dated 1262[706].  “Alexander dictus Villain miles et dom
2 CONC inus de Steene et uxor mea” confirmed the donation of property to Baudeloo abbey made by "bonæ memoriæ dominam Avezoetam matrem meam" by charter dated Aug 1279[707].  -         SEIGNEURS VILAIN de GAND, COMTES d´ISENGHIEN[708].  2
2 CONC .         SIGER .  "Sigerus castellanus Gandensis" donated property to Affleghem, for the anniversaries of "meum et matris mæ Petronillæ et uxoris meæ Beatricis", with the consent of “Hugo primogenitus filius meus, Sigerus filius 
2 CONC meus”, by charter dated 1218[709].  3.         GERARD (-after Feb 1264).  "Gerardus de Gandavo miles, avunculus castellani Gandensis, et Elizabeth uxor mea" donated property to Biloka abbey by charter dated Sep 1254, and "Hugo cas
2 CONC tellanus Gandensis et dominus de Hosdain" confirmed the donation made by "avunculus noster dominus Gerardus de Gandavo miles, uxor sua domina Elizabet" by charter dated Jan 1254 (O.S.)[710].  Marguerite Ctss of Flanders confirmed 
2 CONC the donation to the churches of Tournai, Gent and Flines made by "Gerardus de Gand miles et Elisabeth eius uxor" by charter dated Aug 1261[711].  "Gerardus dictus Diabolus de Gandavo miles et Elisabeth eius uxor" confirmed the pre
2 CONC vious donations by charter dated Feb 1264[712].  m ELISABETH, daughter of --- (-after Feb 1264).  "Gerardus de Gandavo miles, avunculus castellani Gandensis, et Elizabeth uxor mea" donated property to Biloka abbey by charter dated
2 CONC  Sep 1254, and "Hugo castellanus Gandensis et dominus de Hosdain" confirmed the donation made by "avunculus noster dominus Gerardus de Gandavo miles, uxor sua domina Elizabet" by charter dated Jan 1254 (O.S.)[713].  Marguerite Cts
2 CONC s of Flanders confirmed the donation to the churches of Tournai, Gent and Flines made by "Gerardus de Gand miles et Elisabeth eius uxor" by charter dated Aug 1261[714].  "Gerardus dictus Diabolus de Gandavo miles et Elisabeth eius
2 CONC  uxor" confirmed the previous donations by charter dated Feb 1264[715]. 
2 CONT
