1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=nor&person=Gudr%F8d%20konge%20i%20Sk%E5ne&list=&vis=
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød konge i Skåne (Guðröður konung á Skáni)
2 CONT
2 CONT In English: Gudrod king of Scania
2 CONT
2 CONT Bror til Halvdan
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT uðröðr (Godred[1]) was a legendary 7th century Scanian king who according to the Ynglinga saga was the brother of Halfdan the Valiant, Ivar Vidfamne's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga tells that Guðröðr married Åsa, the daughter of the Swedish king Ingjald Ill-ruler. She backtalked Halfdan so that Guðröðr killed him, and having done so, she arranged the death of Guðröðr himself. Then she fled 
2 CONC back to her father in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guðröðr was succeeded by his nephew Ivar Vidfamne who avenged his father and uncle, and conquered Sweden and other countries.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gu%C3%B0r%C3%B6%C3%B0r_of_Scania
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingjald had two children, a son Olof Trätälja and a daughter Åsa. His daughter had inherited her father's psychopathic disposition. She married king Guðröðr of Skåne. Before she murdered her husband she managed to make him kill hi
2 CONC s own brother Halfdan the Valiant, the father of the great Ivar Vidfamne.
2 CONT
2 CONT In order to avenge his father, Ivar Vidfamne gathered a vast host and departed for Sweden, where he found Ingjald at Ræning. When Ingjald and his daughter realized that it was futile to resist, they set the hall on fire and succum
2 CONC bed in the flames.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guðröðr (Godred) was a legendary 7th century Scanian king who according to the Ynglinga saga was the brother of Halfdan the Valiant, Ivar Vidfamne's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga tells that Guðröðr married Åsa, the daughter of the Swedish king Ingjald Ill-ruler. She backtalked Halfdan so that Guðröðr killed him, and having done so, she arranged the death of Guðröðr himself. Then she fled 
2 CONC back to her father in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guðröðr was succeeded by his nephew Ivar Vidfamne who avenged his father and uncle, and conquered Sweden and other countries
2 CONT
