1 NOTE Gudrod's brother = Halfdan, was the father of Ivar Vidfadme
1 NOTE He was King in Skåne.
1 NOTE He was King in Skåne.
1 NOTE Guðröðr (Godred[1]) was a legendary 7th century Scanian king who according to the Ynglinga saga was the brother of Halfdan the Valiant, Ivar Vidfamne's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga tells that Guðröðr married Åsa, the daughter of the Swedish king Ingjald Ill-ruler. She backtalked Halfdan so that Guðröðr killed him, and having done so, she arranged the death of Guðröðr himself. Then she f
2 CONC led back to her father in Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guðröðr was succeeded by his nephew Ivar Vidfamne who avenged his father and uncle, and conquered Sweden and other countries.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Guðröðr's family
2 CONT Hervarar saga and Hversu Noregr byggdist give more information about his brother Halfdan the Valiant and his son Ivar Vidfamne, and by implication about Guðröðr himself.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hversu Noregr byggdist gives Halfdan the Valiant's father as Harald the Old, his grandfather as Valdar and his great-grandfather as Hróarr (i.e. the Hroðgar of Beowulf).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hervarar saga provides the information that Halfdan's mother was Hild, the daughter of the Gothic king Heiðrekr Ulfhamr, the son of Angantyr who defeated the Huns.
