1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidrek https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heidrek
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek or Heiðrekr was one of the main characters in the cycle about the magic sword Tyrfing.
2 CONT
2 CONT He appears in the Hervarar saga, and probably also in Widsith, line 115, as Heathoric together with his sons Angantyr (Incgentheow) and Hlöð (Hlith), and Hlöð's mother Sifka (Sifeca).
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek was the son of king Höfund and his wife Hervor, a shieldmaiden. Like his mother in her youth, he was ill-natured and violent. In order to mend this, he was raised by the wise Geatish king Gizur, but this did not improve hi
2 CONC s disposition. One day, when his parents had a banquet, Heidrek arrived uninvited and late at night, he started a quarrel which ended in manslaughter. His father, king Höfund, banished Heidrek from his kingdom, although Hervor did
2 CONC  her utmost to soften Höfunds feelings against his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hervor secretely gave her son the sword Tyrfing as she bid him farewell, and his brother Angantyr kept him company for a while. When they had walked for some time, Heidrek wanted to have a look at the sword. Since he had unsheathe
2 CONC d it, the curse the Dwarves had put on the sword made him kill his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a while, Heidrek met a patroll moving a prisoner who was to be executed as he had murdered his master. He remembered his father's advice and resolved to buy the criminal. Then he continued his journey and met a patroll movin
2 CONC g a scoundrel who had killed his comrade. Likewise, Heidrek bought the man's life in order to disobey his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon, Heidrek arrived in Reidgotaland, entered the Gothic king Harald's service and disposed him of two rebellious jarls. This rendered him half the Gothic kingdom and the king's daughter, Helga. Heidrek and Helga had a son who wa
2 CONC s named Angantyr after Heidrek's brother and grandfather. During the same time old king Harald had a son who was named Halfdan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, Reidgotaland was struck with bad crops and starvation. The Godis (pagan priests) determined that they had to sacrifice the most noble young man of the kingdom to Odin in order to return the good crops. Immediately, 
2 CONC people started to quarrel about which one of the princes was the most noble, and so they asked king Höfund of Glæsisvellir. King Höfund decided that it was Angantyr (his own grandson) who was the most noble prince. Höfund also tol
2 CONC d Heidrek to ask king Harald that in recompense for sacrificing his own son, he was to receive half the Gothic army as his own. King Harald accepted.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, when Höfund called for a Ting (council) in order to sacrifice Angantyr, Heidrek objected and said that Odin would be happy if he instead of Angantyr, received king Harald and his son Halfdan. Then, Heidrek made a coup d'é
2 CONC tat with his half of the Gothic army, using Tyrfing to kill king Harald and his son. When his wife Helga learnt of the news, she committed suicide by hanging herself.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek used his army to subjugate the Gothic kingdom and ruled with brutal force. He defeated Humle, the king of the Huns, and captured his daughter Sifka whom he raped. When she was pregnant, she was sent back to her father's ki
2 CONC ngdom where she bore a son who was named Hlöd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek married Olof, the daughter of Åke the King of the Saxons. She often asked to go home and visit her family, and since Heidrek remembered his father's advice, he always gladly consented. This would turn out to be an unwise s
2 CONC trategy, because one day he made the journey to Saxony in order to see his wife among her family. He found her in the arms of a blond thrall and immediately divorced her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Instead, he married a girl from Finland who was named Sifka, like the Hunnic princess. One day, they were visiting king Rollaug of Gardariki. In order to oppose a fourth word of advice given by his father, he told Sifka a secret a
2 CONC nd asked her to swear an oath never to tell anyone. The secret was that he had accidentally killed King Rollaug's son, in a hunting accident.
2 CONT
2 CONT Naturally, Sifka immediately ran to King Rollaug and told him about the news, which caused King Rollaug to capture Heidrek and to kill all of his retinue. The two men who bound him were no others but the two culprits he had saved 
2 CONC from the gallows.
2 CONT
2 CONT When king Rollaug was about to burn Heidrek alive, someone broke the news that the prince was still alive and that Heidrek was innocent. Rollaug apologized and in recompense for Heidrek's losses he gave him his own daughter, Herge
2 CONC rd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heidrek and Hergerd had a daughter who was named Hervor, the shieldmaiden, after her grandmother who had just died. This was the beginning of a time of pieceful reign from Heidrek's side.
2 CONT
2 CONT During a voyage, Heidrek camped at the Carpathians (Harvaða fjöllum, cf. Grimm's law). He was accompanied by eight mounted thralls, and when Heidrek slept at night, the thralls broke into his tent and took Tyrfing and slew Heidrek
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT This was the last one of Tyrfing's three evil deeds. Heidrek's son Angantyr caught the thralls, killed them and reclaimed the magic sword, but the curse had ceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrfing
