1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bio Summary: Margaretha van Halewijn
2 CONT Role: High-ranking noblewoman and "Diplomatic Bridge" to the urban and military nobility.
2 CONT Active Period: mid-to-late 13th Century (fl. 1250–1280).
2 CONT In Warlop’s Chapter 220, Margaretha (daughter of Wauthier IV and Marguerite de Oudenaarde) is a textbook example of how a family at the peak of its power used its daughters to "lock in" alliances across different regions of Flande
2 CONC rs. Warlop identifies her two marriages as high-status unions that connected the Halluins to the Ghent patriciate and the Lille border lords.
2 CONT '''1. Documented Evidence (The Warlop Rigor)'''
2 CONT Warlop verifies Margaretha through her involvement in the complex dower (widowhood) rights associated with her two powerful husbands:
2 CONT • The Vaernewyck Succession: Warlop cites records from the Castellany of Ghent where Margaretha, as the widow of Simon III van Vaernewyck, manages her maritagium (dowry) and the inheritance of her Vaernewyck children.
2 CONT • The de Croix Marriage: Warlop identifies her second marriage to Jean III de Croix through the Cartulary of the Count of Flanders. In 1272, Jean de Croix is documented as having business involving his wife "Margareta de Halewijn,
2 CONC " specifically concerning lands near the border of the Lille and Courtrai districts.
2 CONT '''2. The Two Marriages'''
2 CONT First Marriage: Simon III van Vaernewyck
2 CONT • Status: He was the Lord of Vaernewyck and a leading figure in the nobility surrounding the city of Ghent.
2 CONT • Strategic Value: This marriage linked the Halluins (who were Lys valley/Ypres based) to the power centers of East Flanders. The Vaernewycks were heerlijke (lordly) families with deep roots in the comtal administration of Ghent.
2 CONT Second Marriage: Jean III de Croix
2 CONT • Status: Lord of Mandre, Croix, and Flers.
2 CONT • Strategic Value: After Simon's death, Margaretha married into the House of Croix, one of the most prominent families of the Lille region. This marriage solidified the Halluin family's "southern strategy," ensuring they had kin i
2 CONC n every major fortress along the border with France.
2 CONT '''3. Children (Identified by Warlop via Inheritance)'''
2 CONT Warlop focuses on her children from the first marriage, as they became the heirs to the Vaernewyck estates:
2 CONT 1. Simon IV van Vaernewyck: The successor to his father; Warlop notes he maintained a close relationship with his Halluin uncles.
2 CONT 2. Eustache van Vaernewyck: Mentioned in property deeds alongside his mother Margaretha.
2 CONT 3. Jean de Croix (from the 2nd marriage): Warlop identifies a younger Jean de Croix who appears in 14th-century records, carrying forward the combined prestige of his parents.
2 CONT Database Entry Note
2 CONT Insert table
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The "Rigor" Check'''
2 CONT A common mistake in non-Warlop genealogies is to confuse this Margaretha with her niece (also named Margaretha). Warlop’s "Tenure Tracking" ensures we have the right one: this Margaretha is the daughter of Wauthier IV because her 
2 CONC dowry lands are specifically identified as being part of the Oudenaarde/Halluin inheritance she received from her parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <span style="color:red;font-weight:bold"> This Biographical summary is drafted with AI assistance, cross-referenced with House of Halluin lineage records, Ernest Warlop, Hist. E. De Vlaamse Adel Voor 1300, pertinent documents of e
2 CONC vidence, etc. (The Summary is intended for leads only, please check your sources.)</span>
2 CONT …..
2 CONT _________________________________________
2 CONT Below from more contemporary generation sources:
2 CONT Marguerite d'HALLUIN
2 CONT Margaretha van HALEWIJN
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1240 Julian (between January 8, 1240 and January 7, 1241) - Halluin, Noorderdepartement, Frankrijk
2 CONT Deceased about 1297 Julian (between January 8, 1297 and January 7, 1298) - Gent, Oost-Vlaanderen, België, aged about 57 years old
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT Roger d'HALLUIN, Heer van Halewijn ca 1212-ca 1256
2 CONT Johanna van GAVERE, Vrouwe van Gavere ca 1210-ca 1265
2 CONT
