1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hildis Princess of Vandals''' (-572) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Generations of genealogists have accepted Hildis as a daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Hilderic-King-of-the-Vandals-Alans/6000000009987656008 Hilderic, King of the Vandals] in Africa. She has been seen, therefore, as a gate
2 CONC way ancestor to the Roman Imperial dynasty of [http://www.geni.com/people/Theodosius-I-the-Great-Roman-Emperor/6000000006267755295 Theodosius]. However, this highly improbable descent is not supported by any contemporary reference
2 CONC . Moreover, the historical facts argue against the connection. Hilderic was deposed by his kinsman [http://www.geni.com/people/Gailamir-King-of-the-Vandals-530-533/6000000003645797803 Gelimer] in 530/31, then in 533 Gelimer himsel
2 CONC f was defeated by the Byzantine general [http://www.geni.com/people/Belisarius/6000000001353750518 Belisarius]. Hilderic's daughter(s) were captured, along with other members of the Vandal royal family. They then disappear from hi
2 CONC story. Because of their descent from [http://www.geni.com/people/Valentinian-III-Western-Roman-Emperor/6000000002119493371 Valentinian III], they represented a dynastic threat to the Emperor [http://www.geni.com/people/Justinian-I
2 CONC -Eastern-Roman-Emperor/6000000003645853347 Justinian]. They were probably placed in a convent. Finally, religious reasons would have presented a barrier to the marriage of a Vandal princess to a Danish king. Even if Justinian had 
2 CONC allowed Hilderic's daughters to marry, the fact that they were Christians would have mandated marriage to Christian princes in the Byzantine sphere of influence. They would not have been married to pagans ruling kingdoms distant f
2 CONC rom the Empire. Justin Swanström (2010).
2 CONT
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Theorized to be Hilderic, king of Vandals. Source missing.
2 CONT * Husband: Valdar HROARSSON
2 CONT **Son: Harald VALDARSSON b: 568 in Jutland, Denmark
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT *Abbrev: Stuart (1992)
2 CONT *Title: Royalty for Commoners
2 CONT *Author: Stuart, R. W.
2 CONT *Publication: Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2nd. Ed. 1992 (firstEd. 1988).
2 CONT *Page: pp. 175-176 (Line 240) 
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT REF RC. Possibly daughter of Hilderic, King of Vandals. If so the royal Vandals line goes back to Genseric, who conquered much of Africa about 425-455.
2 CONT
2 CONT *d. c. 572
2 CONT *Married Valdar Hroarsson (547-)
2 CONT *Children: [listed under entry for Valdar Hroarsson]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. "Royalty for Commoners",  Roderick W. Stuart, 1992, 2nd edition.
2 CONT *This book lists all of the known ancestors of John of Gaunt, which amounts to most of the Medieval royalty of Europe. Also see the following article: "A Mediaeval Miscellany: Commentaries on Roderick W. Stuart's Royalty for Commo
2 CONC ners," The American Genealogist 69 (April 1994)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hilda Hildericsdotter [Parents] 1 was born 2 about 530 in Denmark. She married 3 Frode VII Harald King of Danes about 546 in Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other marriages:
2 CONT *Harold Valdarsson
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT *M 	i 	Halfdan III King of Danes
2 CONT
