2 CONT ID: I69381
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Hildis of the VANDALS
2 CONT *Suffix: Vandal Princess
2 CONT *Title: Vandal Princess
2 CONT *Sex: F
2 CONT *Birth: Abt 515
2 CONT *Death: Abt 572
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT *Sources: RC 240; Kraentzler 1666, 1793.
2 CONT *RC: Hildis, Vandal princess, died about 572.
2 CONT *K-1666 calls her Hildis and married to Harold Valdarsson. RC says this man was her son. K-1793 calls her Hilda, married to Frode VII. Both these lines have her as the daughter of Hilderic of the Vandals. Will stick with RC. Also 
2 CONC Kraentzler's birthdate, 572, is RC's death date.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Some authorities give, as her father, Hilderic, King of Vandals, thus opening up the possiblity of a royal Vandals line going back to Genseric, a Vandal who conquered much of Africa about 425-455 AD. This lineage may be soun
2 CONC d but needs more work. Hilderic's RIN is 9302. Since this line, going back, was from Simpson Gedcom (looks like it from Kraentzler), will include it--but with a caveat. Incidentally, this Simpson/Kraentzler material had Hildis mar
2 CONC ried to wrong man, two generations up and gave her a c515 birth date. Also, Simpson has the line going clear back to Adam, which is mighty, mighty, mighty iffy. And add mighty many more times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 12 JUL 2000 at 21:33:25
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Her ancestry is found elsewhere on this tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hildis' father was Hilderic Christian Of Vandais and her mother was Amfleda Vandals.  Her paternal grandparents were Hunneric Vandals and Eudoric Eudoxia Vandais. She had a sister named Hildu.  She was the older of the two childre
2 CONC n.
