1 OCCU Shieldmaiden
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heidrek had a daughter who he named Hervor. She was a shieldmaiden and was the commander of a Gothic fort facing Myrkviðr, and she would fall in battle against the Huns.
2 CONT
2 CONT One morning at sunrise, Hervor stood on a tower over the fortress gate. She saw a great cloud of dust to the south near the forest, so that for a long time the sun was hidden. Then she saw something shining under the dust-cloud, a
2 CONC nd it seemed to her that she looked on gold: fair shields chased with gold, gilded helms and white byrnies. She saw then that this was the Hunnish army and a very great host it was.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hervor rushed down and called the trumpeter and ordered him to sound the alarm and assemble the army. And then Hervor said, “Take your weapons and prepare for battle, and you Ormar, ride to the Huns and challenge them to battle be
2 CONC fore the south gate.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Ormar spoke:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Sure I'll gallop
2 CONT
2 CONT grasping shield
2 CONT
2 CONT and give battle
2 CONT
2 CONT for the Gothic peoples.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Then Ormar rode from the fortress towards the army. He called in a loud voice and bade them ride to the fortress, “And out before the south gate upon the plain, there I challenge you to battle. Whoever comes first will wait for th
2 CONC e other.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Now Ormar rode back to the fortress, and found Hervor armed and all the army ready. Now they rode out of the fortress with their army against the Huns, and there began a mighty battle. And as the Huns have a much bigger force, the
2 CONC  slaughter turned to the Gothic side, and at last Hervor fell, and many Goths around her. And when Ormar saw her fall, he fled along with all who survived. Ormar rode day and night as fast as he could to King Angantyr in Arheimar.
2 CONC  The Huns now take to harrying the land, pillaging and burning far and wide.
2 CONT
2 CONT And when Ormar came before King Angantyr he said:
2 CONT
2 CONT “From the south I've come
2 CONT
2 CONT to say this news:
2 CONT
2 CONT burnt's Mirkwood Heath
2 CONT
2 CONT and the whole forest,
2 CONT
2 CONT Goth-folk all blotched
2 CONT
2 CONT with blood of men.”
2 CONT
2 CONT And again he spoke:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Down, I hear,
2 CONT
2 CONT is Heidrek's lass;
2 CONT
2 CONT heard your sister,
2 CONT
2 CONT the Huns felled her--
2 CONT
2 CONT and of your people
2 CONT
2 CONT plenty more.
2 CONT
2 CONT More cheery in battle
2 CONT
2 CONT than chatting to suitors
2 CONT
2 CONT or taking the bench
2 CONT
2 CONT at a bridal feast.”
2 CONT
2 CONT When King Angantyr heard this, he grinned and was slow to speak, but at last he said:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Unbrotherly
2 CONT
2 CONT the bloody game
2 CONT
2 CONT they played with you,
2 CONT
2 CONT excellent sister.”
