1 NOTE [edit] Hervor, Daughter of Heidrek
2 CONT Heidrek had a daughter who he named Hervor. She was a shieldmaiden and was the commander of a Gothic fort facing Myrkviðr, and she would fall in battle against the Huns (see Hlöd, Hlöðskviða). When Ormar reported Hervor's death 
2 CONC to king Angantyr, he said:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sunnan em ek kominn 
2 CONT at segja spjöll þessi: 
2 CONT sviðin er öll mörk 
2 CONT ok Myrkviðar heiðr, 
2 CONT drifin öll Goðþjóð 
2 CONT gumna blóði. 
2 CONT Mey veit ek Heiðreks, 
2 CONT systur þína, 
2 CONT svigna til jarðar; 
2 CONT hafa Húnar 
2 CONT hana fellda 
2 CONT ok marga aðra 
2 CONT yðra þegna, 
2 CONT léttari gerðist hún at böð 
2 CONT en við biðil ræða' 
2 CONT eða í bekk at fara 
2 CONT at brúðar gangi.  "From the south I've come 
2 CONT to say this news: 
2 CONT burnt's Mirkwood Heath 
2 CONT and the whole forest, 
2 CONT Goth-folk all blotched 
2 CONT with blood of men. 
2 CONT Down, I hear, 
2 CONT is Heidrek's lass; 
2 CONT heard your sister, 
2 CONT the Huns felled her - 
2 CONT and of your people 
2 CONT plenty more. 
2 CONT More cheery in battle 
2 CONT than chatting to suitors 
2 CONT or taking the bench 
2 CONT at a bridal feast."   
2 CONT
2 CONT When King Angantyr heard this, he grinned and was slow to speak, but at last he said:
2 CONT
2 CONT Óbróðurliga vartu leikin, in ágæta systir. 
2 CONT "Unbrotherly the bloody game they played with you, excellent sister." 
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Sources
2 CONT Herikson, Alf. (1998), Stora mytologiska uppslagsboken. 
