2 CONC kom í höfuð konungi skotit; féll hann þegar af hestinum ok fékk bana. Í þann tíma var sá höfðingi gramr kallaðr er herjaði, en hermennirnir gramir.[5] 		
2 CONT
2 CONT King Dygve's son, called Dag, succeeded to him, and was so wise a man that he understood the language of birds. He had a sparrow which told him much news, and flew to different countries. Once the sparrow flew to Reidgotaland, to 
2 CONC a farm called Varva, where he flew into the peasant's corn-field and took his grain. The peasant came up, took a stone, and killed the sparrow. King Dag was ill-pleased that the sparrow did not come home; and as he, in a sacrifice
2 CONC  of expiation, inquired after the sparrow, he got the answer that it was killed at Varva. Thereupon he ordered a great army, and went to Gotland; and when he came to Varva he landed with his men and plundered, and the people fled 
2 CONC away before him. King Dag returned in the evening to his ships, after having killed many people and taken many prisoners. As they were going across a river at a place called Skjotan's [the Weapon's] Ford, a labouring thrall came r
2 CONC unning to the river-side, and threw a hay- fork into their troop. It struck the king on the head, so that he fell instantly from his horse and died. In those times the chief who ravaged a country was called Gram, and the men-at-ar
2 CONC ms under him Gramer.[6][7] 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Then Snorri quoted Ynglingatal (9th century):
2 CONT
2 CONT     Frák at Dagr
2 CONT     dauða orði
2 CONT     frægðar fúss
2 CONT     of fara skyldi,
2 CONT     þá er valteins
2 CONT     til Vörva kom
2 CONT     spakfrömuðr
2 CONT     spörs at hefna.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ok þat orð
2 CONT     á austrvega
2 CONT     vísa ferð
2 CONT     frá vígi bar,
2 CONT     at þann gram
2 CONT     af geta skyldi
2 CONT     slöngviþref
2 CONT     Sleipnis verðar.[5][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT     What news is this that the king's men,
2 CONT     Flying eastward through the glen,
2 CONT     Report? That Dag the Brave, whose name
2 CONT     Is sounded far and wide by Fame --
2 CONT     That Dag, who knew so well to wield
2 CONT     The battle-axe in bloody field,
2 CONT     Where brave men meet, no more will head
2 CONT     The brave – that mighty Dag is dead!
2 CONT
2 CONT     Varva was wasted with the sword,
2 CONT     And vengeance taken for the bird --
2 CONT     The little bird that used to bring
2 CONT     News to the ear of the great king.
2 CONT     Varva was ravaged, and the strife
2 CONT     Was ended, when the monarch's life
2 CONT     Was ended too – the great Dag fell
2 CONT     By the hay-fork of a base thrall![6][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that Skjótansvað/Vápnavað appear both in Ynglinga saga and in Historia Norwegiæ's earlier summary of Ynglingatal but not in Snorri's later quotation from it, suggests that all of Ynglingatal was not presented by him.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Dag kunde kommunisera med fåglarna. Han brukade skicka ut dem för att få information. En gång slog en bonde ihjäl en av hans sparvar. För at hämnas reste Dag ut på plundringsfärd. På väg hemåt igen slängde en arbetsman en högaffel
2 CONC  i ryggen på honom och han dog.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. DAG - King from 190 to 220. The Saga tells that Dag had a special gift and could communicate with the birds. He had a sparrow which he would send to other countries to gather information for him. On one of the sparrow's visits 
2 CONC to another country, a peasant killed the sparrow. When Dag heard about this he took a great plundering expedition to avenge the bird's death. After plundering, raiding and killing many people. Dag was returning to his ship when a 
2 CONC workman in the field threw a hay fork into the troop, striking the king in the head, killing him. His son was:
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. AGNE - King from 220 to 260. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT King Dag was so wise that he understood the language of the birds. He had a pet sparrow who flew all over and brought him news. One day the sparrow was killed by a farmer. When he discovered that the farmer who killed his sparrow 
2 CONC lived in Varva, Gotland, he gathered an army and went plundering. But on that trip a laborer came running and threw a hay-fork which struck Dag in the head and killed him.
2 CONT --------------------
