1 NOTE Dag was King from 190 to 220. The Saga tells that Dag had a special gift and could communicate with the birds. He had a sparrow which he would send to other countries to gather information for him. On one of the sparrow’s visits t
2 CONC o another country, a peasant killed the sparrow. When Dag heard about this he took a great plundering expedition to avenge the bird’s death. After plundering, raiding and killing many people, Dag was returning to his ship when a w
2 CONC orkman in the field threw a hay fork into the troop, striking the king in the head, killing him. 
1 NOTE !SOURCES:
2 CONT     1. The Viking Age, Gen. Hist. 19, v. 1, p. 67
2 CONT     2. The Saga Library F Ice. 1, pt 4 of Heimskringla
