2 CONT King of Vestfold Hálfdan Mildi Eysteinsson was called Halfdan the Mild, but the Bad Entertainer; that is to say, he was reported to be generous, and to give his men as much gold as other kings gave of silver, but he starved them i
2 CONC n their diet. He was a great warrior, who had been long on Viking cruises, and had collected great property.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hlíf Dagsdóttir, daughter of konung av Vestmörum Dagr av Vestmörum.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Holtar, Vestfold, Norway, in his chief house, on the bed of sickness. He was buried in Borre, Raden, near Vodle, Vestfold, Norway, under a mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT So says Thjodolf: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "By Hel's summons, a great king
2 CONT
2 CONT Was called away to Odin's Thing:
2 CONT
2 CONT King Halfdan, he who dwelt of late
2 CONT
2 CONT At Holtar, must obey grim Fate.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Borre, in the royal mound,
2 CONT
2 CONT They laid the hero in the ground."
