1 NOTE 39th great grandfather
1 NOTE He ruled from 770 to 800.
1 NOTE He ruled from 770 to 800.
1 NOTE Halfdan, Halvdan II; 
2 CONT Eysteinsson, Oysteinsson
2 CONT "the Mild (le Débonnaire)", "the Old of Oppland", "Halfdan the Old" (second)
2 CONT roi (King) de Vestfold 750-800 , (vers 755 - vers 802) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was called Halfdan the Mild, but the Bad Entertainer; that is to say, he was reported to be generous, and to give his men as much gold as other kings gave of silver, but he starved them in their diet. He was a great warrior, wh
2 CONC o had been long on viking cruises, and had collected great property. 
2 CONT Holtar, in Westfold, was his chief house; and he died there on the bed of sickness, and was buried at Borre under a mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT
