2 CONC n Ragnarsson (Halfdene) and Ubbe Ragnarsson (Hubba), invaded the East Anglian region of England. An accommodation was quickly reached with the East Anglians. The following year, Ivar led his forces north on horseback and easily ca
2 CONC ptured Jorvik from the Northumbrians who were at that time engaged in a civil war.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ivar is also attributed with the slaying of St Edmund of East Anglia in 869 AD.
2 CONT
