1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''refer to other language tabs for Swedish / Danish / Norwegian''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%B6rn_Ironside
2 CONT
2 CONT Björn Ironside was a legendary king of Sweden who lived sometime in the 9th century. He is said to have been the first ruler of the Munsö dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hervarar saga ok Heiðreks (The Saga of Hervör and Heidrek)''' tells that Eysteinn Beli was killed by Björn and his brothers as told in Ragnar Lodbrok's saga, and they conquered all of Sweden. When Ragnar died Björn Ironside inh
2 CONC erited Sweden. He had two sons, Refil and Erik Björnsson, who became the next king of Sweden.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ragnarssona þáttr (The Tale of Ragnar's Sons)''' tells that he was the son of the Scandinavian king Ragnar Lodbrok and Aslaug, and that he had the brothers Hvitserk, Ivar the Boneless and Sigurd Snake-in-the-Eye, and the half-b
2 CONC rothers Fridleif, Eric and Agnar.
2 CONT
2 CONT The '''Annales Bertiniani''' and the '''Chronicon Fontanellense''' tell of a Viking leader named Berno who pillaged on the Seine in the 850s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Around 1070, '''William of Jumièges''' referred to him as Bier Costae ferreae (Ironside) who was Lotbroci regis filio (son of king Lodbrok).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT His ancestry is found in other parts of this tree. Bjorn (Ironside)'s father was Ragnar "Lodbrock" Sigurdsson and his mother was Aslaug Sigurdsdatter. His paternal grandparents were Sigurd "Ring" Randversson and Alfhild Gandolfsda
2 CONC tter; his maternal grandparents were Sigurd (Fafnisbana) Sigmundsson and Bynhild Budlasdatter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bjørn was one of the major Viking raiders from the mid 850s until 862. During 856-7 he was on the Seine and his name is associated with the vikings who established or took over a base on the island of Oissel where they were at las
2 CONC t beleagured by Charles the Bald. They managed to raise the siege after 12 weeks. Later he and Hastein made a four year cruise with 62 ships to Spain, North Africa and Italy and possibly further east. Two of their ships laden with
2 CONC  gold, silver and prisoners were captured by the Moors off the coast of Spain. They were next at Guadalquivar but did not prosper and some say they went upriver as far as Seville. Then through the Straits of Gibralter to Algeciras
2 CONC  to plunder and next to the North African shore in the Cabo Tres Forcas region where they rounded up prisoners for ransom and took a few with them who eventually wound up in Ireland. Then it was back to Spain's Murcia coast, the B
2 CONC alearics, southern France and sacked Narbonne and then wintered on the island of Camargue in the Rhone delta. They raided Arles, Nimes and Valence but took a beating from the Franks and went to the Ligurian Riviera and then raided
2 CONC  Pisa and east to Alexandria, raided Luna mistakenly thinking it was Rome, and by 861were back at Gibralter where the Moorish fleet defeated them. The survivors reached Navarre and captured Pamplona and ransomed its prince and in 
2 CONC 862 one 20 of the 62 ships sailed safely back into the mouth of the Loire.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT He led the great Viking raid around Spain into the Mediterranean, 859. Bjørn Ironside certainly played an important role in France. His father Ragnar Lodbrok can be identified in contemporary Frankish annals with his nickname Lodb
2 CONC rok translated to Hoseri (in German language Hosen), meaning fur or leather breeches. Variations are Ogier and Oschery. He operated from the Seine to the border of Spain from 840 to 851. He conquered Aquitania from the Franks, and
2 CONC  he used Bordeaux as his stronghold for years. This conquer, one out of more, included Poitou, which in the sagas is called Peita. Saxo is saying Petiæ and that Ragnar conquered Petiæ. this is confirmed in annals. This is the dist
2 CONC rict in the Loire area. In Western Europe his sons are more reported. Ragnar Lodbrok himself were operating more in East Europe
2 CONT
2 CONT ====================
