2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bj%C3%B6rn_Ironside
2 CONT Björn Ironside (Old Norse: Björn Járnsíða, Swedish: Björn Järnsida) 
2 CONT Swedish king (ca 785-800) was a legendary viking from the 8th century. 
2 CONT He was one of the sons of Ragnar Lodbrok. He pillaged in Italy and 
2 CONT took part in the conquest of Paris with his father Ragnar Lodbrok.
2 CONT He acquired the name Ironside because he was never wounded in battle. 
2 CONT This invulnerability was attributed to his mother Aslaug's use of seid 
2 CONT in order to make him impervious to iron and steel.
2 CONT According to Hervarar saga he inherited Sweden from his father while 
2 CONT his brother Sigurd Snake-Eye inherited the remainder of Scandinavia.
2 CONT The dynasty he founded is called the House of Munsö by modern 
2 CONT historians, because a local tradition claims that he is buried in 
2 CONT Björnshögen at Husby on the island of Munsö. Many of his dynasty were 
2 CONT to be named Björn.
2 CONT He had two sons, Refil and Erik Björnsson, and Erik succeeded him on 
2 CONT the throne.
2 CONT Nedan från
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Muns%C3%B6
2 CONT The House of Munsö is the Scandinavian semi-legendary dynasty which is 
2 CONT descended from Björn Ironside, one of the sons of Ragnar Lodbrok. 
2 CONT According to Saxo Grammaticus, it was a branch of the House of 
2 CONT Yngling. It is named after the island on which Björn Ironside is 
2 CONT reputedly buried. If the sources are correct, the dynasty was to rule 
2 CONT Sweden from the late 8th century until 1060.
2 CONT It is also called the House of Ivar and Ragnar Lodbrok, the Old 
2 CONT Dynasty or the House of Uppsala.
