2 CONT BJÖRN I "Ironside" 804.  
2 CONT ERIK I Björnson 808.  
2 CONT ERIK II Raefilson 820.  
2 CONT EMUND (reigned in the south) and BJÖRN II (reigned at Uppsala) 859.  
2 CONT ERIK III Emundson  873.  Snorre records that "Eirik Eymundson king of 
2 CONT Sweden" conquered Vermaland and areas to the north to Svinasund, 
2 CONT calling the territory "West Gautland", appointing Hrane Gauzke as 
2 CONT jarl[3].  Snorre records the death of King Eirik Eymundson when King 
2 CONT Harald had been "ten years king of all Norway"[4].  
