2 CONC  Gerda Hålgadottir , Ladgerda, from Gaulardal near Lade todays Trondheim was in Ragnars age and they met in Lade when Ragnar was newly chosen King after his father Sigurd Ring Randversson. Ragnar and Ladgerda had three documented 
2 CONC children . One son Fridleif and two unnamed daughters. After he left Ladgerda to deal with an uprise against him in Denmark he sailed to east Geatland to meet Earl Herröd. Herröd wanted after an event that Ragnar should marry his 
2 CONC daughter Thora which Ragnar did. They had two sons Erik and Agnar. Anyway Thora died young appr 815-817when the boys were small. According to documents in Norway and Iceland Ragnar became depressed and restless and couldn't stay h
2 CONC ome. He sailed away with his men raiding. On one 'sailtrip' he came to the very southmost part of Norway where he met Aslög Sigurdsdatter for the first time. They married and had many children among them Ivar 'Boneless', Björn 'Ir
2 CONC onside,' Sigurd 'Snake-in-the eye', Halvdan 'Vitserk', Rognvald, Ragnhild, Husto, Aalof, Radbard. If we consider ages here, Thora would have been born appr 800 and mother of at 15-17 .  Aslög would have been born appr 805 and moth
2 CONC er of Ivar around appr 820 as 15-17 years of age. Ladgerda is written to have died in Leire 873 and Aslög 883 in Ringerike. Ivar died in Ireland 873 perhaps burried in Repton near a church where a Kings grave is found from his dea
2 CONC thyears. Björn drowned on his way back from the Mediterranean Sea outside the Frisian coast together with Hastein. Therefore Björn couldn't participate in the killing of King Aella 866. Sigurd 'Snake in the eye' died 891 born appr
2 CONC  824. His daughter Ragnhild was married to Halvdan 'the Black' father of Harald ' Fairhair Halvdanson. Haldan  'Vitserk' took Kiev 866 but was ambushed by Oleg 882. Probably born appr.826. Ubbe is a halfbrother and the result of R
2 CONC agnars visit to earl Esbjörn in Frisland where he met Gisla Esbjörnsdaughter. That happened while Ragnar was in relation with Aslög as Ubbe was fighting and a leader same years as Ivar, Björn, Sigurd, Halvdan and Rognvald
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT A mythical viking warrior, potentially based on a historical person, Eric is described in the sagas and other earl medieval sources as one of the eldest sons of Ragnar Loðbrók.
2 CONT Important to understand that 'sagas' are not fairytales. The word 'saga' is related to nowadays ' utsaga' meaning outsaying , statement and telling. These days most people were not literate ( could read and write ) and all informa
2 CONC tion about births, deaths, marriages, trade, warfare, punishments was communicated oral around a bonfire with elders experienced people.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eric and his brother, Agnar, are accomplished warriors famous in their own rite and attack the vasal- King Eystein Beli' Haraldsen  of Uppsala that their father Ragnar and ( Harald 'Hildetann' Röreksson  installed in Sweden to rul
2 CONC e in Ragnar's absencee. The Swedish chieftains unify against the two brothers, remaining loyal to Ragnar, and the brothers are overcome. Agnar is killed out right while Eric is captured and chooses to die rather than accept defeat
2 CONC . 
2 CONT The defeat and death of Erik and Agnar triggers a revenge attack on King Eystein by their step-mother Aslaug and her son's Ivar, Sigurd, Bjorn and Halvdan ( Hvitserk) who slay the vasal-king for killing their elder brothers.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Further Reading===
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tale_of_Ragnar%27s_Sons Wikipedia]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Danish_History/Book_IX Saxo]
2 CONT *[http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/ThattrRagnarsSonar.html Ragnarsson Saga]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT *Date of birth based on father's birth as discussed [http://www.geni.com/discussions/129645?msg=1013734 '''here'''] and [http://www.geni.com/discussions/129645?msg=1013825 '''here'''].
2 CONT *Location of birth based on his father, Ragnar, being most commonly referred to as king of Denmark. 
2 CONT *Date of death based on birth dates of his brothers Ivar, Sigurd, Bjorn and Hvitserk who saga tradition recounts all participate in avenging his death.  
2 CONT *Location of death based on King Eystein marching from Uppsala to defeat Eric and Agnar.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT “Don’t care, cur, to hear you, killer if you offer; (Eystein, they say, slew Agnar) I don’t want your daughter. To mourn me I’ve no mother; make haste, hey!, impale me. I’ll die over host hoisted, highest o’er the slaughter.”
2 CONT
2 CONT And before he was lifted up on the spears, he saw a man riding hard. Then he said:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Send word to my slender sweet stepmother, greet her: (my forays east are ended) say all my rings are hers. Great will grow their anger when they get to know it, when she brings her bounteous boys news of my demise.”
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.germanicmythology.com/FORNALDARSAGAS/ThattrRagnarsSonar.html
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
