2 CONT Ubbi, Ubbo dux Fresiorum 
1 NOTE Ubbi ‘the Frisian’, leader of the ‘Scaldingi’, the vikings of the 
2 CONT Scheldt, that came to England in 855. In later sources he was 
2 CONT identified as a son of the legendary Ragnarr Loðbrókk. He was killed 
2 CONT in battle in Wessex in 878. 
1 NOTE source: HC 50, 52; ALD 506; AL 53; CR 16; ASC 71; VAM 62; ASC 878; VE 
2 CONT 510-511  
1 NOTE http://genuki.cs.ncl.ac.uk/DEV/Northam/WestwardHoMurray1879.html
1 NOTE The village of Appledore is interesting for its antiquity, and for a 
2 CONT legend of the Danish warrior Hubba, who is said to have landed near 
2 CONT this village, in the reign of Alfred, from a fleet of 33 ships, and to 
2 CONT have laid siege to a neighbouring castle, called Kenwith, the site of 
2 CONT which is now only surmised to be a hill called Henny Castle (near 
2 CONT Kenwith Lodge), N.W. of Bideford. The strength of this place, however, 
2 CONT proved too great for its assailants. Hubba was slain under its walls, 
2 CONT and his followers driven with slaughter to the shore. At one spot, it 
2 CONT is said, they rallied, and so checked their pursuers as to be enabled 
2 CONT to regain their ships; and a field by the roadside, near the village 
2 CONT of Northam, is to this day pointed out as the place where they turned, 
2 CONT and has been known from time immemorial as the Bloody Corner. Biorn 
2 CONT Ironside, the companion of Hubba, was slain in this headlong retreat, 
2 CONT and the magical Raven banner was taken by the English. It was a black 
2 CONT bird, probably a stuffed specimen of the raven, which hung quiet when 
2 CONT defeat was at hand, but clapped its wings before victory. Hubba, we 
2 CONT are told, was buried beneath a cairn on the shore, and the name of 
2 CONT Hubblestone - given to a flat rock near the quay at Appledore - is 
2 CONT said to mark the locality. This defeat took place in Devonshire (Sax. 
2 CONT Chron. ad ann. 877-78); but the identification of the site with Henny 
2 CONT Castle is quite uncertain.
