1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dette er feil Ragnhild Dagsdatter da hun er født ca 970. Det er mer sannsynlig Eiliv Ormsson Bratsberg var gift med ei datter av Dag Ringsson Oplendene (født ca 990) som er barnebarn av kong Dag Ringsson i Hedemark
2 CONC en og NN Finnsdatter. På en pussig måte er datteren til Dag Ringsson Oplendene gitt navnet Eiliv, som Eiliv Ormsson! Det er mer sannsynlig at Dag Ringsson Oplendenes datter bør være Ragnhild Dagsdatter født ca 1040, og ikke Eiliv.
2 CONC  (Se: https://www.geni.com/people/Dag-Oplendene/6000000001169224371?through=6000000001169224362)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Ranghild Dagsdotter=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Dag Ringsson Hedmark
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#_Toc360005218 Kings of Norway From Project MedLands]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dag Ringsson, King of Hedemark'''  m ---.  The name of Dag's wife is not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dag & his wife had three children'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * (i)          '''RÖREK''' (-1021).  Snorre names "two brothers…Hrorek and Ring" as kings in Hedemark, recording that they supported the accession of King Olav Haraldson[116].  King of Hedemark.  He was blinded on the orders of Ol
2 CONC av II King of Norway. 
2 CONT * (ii)         '''RING'''  Snorre names "two brothers…Hrorek and Ring" as kings in Hedemark, recording that they supported the accession of King Olav Haraldson[118].  King of Hedemark.  He was banished on the orders of Olav II Kin
2 CONC g of Norway[119].  m ---.  The name of Ring's wife is not known.  
2 CONT * (iii)        '''RAGNHILD'''  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  m '''RAUD, from Österdalen.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ring & his wife had two children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a)       '''DAG Ringsson'''  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  1030.
2 CONT * (b)       '''EMUND Ringsson'''  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  An official in Polotzk.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' - http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWAY.htm#_Toc360005218
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://snl.no/Ring_Dagsson RING DAGSSON (Hringr), by the NORWEGIAN ENCYCLOPEDIA]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ring is mentioned in the sagas as king in Ringsaker at the beginning of the 1000s. Snorre's royal sagas claim that he was the great-grandson of Harald Hårfagre , and thus a relative of both King Olav Tryggvason and King Olav Haral
2 CONC dsson .
2 CONT
2 CONT The sagas tell that he was part of the association of five little kings around Lake Mjøsa who wanted to fight Olav Haraldsson. Rørek , the leader of the association, is said to have been Ring's brother. Olav Haraldsson and his men
2 CONC , however, surprised the kings at Ring's home, and they were taken prisoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav Haraldsson left Rørek blind, while Ring was sent out of the country. He is said to have settled in Sweden where he held a high position.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Snorre's royal sagas say that Ring's sister, Ragnhild, is said to have married the Swede Raud, and lived in Østerdalen . They became King Olav's friends, and their sons, Dag and Sigurd, joined Olav's hird.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT When Knut the Mighty came to Norway in 1028, King Olav fled to Sweden and sought out Dag , the son of Ring. It is unclear whether Ring was still alive, but a verse composed by Olav's poet Tormod Kolbrunarskald mentions that Ring a
2 CONC nd Dag were leaders in the battle of Stiklestad in 1030. If this is Ring Dagsson, he must have either fallen in the battle or died shortly after. In that case, contrary to what is said about his brother Rørek, he must have reconci
2 CONC led with King Olav after his exile.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
