2 CONT The sagas tell that he was part of the association of five little kings around Lake Mjøsa who wanted to fight Olav Haraldsson. Rørek , the leader of the association, is said to have been Ring's brother. Olav Haraldsson and his men
2 CONC , however, surprised the kings at Ring's home, and they were taken prisoner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav Haraldsson left Rørek blind, while Ring was sent out of the country. He is said to have settled in Sweden where he held a high position.
2 CONT
2 CONT Snorre's royal sagas say that Ring's sister, Ragnhild, is said to have married the Swede Raud, and lived in Østerdalen . They became King Olav's friends, and their sons, Dag and Sigurd, joined Olav's hird.
