1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Marriage: 1282 and not 1252 see [https://books.google.fr/books?id=pIFCAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA331 La Belgique héraldique]: recueil historique, chronologique, généalogique et biographique complet de toutes les maisons noble
2 CONC s reconnues de la Belgique, Adriaens, 1867. or [https://books.google.fr/books?id=_RJTAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA8 Généalogie de la famille de Roye], originaire de Picardie Fel. Vict Goethals Polack-Duvivier, 1854
2 CONT
2 CONT And other sources  like Histoire de la ville de Roye Émile Coët - H. Champion, 1880
2 CONT
2 CONT * Note : Can't be born 20 years after her father dies as My Heritage sources pretend ! better source are needed
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfravalver.htm#MarieRoyeMRobertWavrin
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)       '''  [MARIE de Roye''' (-after Apr 1282).  Guy Count of Flanders confirmed the sale of revenue “partie de son fief de Vlargelo dans les paroisses de Schore et de Kayhem” to Lille abbey made by “messire Robert de Wavrin S
2 CONC ire de Saint-Venant”, making provision for “Marie de Roye sa femme” should Robert predecease her, by charter dated Apr 1282[896].  Goethals names Jean Seigneur de Roye and his wife “l’héritière de Hangest” as her parents[897]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' [as his first wife,] ROBERT de Wavrin Seigneur de Saint-Venant, son of ROBERT [II] de Wavrin & his [first wife Eustachie de Châtillon/second wife Mathilde de Béthune] ([1230/50]-[1308]).] 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
