1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Florence de Lalaing'''
2 CONT (mineure en 1338) + 13/08/1380 (inh. à Berelles)
2 CONT
2 CONT  ép. dès 1346 Gillon de Reumont (alias Gilles de Rumont) (cadets de la Maison de Roisin) 
2 CONT
2 CONT chevalier, seigneur de Rumont et Berelle, homme de fief du Hainaut (cité 02/05/1362 dans un acte à Mons ; armes : «Bandé de gueules & d’argent de six pièces, brisure au lambel de trois pendants de gueules»)
2 CONT postérité Reumont dont Jean, seigneur de «Ruymont» & Bérelle
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT Mineure en 1338.
2 CONT Source : F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT Source : FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT Death: F Brasssart, 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Florence de Lalaing''', minor in 1338 and (29,) We find in the account of the Grand Bailliag) of Hainaut, from September 15, 1350 to May 15, 1351, fo 4 vo, that at the request of "monsr Simon de Lalaing", the bailiff "fist arri
2 CONC ester, sour monsr Joffroit de Saindizier, no property belonging to the tiestament monsr le ovesque de Vredun ", cited with two of his sisters, Marie and Jeanne, in a receipt that their eldest brother issued, in their name, to the 
2 CONC lady of Aspremont (their maternal grandmother ), to Quiévrain, on the Sunday after Christmas Day (December 27) 1338, for the arrears of an annuity of 200 livres which the said lady owed on account of the marriage of the late lord 
2 CONC and the lady of Lalaing, which annuity had been assigned in the share, of these three young ladies.
2 CONT
2 CONT (29)	Saint-Genois, Monum. anciens, Paris, 1782, in-fo, I,-p. 225.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne,  Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 25-
2 CONC 26.''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''FLORENCE de Lalaing''' (-13 Aug 1380, bur Berelles).  “Collart Sire de Lallaing...”, for himself and on behalf of “ses trois sœurs Florence, Marie et Jeanne”, acknowledged receipt of payments due from “Isabiaus de Kievraing Dam
2 CONC e de Spremont” connected with the marriage of “Simon Sgr de Lallaing son pere et de sa mere” by charter dated end-Dec 1338[410].  A charter dated 21 Dec 1346 records that “Nicollon signeur de Lalaing sen aisnet fil chevalier” sold
2 CONC  property with the consent of “...Gillion de Reumont et demisielle Florence sa femme, demisielle Margherite de Lalaing canoinnesse de Malboege, demisielle Marie de Lalaing canoinesse de Niuielle, et demisielle Gille de Lalaing, se
2 CONC reurs audit signeur de Lalaing”[411].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([Dec 1338/Dec 1346]) GILLES de Reumont, son of --- (-bur Berelles). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Cawley, Charles. “NORTHERN FRANCE-CAMBRAI, DOUAI, VALENCIENNES.” Medieval Lands, Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, 24 Mar. 2022, https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfracado.htm#_Toc44147371''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT Curator note: Le village est l'ancien fief des seigneurs de Bérelles. Il fut par la suite sous l'autorité des seigneurs de Barbençon.
2 CONT “ The village is the former stronghold of the lords of Bérelles. It was subsequently under the authority of the lords of Barbençon.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:
2 CONT Mineure en 1338.
2 CONT Source : F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT Source : FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT Death: F Brasssart, 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Florence de Lalain'''
2 CONT (minor in 1338) + 13/08/1380 (inh. in Berelles) 
2 CONT th. from 1346 Gillon de Reumont (alias Gilles de Rumont) (cadets of the House of Roisin) knight, lord of Rumont and Berelle, man of fief of Hainaut (cited 02/05/1362 in an act in Mons; arms: "Bandé de Gules & Argent of six pieces,
2 CONC  broken on the label of three pendant gules")
2 CONT Reumont posterity including Jean, lord of “Ruymont” & Bérelle
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
