2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Willem III van Nevele, Heer van Oosthosen
2 _PRIM Y
2 NOTE The Heraldic Proof: The "Gavere Upgrade"
3 CONT The most technical proof of this descent is the color of the shield.
3 CONT * Old Nevele (Pre-Gavere): Argent (Silver), a cross gules.
3 CONT * Nevele-Gavere (Post-Raso VIII): Or (Gold), a cross gules.
3 CONT Willem II used the Gold field. In medieval heraldry, you could only change the "metal" of a shield (from Silver to Gold) if you were incorporating the colors of a superior or more prestigious house. By using the Gold of the Gavere
3 CONC  Lions for the Nevele Cross, Willem II was visually shouting: "I am a Gavere by blood, even if I am a Nevele by land."
