1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Ragnhild 'Hild' Hrólfsdóttir Nefia (Nefja), married to Ragnvald Mørejarl.
2 CONT
2 CONT (NB: These are Norwegians, and NOT from Orkney. Ragnhild was born in Vestfold, Norway, and died in Norway. OBS: There is NO SUCH PLACE as "Maer" in Nord-Trøndelag, and Møre where her husband was the Earl (Jarl) is NOT in Trøndelag
2 CONC . Hild was NOT a "countess", such titles did not exist at the time. Please remove such bad data.)
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Roger Slektsforskning:''' [http://slektsforskning.com/login/person/anetre/tekst/Hild%20Rolvsdattereng.asp Hild Rolvsdatter]
2 CONT * '''Idar Lind:''' ''Norrøn mytologi frå A til Å'' (Det Norske Samlaget) [http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=asatru&person=Hild%20daughter%20of%20 Rolf Hild Rolvsdotter (Hildi Hrólfsdóttir)]
2 CONT * '''Tore Nygard:''' [http://www.tore-nygaard.com/middelalder/2213.htm Hild Rolvsdatter]
2 CONT ** Tore Nygaard oppdaterte nettsiden sin. — Tore Nygaard updated his website.27. november 2022.
2 CONT ** 'Han sier: «Jeg har funnet det nødvendig å fjerne Java-avhengige applikasjoner.» — He says, "I have found it necessary to remove Java-dependent applications."
2 CONT '''———————————————————————————————'''
2 CONT Hild Rolvsdatter levde fra 845 til 886. Hun var datter av odelsbonden Rolv Nevja. Nefja eller Nevja er ikke et slektsnavn, men et tilnavn faren Rolv hadde. Betydninger er "nese" og hadde trolig å gjøre med skatteinnkreving (pr. ne
2 CONC se). Hild er kjent som "datter av Rolf Nefja".
2 CONT
2 CONT Hild var gift med Ragnvald Mørejarl. Død omkring 890. De hadde barna:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hertug Gange-Rolv Ragnvaldson av Normandie. Født mellom 860 og 866. Død 931. 2. Tore Teiande Ragnvaldson Mørejarl. Født omkring 862. Død mellom 938 og 940.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hild (Ragnhild) reiste til kong Harald Hårfagre for å be om nåde for sin sønn, Gange-Rolv, da han av kongen ca. 886 var lyst fredløs over hele Norge på grunn av strandhugg i Viken, men Gange-Rolv måtte forlate landet.
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Medlands: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#Ragnvalddied894B Norway Nobility]
2 CONT '''RAGNVALD "the Wise"''', son of [EYSTEIN "Glumra/Clatterer" Jarl in Norway & his wife ---] (-[894]). ''Orkneyinga Saga'' names “Eystein the Clatterer, father of the wise counsellor Earl Rognwald the Powerful…”, adding that “Earl
2 CONC  Rognwald campaigned with King Harald Fine-Hair who gave him charge of North More, South More and Romsdale”[145]. Snorre names "Ragnvald Earl of More, a son of Eystein Glumra" when recording that he had become a supporter of King 
2 CONC Harald who had invested him with the districts of North More and Raumsdal[146].  Snorre records that he was created Jarl of North and South Möre and of Raumsdal in Norway by Harald I "Hårfagre" King of Norway after his victory at 
2 CONC Solskiel [869] against Hunthiof King of Möre and Nokve King of Raumsdal[147]. ''Orkneyinga Saga'' and Snorre both record that King Harald granted Shetland and Orkney to Ragnvald in compensation for the death of his son Ivar[148]. 
2 CONC The ''Historia Norwegie'' records that "''principi Rogwaldi''" crossed the Solund Sea, destroyed the peoples of the Orkney islands, in the days of "''Haraldi Comati regis…Norwegie''"[149]. ''Orkneyinga Saga'' records that “Halfdan
2 CONC  Long-Leg and Gudrod Gleam, King Harald´s sons by Snæfrid” attacked “Earl Rognvald of More, killed him and assumed his authority”[150]. Snorre records that Ragnvald was ambushed in his hall and burned alive by Halfdan Haaleg and G
2 CONC udred Liomi, two of King Harald's sons[151]. '''–''' '''m''' ['''RAGNHILD''', daughter of HROLF “Nevja/Nose” & his wife ——. ''Orkneyinga Saga'' records that “Earl Rognwald” married “Ragnhild the daughter of Hrolf Nose”[148]. Snorr
2 CONC e names "Hild, a daughter of Rolf Nefia" as the wife of "Earl Ragnvald"[149].] '''—''' '''[Ragnvald & his wife had four children:]'''
2 CONT #  ['''IVAR''' (-killed in battle either Hafrsfiord [872] or Orkney [874]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Ivar and Thorer the Silent” as the two other sons of “Earl Rognwald” and his wife “Ragnhild the daughter of Hrolf Nose”, adding th
2 CONC at Ivar was killed in battle fighting with Harald I "Hårfagre" King of Norway in Scotland[150].   Snorre names "Ivar, a son of Ragnvald Earl of More" when recording his death in battle during a Viking campaign against the Scottish
2 CONC  islands[151].  The Complete Peerage dates the appointment of Sigurd (Ivar´s reported paternal uncle) as Jarl of Orkney to [875][152], which means that Ivar must have been killed shortly before this date.  However, as explained be
2 CONC low this causes considerable chronological difficulties with the reported events in the career of Turf-Einar, Ivar´s youngest illegitimate half-brother, so should be considered as extremely approximate.  
2 CONT # ['''ROLLO''' [Hrolf "Ganger/the Walker"] (-[928]).  Orkneyinga Saga names “Hrolf who conquered Normandy” as son of “Earl Rognwald” and his wife “Ragnhild the daughter of Hrolf Nose”, adding that he was so big that no horse could
2 CONC  carry him, giving rise to his name “Göngu-Hrolf”[153].   Snorre names "Rolf and Thorer" as the two sons of "Earl Ragnvald" and his wife Hild, recording that Rolf was banished from Norway by King Harald and travelled to the Hebrid
2 CONC es, settling first in Orkney before moving southwards through Scotland, and eventually conquering Normandy[154].  The Historia Norwegie records that, after Orkney was conquered by "principi Rogwaldi" and his followers, "de quorum 
2 CONC collegio…Rodulfus" captured Rouen in Normandy, commenting that he was known as "Gongurolfr" because he was obliged to walk as he was too large to travel on horseback[155].  This source makes no reference to any blood relationship 
2 CONC between Rollo and "principi Rogwaldi".   According to Dudo of Saint-Quentin, Rollo arrived in northern France in 876[156], although there is some debate about [900] being a more likely date[157].  William of Jumièges records that 
2 CONC Rollo was chosen by lot to be leader of the Viking colonists[158].  Viking raids intensified in northern France.  Although they were defeated after raiding Chartres [911], Charles III "le Simple" King of the West Franks granted th
2 CONC e Normans land around Rouen in which to settle[159].  The uncertain nature of the demise was the source of future problems between the French crown, which claimed that it was an enfeofment for which the ruler owed allegiance, and 
2 CONC the later Dukes of Normandy who claimed it was an unconditional allod for which no allegiance was owed.  A charter dated 14 Mar 918 which granted land to the monastery of Saint-Germain-des-Prés "except that part…which we have gran
2 CONC ted to the Normans of the Seine, namely to Rollo and his companions"[160].  He was later known as '''ROBERT I Comte [de Normandie]'''.]   –  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY.htm#RobertIdied928 '''DUKES of NORMANDY''']. 
2 CONT # [THORE Ragnvaldsson "Tause/the Silent".  Orkneyinga Saga names “Ivar and Thorer the Silent” as the two other sons of “Earl Rognwald” and his wife “Ragnhild the daughter of Hrolf Nose”[161].  Snorre names "Rolf and Thorer" as the
2 CONC  two sons of "Earl Ragnvald" and his wife Hild[162].  He succeeded his father in [894] as Jarl of Möre, having dispossessed Gudrod "Ljome", son of King Harald, who had seized Möre on the death of Jarl Ragnvald[163].   m ([890]) AL
2 CONC OF "Aarbod/Season-bettering", daughter of HARALD I "Hårfagre/Harfagri/Fairhair" King of Norway & his second wife Gyda of Hordaland.  Snorre records that King Harald gave Jarl Thore his daughter "Alof, called Arbot" after the king 
2 CONC confirmed him as Jarl of Möre[164].]  [Thore & his wife had one child:] 
2 CONT ## a) ['''BERGLJOT Thoresdatter'''. The ''Historia Norwegie'' names "''Bergliota filia Thoris Tacentis''", from "''nobilissima Morensium ac Halogensium comitum prosapia''", as the wife of "Siwardo"[165]. Snorre names "''Bergljot, 
2 CONC a daughter of Earl Thorer the Silent''" & his wife as the wife of Sigurd[166].  '''m''' [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORWEGIAN%20NOBILITY.htm#Sigurddied962 '''SIGURD'''] Jarl,  son of HAAKON Grjotgardson Jarl of Haalogaland & 
2 CONC his wife -- (-murdered Oglo 962).]
2 CONT # ['''GORM'''. Guillaume de Jumièges refers to an unnamed Danish warrior “dux” who left two sons “maior natu Rollo, alter...iunior Gurim”[168]. Gorm is '''not''' referred to in the Sagas.]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[Ragnvald had three illegitimate children by unknown mistresses:]...&c.''' 
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT Fra Snorre Sturlason: Harald Hårfagres saga: «24. Ragnvald Mørejarl var den kjæreste venn kong Harald hadde, og kongen satte ham høyt, Ragnvald jarl var gift med Hild, datter til Rolv Nevja (Nese); deres sønner var Rolv og Tore. .
2 CONC .. Rolv var en stor viking; Han var så svær av vekst at ingen hest kunne bære ham, derfor gikk han til fots overalt. Han ble kalt Gange-Rolv. Han herjet ofte i Austerveg. En sommer han kom østfra til Viken fra vikingtog, hogg han 
2 CONC strandhogg der. Kong Harald var i Viken; han ble alvorlig sint, da han fikk høre om dette, for han hadde strengt forbudt å rane innenlands. Kongen lyste på tinget at han gjorde Rolv fredløs i Norge. Da Hild, Rolvs mor, fikk vite d
2 CONC ette, dro hun til kongen på ba om fred for Rolv, men kongen var så sint at det nyttet henne ikke å be. Da kvat Hild dette: Du vraker Nevjas navne, driver som varg av landet bønders kjekke helbror; hvorfor så bister, herre? farlig 
2 CONC å vise ulvhug mot slik en ulv, høvding; han blir ikke god mot fyrstens flokk om til skogs han renner». 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1). Snorre Sturlason: Harald Hårfagres saga, avsnitt 24. Mogens Bugge: Våre forfedre, nr. 281. Bent og Vidar Billing Hansen: Rosensverdslektens forfedre, side 76. 
2 CONT ----------------------------------
2 CONT "Earl Ragnvald was King Harald's dearest friend, and the king had the greatest regard for him. He was married to Hild, a daughter of Rolf Nefia, and their sons were Rolf and Thorer. Earl Ragnvald had also three sons by concubines,
2 CONC  -- the one called Hallad, the second Einar, the third Hrollaug; and all three were grown men when their brothers born in marriage were still children Rolf became a great viking, and was of so stout a growth that no horse could ca
2 CONC rry him, and wheresoever he went he must go on foot; and therefore he was called Rolf Ganger." (from Harald Hårfagre's saga)
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT '''Ragnhild Hrolfsdottir (1) F, #104778''' 
2 CONT Last Edited=28 Oct 2002    
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnhild Hrolfsdottir was also known as Hilda (?). Children of Ragnhild Hrolfsdottir and Ragnvald I 'the Wise' Eysteinsson, Earl of More -1. Ivar Ragnvaldsson (1) -2. Thori 'the Silent' Ragnvaldsson, Jarl of More+ (1) -3. Rollo Ra
2 CONC gnvaldsson, 1st Duc de Normandie+ b. c 846, d. c 931 (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10478.htm#i104778
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.geneajourney.com/nrmndy.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnvald I, "the Wise", Jarl of North and South More and of Ramsdal, b abt 832, Norway, d 890. He md Hiltrude abt 850, daughter of Hrolf Nefia. She was b abt 834. Child of Ragnvald the Wise and Hiltrude was: Rollo/Robert I of Norm
2 CONC andy [a], 1st Duke of Normandy, aka Ganger Rolf, b abt 855, Norway, d abt 927-931, prob Normandy, France. He md Poppa of Bayeux abt 886, daughter of Berenger,Count of Bayeux. She was b abt 876.
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT
2 CONT Ragnhild är sannolikt moder till såväl den berömde 'Gånge-Rolf' som faderns efterträdare som jarl i Möre, Norge, Tore 'den tyste'. (Källa: Directory of Royal Genealogical Data, Hull, England) Hild Nevja Rolvsdatter levde mellan år
2 CONC  845 och 886. Hild (Ragnhild) reste till kung Harald 'Hårfager' för att be om nåd för sin son, Gånge-Rolf, då han av kungen cirka år 886 blev fredlös över hela Norge på grund av ett otillåtet strandhugg i Viken, Norge. (Källa: Kje
2 CONC ll Høyer, Norge)
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT The mother of Rollo is Rognald Eysteinson's fifth wife, Ragnhild Hrolfsson, b. about 848 in Norway {I assume the second name should be Hrolfsdotr}.
2 CONT References: [RFC]
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT Rognhild* HROLFSDATTER (Countess) 0848 - 0892
2 CONT
2 CONT * TITLE: Countess
2 CONT * BIRTH: 0848, Norway
2 CONT * DEATH: 0892, Orkney,Orkney Islands,Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Hrolf* NEFJA
2 CONT '''Family:''' Ragnvald I* of More EYSTEINSSON – MARRIAGE: 0867, Maer,Nord Trondelag,Norway 
2 CONT 1.  Ivar RAGNVALDSSON
2 CONT 2.  Thori, Jarl of More Ragnvaldsson The SIL
2 CONT 3. +Rolf* RAGNVALDSSON
2 CONT 4. +Einar "Turf" ROGNVALDSSON 
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT Her son Rolf Ganger plundered much in the East sea. One summer, as he was coming from the eastward on a viking's expedition to the coast of Viken, he landed there and made a cattle foray. As King Harald, Rolf's father, happened to
2 CONC  be in Viken, he heard of it, and was in a great rage; for he had now forbid the plundering within the bounds of the country. The king assembled a Thing, and had Rolf declared an outlaw over all Norway.  When Ragnhild heard of it,
2 CONC  she hastened to the king, and entreated peace for Rolf; but the king was so enraged that here entreaty was of no avail. Then she spoke up:  "Do you think, King Harald, in your anger, To drive away my brave Rolf Ganger Like a mad 
2 CONC wolf, from out the land? Why is your cruelty so fell? Think twice, king, it's ill With such a wolf at wolf to play, Who, driven to the wild woods away May make the king's best deer his prey."
2 CONT
2 CONT [Heimskringla, or The Chronicle of the Kings of Norway, Harald Harfager's Saga].
2 CONT ——————————————————————————————
2 CONT Her son Rolf Ganger plundered much in the East sea. One summer, as he was coming from the eastward on a viking's expedition to the coast of Viken, he landed there and made a cattle foray. As King Harald, Rolf's father, happened to
2 CONC  be in Viken, he heard of it, and was in a great rage; for he had now forbid the plundering within the bounds of the country. The king assembled a Thing, and had Rolf declared an outlaw over all Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Ragnhild heard of it, she hastened to the king, and entreated peace for Rolf; but the king was so enraged that here entreaty was of no avail. Then she spoke up: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Do you think, King Harald, in your anger,
2 CONT >To drive away my brave Rolf Ganger
2 CONT >Like a mad wolf, from out the land?
2 CONT >Why is your cruelty so fell?
2 CONT >Think twice, king, it's ill
2 CONT >With such a wolf at wolf to play,
2 CONT >Who, driven to the wild woods away
2 CONT >May make the king's best deer his prey."
