1 OCCU Legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling, Rey en Jutland & Vestfold, King of Vestfold, King of Norway, Ruled 810-40
1 TITL King
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.friesian.com/germania.htm#orkney
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav Geirstadalv (Gudrødsson) (Ólaf Geirstaðaálf) ca ?-840, PAM
2 CONT
2 CONT (In English: Olaf Geirstad-Alf)
2 CONT
2 CONT King in part of Norway: Vestfold
2 CONT == Basics ==
2 CONT * Father: Gudrød the Hunter (Veidekonge)
2 CONT * Mother: Alvhild Alvarinsdotter
2 CONT * Wife: Unknown
2 CONT ** Son: Ragnvald Heidumhere
2 CONT
2 CONT No other children are documented in Ynglingesoga,
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT http://lind.no/nor/index.asp?lang=gb&emne=nor&person=Olav%20Geirstadalv%20%28Gudr%F8dsson%29
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olav_Geirstadalv_Gudr%C3%B8dsson
2 CONT
2 CONT == Geni disambiguation notes ==
2 CONT Harald Hårfagre's saga mentions a son of Harald who was also named Olaf Geirstad-Alf.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is another Olav son of Gudrød son of Halfdan, but sagas dealing with the Icelanders who came via Ireland claim that he's descended from a different Halfdan (the two Gudrøds are fairly well documented as uncle and nephew).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ynglingesaga does not say anything about the name of his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød died when Olaf was twenty years old and he and Halfdan divided their kingdom between them. Olaf took the southern part and resided in Geirstad. They only inherited Vestfold because Alfgeir took Vingulmark for himself and ma
2 CONC de his son Gandalf Alfgeirsson its king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga relates that Olaf was a skillful man and a great warrior. He was also handsome, big and strong. He was the father of Ragnvald the Mountain-High.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reigns of Olaf and Halfdan the Black, Värmland started to pay tribute to the Swedish king Erik Anundsson instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of illness. Tjodolf of Hvin sang about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Long while this branch of Odin's stem
2 CONT
2 CONT     Was the stout prop of Norway's realm;
2 CONT
2 CONT     Long while King Olaf with just pride
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ruled over Westfold far and wide.
2 CONT
2 CONT     At length by cruel gout oppressed,
2 CONT
2 CONT     The good King Olaf sank to rest:
2 CONT
2 CONT     His body now lies under ground,
2 CONT
2 CONT     Buried at Geirstad, in the mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, he was worshipped as an elf, and was called the Geirstad-alf (the "elf of Geirstad").
2 CONT
2 CONT A hypothesis identifies Geirstad with Gjerstad near Gokstad, and his burial with the Gokstad Ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød died when Olaf was twenty years old and he and Halfdan divided their kingdom between them. Olaf took the southern part and resided in Geirstad. They only inherited Vestfold because Alfgeir took Vingulmark for himself and ma
2 CONC de his son Gandalf Alfgeirsson its king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga relates that Olaf was a skillful man and a great warrior. He was also handsome, big and strong. He was the father of Ragnvald the Mountain-High.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reigns of Olaf and Halfdan the Black, Värmland started to pay tribute to the Swedish king Erik Anundsson instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of illness. Tjodolf of Hvin sang about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while this branch of Odin's stem 
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the stout prop of Norway's realm; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while King Olaf with just pride 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruled over Westfold far and wide. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At length by cruel gout oppressed, 
2 CONT
2 CONT The good King Olaf sank to rest: 
2 CONT
2 CONT His body now lies under ground, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at Geirstad, in the mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, he was worshipped as an elf, and was called the Geirstad-alf (the "elf of Geirstad").
2 CONT
2 CONT A hypothesis identifies Geirstad with Gjerstad near Gokstad, and his burial with the Gokstad Ship
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Jutland and Vestfold
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav «Geirstadalv» Gudrødsson var Halvdan Svartes 19 år eldre bror. De delte Vestfold mellom seg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ifølge Snorre hadde Olav gjort store bragder «i vest», noe som har skapt grunnlaget for hypotesen om at han er identisk med Kong Olav Kvite Gudrødsson, som i 861 grunnla Dublin sammen med Ivar Beinlaus Lodbroksson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ifølge Snorre var Olav meget populær hos sine folk, var høyvokst og da han døde «av fotaverk» ca. 50 år gammel kastet folkene hans opp haug over ham på Geirstad (idag Gjekstad ved Sandefjord). Da graven ble åpnet fant arkeologene 
2 CONC i Gokstadskipet en høyreist mann sittende på en stol. Leger fastslo at hans ene ben var sterkt angrepet av arthritis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Harald Grenskes dronning Åsa hadde vanskelig for å bli forløst. Hun fikk beskjed i en drøm av Kong Olav Geirstadalv om å sende en huskar til Geirstad, grave seg ned og ta sverdet «Bæsing» og hugge hodet av krigeren. Beltet hans sk
2 CONC ulle så legges over magen hennes og hun ville bli forløst. Dette ble gjort og gutten ble født. Han ble kalt Olav etter slektens «alv» i haugen og fikk senere sverdet Bæsing i «tanngave», Dette sverdet brukte han hele sitt voksne l
2 CONC iv og kastet det først fra seg i dødsøyeblikket på Stiklestad 29. juli 1030. Halvbroren Harald Sigurdsson reddet med seg sverdet og ga det senere til sin sjef i Konstantinopel, general Georgios Monomachus. Tilnavnet Geirstadalv fi
2 CONC kk kongen først etter sin død. Det skal ha medført lykke å avlegge gravhaugen besøk før viktige reiser skulle foretaes.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Vestfold and Jutland, Norway 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gokstad ship is a late 9th century Viking ship found in a ship burial beneath a burial mound at Gokstad farm in Sandar, Sandefjord, Vestfold, Norway. It was excavated in 1880 by Nicolay Nicolaysen.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gokstad ship at the Viking Ship Museum in Oslo, Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 The ship
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 The skeletal remains
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 The grave goods
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 See also
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 References
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 External links
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]The ship
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gokstad ship is clinker-built, constructed largely of oak. The ship is 24 m long and 5 m wide. It is the largest in the Viking Ship Museum in Oslo. The ship was built to carry 32 oarsmen, and the oar holes could be hatched dow
2 CONC n when the ship was under sail. It's utilized a square sail of c. 110 square meters, which, it is estimated, could propel the ship to over 12 knots. While the ship was traveling in shallow water, the rudder could be raised.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dendrochronological dating suggests that the ship was built of timber that was felled around 890 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ship's design has been demonstrated to be very seaworthy. A replica of the ship crossed the Atlantic from Bergen, Norway to be exhibited at the World's Columbian Exposition, Chicago, in 1893. Another replica, the Gaia, current
2 CONC ly has Sandefjord as its home port.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gokstad Viking ship excavation. Photographed in ~1880
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]The skeletal remains
2 CONT
2 CONT During the excavations, the skeleton of a male aged between 50-70 years was recovered. The skeleton was found in a bed inside a timber-built burial chamber. Although the identity of the person buried is unknown, it has been sugges
2 CONC ted that it is that of Olaf Geirstad-Alf, a petty king of Vestfold. He was of the House of Yngling, and died about this time, according to the Heimskringla.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]The grave goods
2 CONT
2 CONT The grave was furnished with grave goods. Apart from the ship itself, they consisted of three small boats, a tent, a sledge and riding equipment. It is believed that the mound was plundered in ancient times. The excavation in 1880
2 CONC  showed that valuables of gold and silver had been removed. In the Viking period, weapons were considered an important part of a man's grave goods. In the case of the Gokstad ship, any such weapons were probably taken by grave rob
2 CONC bers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gokstad Viking ship replica at the World's Columbian Exposition, Chicago 1893
2 CONT
2 CONT Currently, the ship, the reconstructed burial chamber, two of the small boats and two tent boards from the burial chamber are displayed in the Viking Ship Museum in Oslo. Some other artifacts that survived the plundering are also 
2 CONC on display in the museum.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød died when Olaf was twenty years old and he and Halfdan divided their kingdom between them. Olaf took the southern part and resided in Geirstad. They only inherited Vestfold because Alfgeir took Vingulmark for himself and ma
2 CONC de his son Gandalf Alfgeirsson its king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga relates that Olaf was a skillful man and a great warrior. He was also handsome, big and strong. He was the father of Ragnvald the Mountain-High.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reigns of Olaf and Halfdan the Black, Värmland started to pay tribute to the Swedish king Erik Anundsson instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of illness. Tjodolf of Hvin sang about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while this branch of Odin's stem 
2 CONT
2 CONT Was the stout prop of Norway's realm; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while King Olaf with just pride 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruled over Westfold far and wide. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At length by cruel gout oppressed, 
2 CONT
2 CONT The good King Olaf sank to rest: 
2 CONT
2 CONT His body now lies under ground, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried at Geirstad, in the mound. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, he was worshipped as an elf, and was called the Geirstad-alf (the "elf of Geirstad").
2 CONT
2 CONT A hypothesis identifies Geirstad with Gjerstad near Gokstad, and his burial with the Gokstad Ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød died when Olaf was twenty years old and he and Halfdan divided their kingdom between them. Olaf took the southern part and resided in Geirstad. They only inherited Vestfold because Alfgeir took Vingulmark for himself and ma
2 CONC de his son Gandalf Alfgeirsson its king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga relates that Olaf was a skillful man and a great warrior. He was also handsome, big and strong. He was the father of Ragnvald the Mountain-High.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reigns of Olaf and Halfdan the Black, Värmland started to pay tribute to the Swedish king Erik Anundsson instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of illness. Tjodolf of Hvin sang about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Long while this branch of Odin's stem
2 CONT     Was the stout prop of Norway's realm;
2 CONT     Long while King Olaf with just pride
2 CONT     Ruled over Westfold far and wide.
2 CONT     At length by cruel gout oppressed,
2 CONT     The good King Olaf sank to rest:
2 CONT     His body now lies under ground,
2 CONT     Buried at Geirstad, in the mound.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, he was worshipped as an elf, and was called the Geirstad-alf (the "elf of Geirstad").
2 CONT
2 CONT A hypothesis identifies Geirstad with Gjerstad near Gokstad, and his burial with the Gokstad Ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Olaf Gudrødsson, or as he was named after his death Olaf Geirstad-Alf, was a legendary Norwegian king of the House of Yngling from the Ynglinga saga. He was the son of Gudrød the Hunter and the brother of Halfdan the Black. Gudrød
2 CONC  and Olaf conquered a large part of Raumarike.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudrød died when Olaf was twenty years old and he and Halfdan divided their kingdom between them. Olaf took the southern part and resided in Geirstad. They only inherited Vestfold because Alfgeir took Vingulmark for himself and ma
2 CONC de his son Gandalf Alfgeirsson its king.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ynglinga saga relates that Olaf was a skillful man and a great warrior. He was also handsome, big and strong. He was the father of Ragnvald the Mountain-High.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the reigns of Olaf and Halfdan the Black, Värmland started to pay tribute to the Swedish king Erik Anundsson instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of illness. Tjodolf of Hvin sang about him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Long while this branch of Odin's stem  Was the stout prop of Norway's realm;  Long while King Olaf with just pride  Ruled over Westfold far and wide.  At length by cruel gout oppressed,  The good King Olaf sank to rest:  His body 
2 CONC now lies under ground,  Buried at Geirstad, in the mound.  After his death, he was worshipped as an elf, and was called the Geirstad-alf (the "elf of Geirstad").
2 CONT
2 CONT A hypothesis identifies Geirstad with Gjerstad near Gokstad, and his burial with the Gokstad Ship.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT It is Olaf's ship that is said to have been found at Gokstad and is now in the Oslo Museum.
2 CONT
2 CONT This man's wife, Tora, was a daughter of Sigurd Orm-i-Øye "d.y." Ragnarsson of Denmark.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT With his death, Vestfold passed to his 1/2 brother Halfdan theBlack.
2 CONT
2 CONT Allied with his 1/2 brother Ragnar Lodbrock.
2 CONT
2 CONT With Ragnar, contemplated invasion of the Franks.
2 CONT
2 CONT His death altered the balance of power as Halfdan did not support imperialaim. 1.Title: Fighting Kings of Wessex Author: G.P. Baker Publication: Combined Books, Conshohocken, PA 1996 Page: p 107 Text: d bef Ragnar Lothbrock's raid
2 CONC s in Ireland, 831. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Härskade på Vestfold
2 CONT
2 CONT Олаф Гудрёдссон (др.-сканд. Olaf Gudrødsson) или как он стал известен после смерти Олаф Гейрстад-Альф (др.-сканд. Olaf Geirstad-Alf) — полулегендарный норвежский конунг династии Инглингов, упомянутый в «Саге об Инглингах». Сын Гуд
2 CONC рёда Охотника, единокровный брат Хальвдана Чёрного, отец Рёгнвальда Достославного. Вместе со своим отцом, Олаф завоевал значительную часть Раумарики. Гудрёд умер, когда Олафу было около двадцати лет. Он унаследовал Вестфольд, а ко
2 CONC гда его брат Хальвдан Чёрный возмужал, то разделил с ним королевство. Олаф взял южную часть и стал править в Гейрстаде. Братья унаследовали только Вестфольд, так как Вингулмарк забрал себе Альвгейр, посадив там правителем своего с
2 CONC ына Гандальва Альвгейрссона. Согласно «Саге об Инглингах», Олаф был могущественным и воинственным человеком, с виду красивым и высоким. Олаф умер в возрасте примерно 50 лет от болезни. После смерти его стали почитать альвом, назыв
2 CONC ая его Гейрстад-Альвом, то есть «альвом из Гейрстада». Согласно одной из теорий, Гейрстад (Гьерстад) находится недалеко от Гокстада. Могилу Олафа связывают с Гокстадским захоронением, где археологи нашли высокого человека сидящего
2 CONC  на стуле, а врачи установили, что ноги этого человека были поражены артритом. Олаф упомянут в поэме Перечень Инглингов, написанной по заказу его сына Рёгнвальда скальдом Тьодольвом из Хвинира. См. также: Инглинги Перечень Инглинг
2 CONC ов Круг Земной Предшественник: Гудрёд Охотник Конунги Вестфольда вместе с Хальвданом Чёрным нач. 820-х — сер. IX века Преемник: Рёгнвальд Достославный. 
