2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: King Olaf Trygvason's Saga:
2 CONT
2 CONT "19. EARL HAKON'S MARRIAGE.
2 CONT Earl Hakon married a girl called Thora, a daughter of the powerful Skage Skoptason, and very beautiful she was. They had two sons, Svein and Heming, and a daughter called Bergljot who was afterwards married to Einar Tambaskielfer.
2 CONC  ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT From Snorre Sturlasson: Saga of Harald Hardråde:
2 CONT
2 CONT "41. OF EINAR TAMBASKELFER.
2 CONT Einar Tambaskelfer was the most powerful lenderman in the Throndhjem land. There was but little friendship between him and King Harald, although Einar retained all the fiefs he had held while Magnus the Good lived. Einar had many 
2 CONC large estates, and was married to Bergliot, a daughter of Earl Hakon, as related above. Their son Eindride was grown up, and married to Sigrid, a daughter of Ketil Kalf and Gunhild, King Harald's sister's daughter. Eindride had in
2 CONC herited the beauty of his mother's father, Earl Hakon, and his sons; and in size and strength he took after his father, Einar, and also in all bodily perfections by which Einar had been distinguished above other men. He was, also,
2 CONC  as well as his father, the most popular of men, which the sagas, indeed, show sufficiently."
