2 CONT
2 CONT Louis "Le Frizon" was a Bâtard de Flandres; his presence acts as a Political Anchor for the Halluin family. If he is missing, the leap Jan II made from "local lord" to "husband of a royal widow" looks like a mistake rather than a 
2 CONC strategic conquest.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Louis dit "Le Frizon" (of Flanders); Chevalier (Knight), Seigneur de Praet et de La Woestine'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''I. THE LEGAL IDENTITY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Land: Praet (near Bruges) and La Woestine (near Woesten/Aalter).
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles: Chevalier (Knight), Seigneur de Praet et de La Woestine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jurisdiction: The Franc of Bruges and the Central Comital Court of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alliances: House of Flanders (Illegitimate Branch); House of Ghistelles (via Maria).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''II. THE STRATEGIC FOOTPRINT'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates Flourished: c. 1360–1396 (Died at Nicopolis).
2 CONT
2 CONT Role: Comital Proxy and Military Commander.
2 CONT
2 CONT Strategic Position: Louis was a "High-Status Satellite" of the House of Flanders. As an illegitimate son of Count Louis de Male, he was granted the prestigious lordship of Praet. His existence provided the Ghistelles family (and s
2 CONC ubsequently the Halluins) with a direct, though unofficial, blood link to the sovereign Counts. His death in the East left a "Power Vacuum" and a "Prestige Widow" (Maria) that Jan II van Halewijn was able to expertly claim.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''III. SUMMARY RESEARCH NOTE: THE NICOPOLIS ANCHOR'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis is the Chronological Hard-Stop for this generation. He died at the Battle of Nicopolis in September 1396. This event is a fixed historical fact. By locking Louis to 1396, we create an impassable wall: Jan II cannot have marr
2 CONC ied Maria before late 1396/1397. This successfully Exorcises any traditional pedigree that tries to place Jan II’s children in the 1380s.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''IV. BIOGRAPHICAL SUMMARY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis, nicknamed "Le Frizon" (The Friesian), was a natural son of Louis de Male, Count of Flanders. Despite his illegitimate birth, he was raised within the highest echelons of the Flemish court and was endowed with the Lordship o
2 CONC f Praet, a significant fief near Bruges. He married Maria van Ghistelles, further consolidating the bond between the Count's family and the powerful Ghistelles lineage. In 1396, Louis joined the "Crusade of Nicopolis" led by John 
2 CONC the Fearless. The campaign ended in a catastrophic defeat at the hands of the Ottoman Empire; Louis was among the high-ranking Flemish knights who fell on the battlefield. His death transformed his widow, Maria, into one of the mo
2 CONC st eligible and strategically important figures in the Flemish marriage market.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''V. DOCUMENTATION AND EVIDENCE'''
2 CONT * Comital Charters: Records of Louis de Male granting the Lordship of Praet to "Louis, our son."
2 CONT * Military Chronicles: Listed among the fallen knights at the Battle of Nicopolis (1396) in contemporary Burgundian accounts
2 CONT * Marriage Record: Documented as the first husband of Maria van Ghistelles (daughter of Roger of Straeten).
2 CONT * Secondary Authority: Père Anselme and Racines et Histoire, confirming his status as a "Bâtard de Flandres."
2 CONT * The Grant of the Seigneury of Praet: The primary document for Louis is the charter issued by his father, Count Louis de Male.
2 CONT * The Nicopolis Rolls (The 1396 Death Anchor): The military registries and chronicles of the Battle of Nicopolis are the most important chronological evidence.
2 CONT * Maria’s Dower Records: After 1396, Maria van Ghistelles would have appeared in documents as the "Widow of the late Louis of Flanders."
2 CONT
2 CONT '''VI. HERALDRY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms: Or, a lion rampant sable, armed and langued gules (Flanders), debruised by a bendlet gules (or a similar mark of bastardy).
2 CONT
2 CONT Status: Comital Bastardy arms. These arms signaled his royal blood while clearly marking his exclusion from the sovereign succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. METHODOLOGICAL COMPLIANCE
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is a Class 1 Identity Lock. By including Louis "Le Frizon," we provide the necessary context for the "Social Upgrade" of the Halluin family. His 1396 death date serves as the Chronological Anchor that prevents the Cla
2 CONC ss 3 Chronological Fold in the Jan I / Jan II generations. This profile is protected against being overwritten as it serves as a foundational "Proof of Widowhood" for Maria van Ghistelles.
2 CONT
2 CONT VIII. DISCLAIMER
2 CONT
2 CONT <span style="color:red; font-weight:bold;">This summary is generated with AI assistance to serve as a research lead for the House of Halluin. This profile is built upon a High-Fidelity Evidence Model. All connections to the House 
2 CONC of Flanders and the Nicopolis campaign are based on documented historical records. Traditional "Ancien Régime" pedigrees that fail to account for the gap between Louis's death and Jan II's marriage have been Exorcised to correct c
2 CONC hronological anomalies. If primary evidence (Charters/Cartularies) contradicts the current placement, the "Unknown" placeholder will be reinstated per Curator’s Logic Step 6.</span>
2 CONT
