2 CONC ers “en avancement de son mariage avec Dame Marie de Guistelles, Dame de Zweueghem et de Rosebeke” granted “les terres et Baronies de Praet et de la Woestine” to his illegitimate son “Messire Louys de Flandres dit le Frizon” (no s
2 CONC ource cited)[865].  Vredius quotes a manuscript which records that Louis “eut en partage [la Wostine] par acte du 25 de septembre 1373” [date not confirmed] and died at Nikopolis 28 Sep 1396[866]. 
2 CONT m as her first husband, MARIE [Isabelle?] van Gistel Vrouw van Zwevegem, daughter of ROGER van Gistel Heer van Straeten & his wife Elisabeth [Margareta] Vrouw van Dudzele (-after 1431).  Père Anselme records her parentage (naming 
2 CONC her “Marie”) and two marriages (reversing their order) (no sources cited)[867].  As noted above under her husband, Espinoy names her “Dame Marie de Guistelles, Dame de Zweueghem et de Rosebeke”.  Vredius quotes a manuscript which 
2 CONC records that “messire Loys de Frise fils bastard de...Loys de Male conte de Flandre...” married “madame...de Ghistelles...fille de messire --- Seigneur de Dudzeele” who later married “--- de Halewijn”[868].  Vredius quotes another
2 CONC  manuscript which records that Louis married “dame Marie de Guistelles fille de messire Rogier chevalier seign. de Dudzeele, Straten et de Dame Isabeau heretiere de Dudzeele”[869].  Her family origin is confirmed by the arms displ
2 CONC ayed on the epitaph of her granddaughter (by her second marriage) Isabelle.  Some doubt about Marie’s name is introduced by the charter dated 25 Apr 1435 which names “Pierre de Boulers escuier”, married to “Margaretha van Halewijn
2 CONC , de oudste dochter van Jan van Halewijn en Isabella van Gistel”[870].  No “Jean d’Halluin” married to “Isabella van Gistel” has been found.  If Marguerite’s father was Jean d’Halluin Seigneur de Roosebeke (the second husband of “
2 CONC Marie”, see below), maybe his wife was named “Isabelle” not “Marie” (that name being recorded only in secondary sources as noted above).  An indication that this suggestion about Marguerite’s parentage is correct is that “Marie va
2 CONC n Gistel”’s son by her first husband married “Johanna van Reigaarsvliet” (see below), presumably a relative of Marguerite’s husband although the precise family relationship has not been established (see the document FLANDERS NOBIL
2 CONC ITY), as multiple marriages between different members of two noble families are often noted.  '''She married secondly Jean d’Halluin Seigneur de Roosebeke, Burggraaf van Harelbeke.'''  Espinoy records that “messire Jean de Flandre
2 CONC ...avec...sa mere Dame de Zweueghem et de Roosebeke” settled the succession of “messire Louys son pere en son vivant Seigneur de Praet et de la Woestine” and settled her dower, recorded in a document dated 1431[871].  This documen
2 CONC t does not name “Marie/Isabelle” but it does provide another indication that she was the mother of Marguerite d’Halluin : her second husband died before 1431, indicating the need to settle her dower. 
2 CONT Louis & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT 1.         JEAN [I] de Flandre (-after 10 Sep 1439).  Heer van Praet en van der Woestijne.  Espinoy records that “messire Jean de Flandre...avec...sa mere Dame de Zweueghem et de Roosebeke” settled the succession of “messire Louys
2 CONC  son pere en son vivant Seigneur de Praet et de la Woestine” and settled her dower (no date), recorded in a document dated 1431[872].  “Ian van Vlaenderen Heere van Praet ande vander Woestine ende Burghemeesters ende Schepenen van
2 CONC den selven Heerschepe van Praet” issued a charter dated 10 Sep 1439[873].  m JOHANNA van Reigaarsvliet, daughter of HENDRIK van Reigaarsvliet & his wife --- van Schendelbeek.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage[874]. 
2 CONC  Vredius quotes a manuscript which records that “Iean de Flandre Seign. de Praet et de la Woestine” married “Ieanne de Reyghersvliet fille de Henry, fils de Gautier”[875].  No primary source has been found which confirms her paren
2 CONC tage and marriage, or her date of death.  Jean & his wife had five children: 
2 CONT a)         LOUIS [II] de Flandre (-24 Aug 1488, bur Aeltere).  Heer van Praet.  An epitaph at Aeltere records the burial of “Lodewyc van Vlaenderen heere van Praet ende vanden lande van de Wostine, van Bevere ende van Onnelé, fs m
2 CONC er Jans ruddere heere van Praet” who died 1488 “op Ste Bartholomeus dach” and who married “vrau Loije van Brugghe fs mijns heeren Jans hjeere van Gruuthuuse”[876].  m LOUISE de Bruges, daughter of JAN [IV] van de Aa dit de Bruges 
2 CONC Heer van Gruuthuse en Grimbergen & his wife Maria van Steenhuize.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage[877].  An epitaph at Aeltere records that “Lodewyc van Vlaenderen heere van Praet...” married “vrau Loije van Brugg
2 CONC he fs mijns heeren Jans hjeere van Gruuthuuse”[878].  Louis [II] & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT i)          LOUIS [III] de Flandre (-1 Jan 1490, bur Aeltere).  His parentage is confirmed by his epitaph, cited below.  Heer van Praet. 
2 CONT -        see below. 
2 CONT ii)         JEAN de Flandre (-6 Sep 1523, bur Beveren near Roeselare).  Heer van Onlede en Beveren.  Grand bailly de Bruges.  An epitaph at Beveren bij Roeselare records the burial of “Jan de Flandres escuier sr de Onelé et de Bev
2 CONC ere, en son temps baillij de la ville de Bruges et du terroir du Franc, ds messire Loijs de Flandres chlr sr de Praet et du paijs de la Wostijne” who died 6 Sep 1523 and “dame Margrite Bolengier” who died 24 Feb 1526 (O.S.?)[879].
2 CONC   m MARGUERITE Boulengier, daughter of --- (-24 Feb [1526/27], bur Beveren near Roeselare).  An epitaph at Beveren bij Roeselare records the burial of “Jan de Flandres escuier sr de Onelé et de Bevere...” and “dame Margrite Boleng
2 CONC ier” who died 24 Feb 1526 (O.S.?)[880]. 
2 CONT iii)        JOSSE de Flandre (-after 1526).  Buylaert records that, after the death in 1523 of Jean de Flandre Heer van Onlede, “zijn broer Josse” inherited “de heerlijkheden Onlede, Beveren en Wijchuize”[881].  m MARTINA van Moer
2 CONC kerke, daughter of ---.  Buylaert records her family origin and marriage, noting that the couple has “verschillende kinderen” and that the family survived until 1592[882]. 
2 CONT b)         JEANNE de Flandre (-after 1446).  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage[883].  A document dated 24 Jan 1441 (N.S.) records a dispute about the marriage contract between “wijlen joncheere Jan van Pouke” and “Je
2 CONC anne van Vlaanderen, dochter van de heer van Praat”[884].  A document dated 1446 records that “Jeanne de Flandre” married “Jean seigneur de Poucques, Vicomte d’Ipre, Seigneur de Thomme et de Winghene, Weldens, fils d’Eulard et de 
2 CONC dame Anastasie d’Oultre, Dame de Weldene, Vicomtesse heritiere d’Ipre” and left two children[885].  m JAN van Poeke Châtelain d’Ypres Seigneur de Thomme, de Winghene et de Wildins, son of EULAARD Heer van Poeke & his wife Anastasi
2 CONC e d’Oultre Dame de Wildins, Châtelaine d’Ypres (-before 24 Jan 1441). 
2 CONT c)         MARGUERITE de Flandre .  Manuscripts cited by Vredius record that “Marguerite de Flandre” married “Louis de Bailleul Seigneur de Donlieu, Marescal heritier de Flandres”[886].  m LOUIS de Bailleul Seigneur de Donlieu, so
2 CONC n of ---.  Maréchal héréditaire de Flandre. 
2 CONT d)         ISABELLE de Flandre .  A manuscript cited by Vredius records that “Isabeau de Flandre” married “Waleran Seigneur de Landas et de Warlain, fils de Messire Mathieu”[887].  m WALERAN de Landas Seigneur de Landas et de Warl
2 CONC ain, son of MATTHIEU de Landas & his wife ---. 
2 CONT e)         LANDRADE de Flandre .  A manuscript cited by Vredius records “Landrade de Flandre, Chanoinesse à S. Wauldrut à Mons en Haynault” who never married[888].  Canoness at Mons Sainte-Waudru.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''' Cawley, Charles. “FLANDERS, COUNTS; Chapter 3. COUNTS of FLANDERS (DAMPIERRE); B. HEEREN van PRAET.” Fmg.ac, 7 Jan. 2025, fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLANDERS. Accessed 12 Apr. 2026.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT A: Dates Flourished:	c. 1360–1396 (Died at Nicopolis).
2 CONT B: Status::	Comital Proxy and Military Commander.
2 CONT C: Strategic Role::	Louis was a "High-Status Satellite" of the House of Flanders. As an illegitimate son of Count Louis de Male, he was granted the prestigious lordship of Praet.
2 CONT His existence provided the Ghistelles family (and subsequently the Halluins) with a direct, though unofficial, blood link to the sovereign Counts. His death in the East left a "Power Vacuum" and a "Prestige Widow" (Maria) that Jan
2 CONC  II van Halewijn was able
2 CONT ----
