1 NAME Yolanda /de Barbançon/ dame de Montigny-Saint-Christophe et de Hantes
2 GIVN Yolanda
2 SURN de Barbançon
2 NSFX dame de Montigny-Saint-Christophe et de Hantes
2 NICK Yoline
2 NICK Jolenta
2 NICK Yolenta
2 NICK Yolande
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Lallaing
3 STAE Nord-Pas-de-Calais-Picardie
3 CTRY France
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1370
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 JAN 1434
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT Ou Jeanne. Dame de Montigny St Christophe (Montignies).
2 CONT Available Sources :J de Saint Genois, 1806, E De Seyn, 1948, L de Herckenrode, 1868, F Brassart, 1879, FV Goethals, 1862, C Butkens, 1726, A Boterdaele, 1912, de Herckenrode, 1844, FV Goethals, 1849.
2 CONT M Pastoureau et M Popoff, 2001, L Dumont, 1776, P Le Doulx, 1800, C Sars de Solmont, 1846.
2 CONT Death: FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. ~1395 Yolande (Yolente, Yoline) de Barbençon, dame de Montigny-Saint-Christophe + 09/01/1434 (fille cadette de Jean, chevalier, seigneur de Barbençon, La Buissière et Merbe, Pair de Hainaut, et de Yolande de Gavre, dite «de Le
2 CONC ns» ou «de Masmines»)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''YOLANDE de Barbançon''' (-9 Jan 1434, bur Lalaing).  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by a memorial in the chapelle du Saint-Sang-Wisnacq, aux Carmes de Valenciennes, which records the arms of her son Guillaume de Lalai
2 CONC ng (died 1475) quartered “Lalaing/Montegny/Barbanchon/Rassenghien”[1820].  She must have married after Oct 1387 as she is not named in the charter which names her supposed two brothers-in-law.  Dame de Hantes.  An epitaph at Lalai
2 CONC ng records the burial of “Otte de Lalaing chevalier...vesquit le dit Otte...cent et trois ans” who died 13 Jan 1441 and “Yolens de Barbenchon dame de Lalaing son...epeuse” who died 9 Jan 1434[1821].  “Charles baron de Lalaing...” 
2 CONC ratified obits at the church of Lalaing, including “Monseigneur Hoste signeur de Lalaing...et...Madame Yolent de Barbenchon son espeuse lesquelz gisent en la chappelle de saint Jehan”, by charter dated 15 Dec 1515[1822]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  m (after Oct 1387) OSTE Seigneur de Lalaing, son of NICOLAS [III] Seigneur de Lalaing & his wife Isabelle de Montigny ([before 1350]-13 Jan 1441, bur Lalaing). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Cawley, Charles. “HAINAUT.” Medieval Lands, Foundation for Medieval Genealogy, 24 Mar. 2022, https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/HAINAUT.htm''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT Mother…
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Johanna-de-Gavre-d-Escournaix/6000000014113456671?through=6000000185362767827 JEANNE de Gavre] (-29 May 1478, bur Deize).  Dame d’Escornaix, de Bracle et de Salardinghe.  Brassart records her parentage
2 CONC  and marriage without citing the sources on which the information is based[581].  An epitaph at Deinze, near Gent records the burial of “Simon de Lalaing chevalier seigneur de Montigny et de Santes fondateur de cette église et Jea
2 CONC nne d’Escornaix dame de Bracle et Salardinghe sa femme”, providing brief biographical details, who died 15 Mar 1476 and 29 May 1478 respectively[582].  '''m ([1436]) [https://www.geni.com/people/Simon-X-de-Lalaing-seigneur-de-Mont
2 CONC igny/6000000014109270790?through=6000000014113456671 SIMON de Lalaing Seigneur de Montigny], son of [https://www.geni.com/people/Othon-II-seigneur-de-Lalaing/6000000014109288443?through=6000000014109270790 OSTE de Lalaing] & his w
2 CONC ife [https://www.geni.com/people/Yolande-de-Barban%C3%A7on/6000000014128720111?through=6000000014109270790 Yolande de Barbançon Dame de Hantes] (-15 Mar 1477, bur Deinze).'''https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/FLEMISH%20NOBILITY.htm#
