3 CTRY Belgium
1 OCCU Sir Paen de Roët; Payne de Roet, Sir Knight Guienne King of Arms (1310 - 1351)"Payne Roet /de Guyenne/", Knight, Knight Guienne King of Arms, Sir Knight Guienne, Herald
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =====NOTE: Paon de Roet's parentage of Katherine Swynford (de Roet) is inferred from Paon's epitaph (in the crypt of St Paul's Cathedral, London): ''Hic jacet Paganus Roet, Miles, Guyenne Rex Armorum, Pater Catheri
2 CONC ne Ducise Lancastriae''. This parentage is generally accepted.=====
2 CONT .
2 CONT
2 CONT This person and their pedigree are currently documented from "The Royal Lineage of Our Noble and Gentle Families together with Their Paternal Ancestry" Compiled by Joseph Foster, 1885
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: http://www.archive.org/details/royallineageofou02fost ]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "a flemish herald from Hainault who was knighted just before his battlefield death"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katherine_Swynford
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT King at Arms suggests he owned estates. Native of Hainault. He & his family permanently settled in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thevalleyfamily.org/getperson.php?personID=I5658485768&tree=fitzvalley
2 CONT
2 CONT A Knight In Queen Philippa's (Edward Iii) Household
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "Paon" is also seen in early records as "Payne", "Payen", "Paonnet", and "Paganus". The surname is seen as "De Rodio", "Roelt", ""Roit", "Rouet", "Ruet", and "De Roeulx". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Paon de Roet was a herald and Knight who was involved in the early stages of the Hundred Years War, and who later became attached to the court of King Edward III of England. He became an ancestor of the monarchs of England by way 
2 CONC of his daughter Katherine's marriage to John of Gaunt. Another of Paon de Roet's daughters married English poet Geoffrey Chaucer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The tomb of Sir Paon de Roet was described by English poet John Weever as "once a fair marble stone inlaid all over with brass, nothing but the heads of a few brazen nails are at this day. Is idle, previously engraved with the rep
2 CONC resentation and Coat of Arms of the party defunct, thus much of a mangled funeral inscription wa of late times perspicious to be read." The inscription on the tomb: "hic Jacet Pagnanus Roet Miles Guyenne Rex Armorum Pater Catherin
2 CONC e Ducisse Lancastrie" which, translated is: "Here lies Paon de Roet, knight, Guyenne Kng of Arms, father of Katherine Duchess of Lancaster." 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Use this information only as clues to do further research, as there is much conflicting information regarding this person on the internet. Much of it appears to have been repeated from one site to the next, without original 
2 CONC source documentation. I also do.  Not have original source documentation. My interest is that this gentleman may be my 18th great grandfather. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paon_de_Roet
2 CONT
2 CONT Paon de Roet (c.1310-1380), also referred to as Sir Gilles de Roet, was a herald and knight from Hainaut who was involved in the early stages of the Hundred Years War. He became attached to the court of King Edward III of England 
2 CONC through the king's marriage to Philippa of Hainaut.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is most notable for the fact that he became the ancestor of the monarchs of England because his daughter Katherine married John of Gaunt. Her children, given the surname "Beaufort", became the forebears of the Tudor dynasty thr
2 CONC ough Margaret Beaufort. Another of his daughters also made a notable marriage, to the poet Geoffrey Chaucer.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=121410570
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paon_de_Roet _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p122.htm#i3667 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Payn Roet, Heer van Roet1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9 Last Edited	24 Mar 2014 M, #3667, b. circa 1305, d. 1380 Father	Payen van Roet, Heer van Roet9 b. c 1275, d. 1322 Charts	Pedigree of James Irvine
2 CONT      Sir Payn Roet, Heer van Roet Said to have married a Picardy farmgirl. He was born circa 1305 at of Henegouwen, Wallonia, Belgium.9 He married Catherine d' Avesnes, daughter of Guillaume III 'the Good', Count of Holland, Zeela
2 CONC nd, and Hainault, Lord of Friesland and Jeanne de Valois, circa 1339.9 Sir Payn Roet, Heer van Roet died in 1380 at Ghent, Flanders, Belgium.9 Family 1 Child	 Phillipa Roet+6 Family 2 Catherine d' Avesnes b. c 1320, d. 1380 Child	
2 CONC  Katherine Roet+10,11,1,2,3,4,5,7,8 b. 25 Nov 1340, d. 10 May 1403 Citations [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 246-247. [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, 
2 CONC p. 38-39. [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 114-115. [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. IV, p. 313. [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 389-390
2 CONC . [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. III, p. 73. [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. IV, p. 232. [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. V, p. 339-340. [S11640] Www.genealogieonline.nl. [S5] Douglas Rich
