0 @N6000000003796269439@ NOTE The Yngling Saga of Heimskingla
1 CONT The Saga of the Norse Kings by Snorri Sturleson
1 CONT (dates may be off):
1 CONT
1 CONT 4. VINLANDE or VINLANDI- a Swedish king who married Driva, daughter of Snow the Old from Finland, where he spent one winter. Vinlande left Finland in the spring, promising to return within three years. When he had not returned aft
1 CONC er ten years, Driva sent the son she had by Vinlande to his father in Sweden and sought: the help of a witch to either kill Vinlande or force him ro rerurn ro Finland. During a nightmare, Vinlande was trampled to death by "Mara" (
1 CONC the nightmare or female ghost). Their son was:
1 CONT
1 CONT 5. VISBUR
0 @N6000000009304938885@ NOTE #Générale##Générale#s:Bauche ; s:Heartland
0 @N6000000004533239809@ NOTE From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT (Redirected from Brynhild)
1 CONT In Norse mythology, Brünnehilde was a shieldmaiden and a Valkyrie. Inthe southern version of the Nibelungenlied legend, she was ordered todecide a fight in favor of the older of two kings. The valkyrie knewthat Odin himself prefer
1 CONC red the young king, Sigmund, yet Friggademanded his death for fathering a son by his own twin sister,Siglind. Brünnehilde decided the battle for Sigmund and saves hisyoung wife, who was pregnant with a son. For this Odin condemned
1 CONC  thevalkyrie to live the life of a mortal woman and cursed her to sleepuntil any man would rescue and marry her. Brünnehilde begged Odin tochange this, reminding him that she had only done what the god hadsecretly wanted, and she 
1 CONC convinced him to allow only the best hero torescue her. Accordingly, Brünnehilde was imprisoned in a ring of firethe only the greatest hero could enter. Sigurd, the son of Sigmund,entered that ring after killing the dragon Fafnir 
1 CONC and awokeBrünnehilde. Sigurd gave her his ring, Andvarinaut, unaware that itwas cursed and she pledges herself to him, despite her propheciesregarding his doom and his marriage to another.
1 CONT
1 CONT Siegfried duly betrayed her and married Gudrun when bewitched by thesorceress Grimhild to forget Brünnehilde. Gudrun's brother, Gunnar,then sought to court Brünnehilde but was stopped by the ring of firethat still surrounded her. 
1 CONC Sigurd exchanged shapes with him andentered the ring of fire a second time. Gunnar and Brünnehildemarried, but she plotted revenge for the deception and betrayal shehad suffered. Her brother-in-law Guttorm killed Sigurd, Brünnehil
1 CONC deherself killed Sigurd's three-year-old son, and then she willedherself to die.
1 CONT
1 CONT According to other sagas, Brünnehilde bore Sigurd a daughter, Aslaug,who later married Ragnar Lodbrok.
1 CONT
1 CONT The role of Brünnehilde in the Nibelungenlied appears to have beeninfluenced by Brunhilda, the historical queen of Austrasia. Thehistory of Brunhilda and her husband Sigebert I includes fratricide, along battle between brothers, a
1 CONC nd dealings with the Huns.
0 @N6000000003220317754@ NOTE {geni:comment} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brynhildr
