0 @N6000000003949721691@ NOTE Gudrod, "the Magnificent", also called "the Hunting-King", son of Halfdan "White-Leg" and Asa (Moriarty) (Sturleson says great grandson of Halfdan "White-leg"), King of Vermaland, Vestfold and Vingulmark, murdered 810-827 at insti
1 CONC gation of (2) wife Asa in revenge for forcibly abducting her and killing c 800 her father and brother; m. (1) Alfhilde, daughter of Alfrim, ruler of Vingulmark; m. (2) Asa, daughter of Harald "Red-Beard", King of Agdir. Asa is bel
1 CONC ieved buried in the Oseberg ship, the richest Scandinavian archeological find. [Ancestral Roots]   Note: My line agrees with Sturleson (Gudrod is great grandson of Halfdan) and not Moriarty (where Gudrod is son of Halfdan).
1 CONT Following Information copied from Wayne Iverson, World Connect db=wiversrm, rootsweb.com
1 CONT Also recorded as Godefrid, the sixth king of Haithabu, murdered in 810.
1 CONT He made war on King Harald Redbeard Herbrandsson and killed Harald and his son Gyrd and took a great booty and Harald's daughter, Asa, who he married. A year after the birth of son Halfdan, Gudrod was anchored in Stiflu Sound wher
1 CONC e a great banquet was given for him and he became very drunk. Upon going on land at the pier, a man leapt at him and speared him through, killing him. The killer was immediately slain and in the morning they found it was Queen Asa
1 CONC 's page. Son Olaf succeeded his father and later he and Halfdan, Asa's son, divided the kingdom.
