0 @N6000000003796269383@ NOTE The Yngling Saga of Heimskingla
1 CONT The Saga of the Norse Kings by Snorri Sturleson
1 CONT (dates may be off):
1 CONT
1 CONT 6. DOMALDE - A Swedish King who died in 130 A.D. During his reign, Sweden was ravaged by famine. No amount of sacrifice would appease the gods, so at last it was decided Co offer the King as a human sacrifice. This was done and th
1 CONC e country then had good crops and people lived in peace. His son was:
1 CONT
1 CONT 7. DOMAR  
0 @N6000000002187696056@ NOTE Domalde
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Domalde was a Swedish king of the House of Ynglings, in Norse mythology. He was the son of Visbur.
1 CONT
1 CONT Snorri Sturluson relats that Domalde's rule was marked by bad crops and starvation. The first autumn, the Swedes sacrificed oxen at the temple at Uppsala, but the next harvest was not better. The second autumn, they sacrificed men
1 CONC , but the following crops were even worse.
1 CONT
1 CONT The third year many Swedes arrived at Gamla Uppsala, and the chiefs decided they had to sacrifice the king. They sprinkled the statues of the gods with his blood (see Blót) and the good harvests returned.
1 CONT
1 CONT Snorri included a piece from Ynglingatal composed in the 9th century:
1 CONT
1 CONT     Hitt var fyrr
1 CONT     at fold ruðu
1 CONT     sverðberendr
1 CONT     sínum drótni,
1 CONT     ok landherr
1 CONT     af lífs vönum
1 CONT     dreyrug vápn
1 CONT     Dómalda bar,
1 CONT     þá er árgjörn
1 CONT     Jóta dolgi
1 CONT     Svía kind
1 CONT     of sóa skyldi.[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     It has happened oft ere now,
1 CONT     That foeman's weapon has laid low
1 CONT     The crowned head, where battle plain,
1 CONT     Was miry red with the blood-rain.
1 CONT     But Domald dies by bloody arms,
1 CONT     Raised not by foes in war's alarms
1 CONT     Raised by his Swedish liegemen's hand,
1 CONT     To bring good seasons to the land.(Laing's translation [2])
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Visbur Mythological king of Sweden Succeeded by:
1 CONT Domar
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ynglingatal
1 CONT     * Ynglinga saga (part of the Heimskringla)
1 CONT     * Historia Norwegiae
0 @N6000000003051322510@ NOTE Domaldi succeeded Visbur, but he was sacrificed by the nobles in order to end a famine brought about by his treachery (according to legend). [Royal Families of Medieval Scandinavia, Flanders, and Kiev]
