0 @N6000000003949928508@ NOTE The Oppland region occupies central-southern Norway, and does not border on the sea. It contains the Jotunheimen, Rondane, and Dovrefjell mountains. Cutting the high ground are two major valleys, Gudbrandsdalen and Valdres. Opplan
1 CONC d remained isolated and sparsely populated throughout the Viking Age, and is still a region of solitude and wilderness. Halfdan 'lived to be an old man, and died in his bed at Toten, from whence his body was transported to Vestfol
1 CONC d, and was buried under a mound at a place called Skaereid, at Skiringsale.' [Ynglinga Saga, ch. 49.] Halfdan ordered the building of a pagan temple at Skaerid, and a little more about early Norse beliefs may be of interest, so as
1 CONC  to build up a better understanding of our ancestors in our imaginations.
