0 @N6000000009304990254@ NOTE #Générale#de gueules au lion rampant d'or
0 @N6000000000437140293@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> III
0 @N6000000003949767617@ NOTE  orginally had Eustace holding Roeux, which is in Artois (now the department of Pas-de-Calais) in France, which is just south of Belgium making it seem reasonable. It turns out, according to Leo van de Pas, citing ES, that Eustace
1 CONC  is of Roeulx, which is in Belgium. Just one letter can make a big difference.
1 CONT Leo van de Pas, citing ES, has "Eustache Canivet, Sire du Roeulx", as father of Agnes, while he was "Eustache III Canivet, Sire de Roeulx" as wife of Marie de Mortagne. I believe that they are the same person. With Agnes' late bir
1 CONC th date compared to Eustache's, maybe there is a question of which Eustache was father of Agnes. There were three Eustache Sire de Rouelx descendants of this Eustache.
0 @N6000000009305017489@ NOTE #Générale#Eustache III ou Wistaffe, dit Canivet (1190-1210) devient seigneur du Roeulx  et de Morlanwelz  lorsque son grand-père part pour la croisade en 1190.Wistaffe du Rues scelle la charte du Hainaut  en 1200 3. Il est encore 
1 CONC cité dans des chartes de 1197, 1198, 1199, 1210 et confirme, en 1202, la fondation de l'hôpital du Roeulx. Son épouse est Béatrix, fille de Baudouin, châtelain de Tournai et Hildegarde de Wavrin qui lui donne : Eustache IV et une 
1 CONC fille qui épouse Jacques de Condé, chevalier et sire de Bailleul  (Beloeil) et de Morialmé.
0 @N6000000000437611324@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> III
0 @N6000000009305086802@ NOTE #Générale#D'or à trois lions de gueules Cri LE ROEUX A MON TOUR!
0 @N6000000009305175320@ NOTE #Générale#d'argent à l'écusson de guelles à l'orle de 9 merlettes de sable
0 @N6000000009304961373@ NOTE #Générale#Marchand hansé en 1283, receveur de la hanse en 1284, 1286 et 1296, mayeur de Saint Omer en 1289, 1291, 1293, 1295, 1297, 1299,1301, 1303
0 @N6000000003220311488@ NOTE Han ble slått til ridder av kong Magnus Lagabøte 1277 og fikk senere også tittel av baron. Var kongelig sysselmann i Viken, men han holdt seg mest hjemme på Bjarkøy. Han ble gift med datter av Hr. Andres til Stovrheim, som igjen v
1 CONC ar sønn av Hr. Gregorius Andresson og hustru Cecilia, datter av kong Håkon Håkonsson. Dette ekteskap kom i stand for å bilegge et langvarig fiendskap mellom begges slekt og venner.
0 @N6000000005561621643@ NOTE Steinar Aasulvson (i Trøndelagen) Herka f. (?) 1235.
