0 @N6000000000945068101@ NOTE Jarl i Trøndelag. 
1 CONT Grjotgard hadde sin hovedgård på Svelven innenfor Agdenes
1 CONT Også på den annen side av Trondheimsfjorden må Håløy-jarlene ha hatt makt, da de
1 CONT siden kalles yrnernes eller ørlændernes jarler. Han var sammen med sin sønn Håkon ved
1 CONT midten av det 9. århundre herre over innseilingen til Trondheimsfjorden.
1 CONT Han ble drept på sin hovedgård av en berserk og der er hans gravhaug.
0 @N6000000007329350070@ NOTE [MAGNUS.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT Hadde sin hovedgård på Svelven innenfor Agdenes.
0 @N6000000003796269368@ NOTE The Yngling Saga of Heimskingla
1 CONT The Saga of the Norse Kings by Snorri Sturleson
1 CONT (dates may be off):
1 CONT
1 CONT 7. DOMAR - King of Sweden from 130 A.D. until his death in 162. Domar had a long and peaceful reign. He was married to Drott, daughter of King Danp, and sister of King Dan Mikkillati, after whom Denmark was named. Their son was:
1 CONT
1 CONT 8. DYGVE 
0 @N6000000003220311284@ NOTE {geni:comment} http://www.look.no/anita/slekt/webcards/ps05/ps05_028.htm
1 CONT {geni:comment} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drott
0 @N6000000003796269330@ NOTE The Yngling Saga of Heimskingla
1 CONT The Saga of the Norse Kings by Snorri Sturleson
1 CONT (dates may be off):
1 CONT
1 CONT 8. DYGVE - King of Sweden from 162 until he died in his bed in 190. His son was:
1 CONT
1 CONT 9. DAG 
0 @N6000000002187696017@ NOTE Dyggve
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Dygvi, Dyggve or Digne was according to Ynglingatal a Swedish king of the House of Ynglings. He died in bed and never reached Valhalla. Instead he went to Hel, Loki's daughter, who acquired a husband of royal blood. In Ynglinga sa
1 CONC ga, Snorri Sturluson included a piece from Ynglingatal composed in the 9th century:
1 CONT
1 CONT     Kveðkat dul,
1 CONT     nema Dyggva hrör
1 CONT     Glitnis gná
1 CONT     at gamni hefr,
1 CONT     því at jódis
1 CONT     Ulfs ok Narfa
1 CONT     Konungmann
1 CONT     kjósa skyldi;
1 CONT     ok allvald
1 CONT     Yngva þjóðar
1 CONT     Loka mær
1 CONT     of leikinn hefr.[1]
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     Dygve the Brave, the mighty king,
1 CONT     It is no hidden secret thing,
1 CONT     Has gone to meet a royal mate,
1 CONT     Riding upon the horse of Fate.
1 CONT     For Loke's daughter in her house
1 CONT     Of Yngve's race would have a spouse;
1 CONT     Therefore the fell-one snatched away
1 CONT     Brave Dygve from the light of day.(Laing's translation [2])
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Domar Mythological king of Sweden Succeeded by:
1 CONT Dag the Wise
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Ynglingatal
1 CONT     * Ynglinga saga (part of the Heimskringla)
1 CONT     * Historia Norwegiae
0 @N6000000003220311274@ NOTE {geni:comment} http://www.look.no/anita/slekt/webcards/ps05/ps05_026.htm
1 CONT {geni:comment} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dyggvi
0 @N6000000000337410056@ NOTE Weis, p. 110, Jarl of the Upplands, c. 830;  said to have fathered two children: swanhild, who married Harald, King of Norway - and Ragnvald.
0 @N6000000001355635270@ NOTE Sources: A. Roots 121E, 143A; RC 44, 166; Kraentzler 1453, 1593, 1609, 1645;
1 CONT AF; The Dukes of Normandy and Their Origins; Pfafman; History of the Vikings;
1 CONT Russell.
1 CONT RC:Eistein Ivarsson, Jarl of Hedemarken (of the Uplands), ca 830.
1 CONT Roots: Eystein Glumra, Jarl of the Upplands, ca. 830, said to have fathered
1 CONT two known children: Swanhild and Ragnvald I.
1 CONT K. calls him Eystein Ivarsson, aka Euslin "Ghimrice/Ghemvice" of Schleswig.
1 CONT K: Eystein "Glumra" Ivarsson, Count of Maere (More). Jarl of the Uplanders
1 CONT in Norway.
1 CONT Russell: Eisten Glumru of Vors, A.D. 870. Names Rogvald as a son, butnot
1 CONT son Malahue and daughter Swanhild. Names instead Sigurd, Jarl of the Orkneys,
1 CONT andd Huldrich, ancestor of Raoul de Toeny.
1 CONT Eystein Glumra was the Earl of Moera (various spellings for this) in Norway
1 CONT and Jarl of Orkney and Shetland.
1 CONT According to both the Heimskringla Saga and the Orkneyinga Saga, Eystein
1 CONT Glumra was the father of Rognvald. The Orkneyinga Saga says Eystein Glumra's
1 CONT earliest forebear was Fornjot, King of Finland and Kvenland. Fornjot's
1 CONT great-great-grandson was Thorri, or Fhorri, who had two sons, Norr and Gorr,
1 CONT who emigrated westward. Norr took the mainland called Norway and Gorrtook the
1 CONT islands. Gorr's son Heiti was the father of Sveithi (Sveide), the SeaKing,
1 CONT who died about 760. Sveithi's son, Halfdan the Old, who died in 800, was the
1 CONT father of Ivar, Earl of the Uplands. And Ivar, in turn, was the father of
1 CONT Eystein Glumra.
1 CONT RC 44 calls this man Eistein Ivarsson, son of Ivar, who was son of Halfdan
1 CONT the Old. So it follows the Sagas for three generations.
1 CONT There was no written language during this period, and the Norse sagas
1 CONT provided oral histories, much like those Alex Haley, author of "Roots,"
1 CONT found in Africa.
