1 CONT NOTE:
1 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
1 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E, 143A; RC 44, 166; Kraentzler 1453, 1593, 1609, 1645; AF; The Dukes of Normandy and Their Origins; Pfafman; History of theVikings; Russell. RC:Eistein Ivarsson, Jarl of Hedemarken (of the Uplands), ca 830. R
1 CONC oots: Eystein Glumra, Jarl of the Upplands, ca. 830, said to have fathered
1 CONT two known children: Swanhild and Ragnvald I. K. calls him Eystein Ivarsson, aka Euslin "Ghimrice/Ghemvice" ofSchleswig. K: Eystein "Glumra" Ivarsson, Count of Maere (More). Jarl of theUplanders in Norway.
1 CONT Russell: Eisten Glumru of Vors, A.D. 870. Names Rogvald as a son, but not son Malahue and daughter Swanhild. Names instead Sigurd, Jarl of theOrkneys, and Huldrich, ancestor of Raoul de Toeny.
1 CONT Eystein Glumra was the Earl of Moera (various spellings for this) in Norway
1 CONT and Jarl of Orkney and Shetland. According to both the Heimskringla Saga and the Orkneyinga Saga,Eystein
1 CONT Glumra was the father of Rognvald. The Orkneyinga Saga says EysteinGlumra's earliest forebear was Fornjot, King of Finland and Kvenland. Fornjot's great-great-grandson was Thorri, or Fhorri, who had two sons, Norr andGorr, who emi
1 CONC grated westward. Norr took the mainland called Norway and Gorrtook the
1 CONT islands. Gorr's son Heiti was the father of Sveithi (Sveide), the SeaKing, who died about 760. Sveithi's son, Halfdan the Old, who died in 800, was the father of Ivar, Earl of the Uplands. And Ivar, in turn, was the father of
1 CONT Eystein Glumra.
1 CONT RC 44 calls this man Eistein Ivarsson, son of Ivar, who was son ofHalfdan
1 CONT the Old. So it follows the Sagas for three generations.
1 CONT There was no written language during this period, and the Norse sagas
1 CONT provided oral histories, much like those Alex Haley, author of "Roots, "
1 CONT found in Africa.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1  NAME Eystein The Noisy /Glumra/, Of The Uplanders
1 CONT 1  BIRT
1 CONT 2  DATE 788
1 CONT 1  BIRT
1 CONT 2  DATE ABT. 800
1 CONT 2  PLAC of, Maer, Nord Trondelag, Norway
1 CONT 2  SOUR S119232
1 CONT 3  DATA
