0 @N6000000003051240844@ NOTE [Weis 110] Jarl of the Upplands, ca. 830, sd. to have fathered two known children: Swanhild (m. HARALD (243A-17), King of Norway), and Ragnvald I.
1 CONT
1 CONT [Wikipedia, "Eystein Ivarsson", retrieved 20 Jul 08]
1 CONT Eystein Glumra also called Eystein Ivarsson (born 788 in Maer, Nord-Trøndelag, Norway) was a petty king of Norway, the son of Ivar Halfdan and the father of Ragnvald Eysteinsson. He was married to Ascrida Rognvaldsdatter c. 819.
