1 CONT Sources: A. Roots 121E, 243A; Norr; RC 166, 295; History of the Vikings;
1 CONT Russell; Pfafman; Kraentzler 1453, 1593; Falaise Roll, page 80; Norr, p59.
1 CONT Roots: Ragnvald I, "the Wise," Jarl of North and South More, and of Ramsdel
1 CONT in Norway, seen 867, died 890. More also spelled Moer and Maer.
1 CONT RC: Rognvald Eysteinsson "the Wise", Jarl of More, a Norwegian Viking.
1 CONT K: Regenwald de Maere & de Reumdahl in Norway. Ragnivald I, Count de Maere.
1 CONT Russell: Rogvald, Jarl of More, A.D. 885.
1 CONT
1 CONT Earl of More/Moer in Norway and Jarl of Orkney and Shetland.He had his name
1 CONT Gallicized to Reginald. He supported King Harold Fairhair in an attempt to
1 CONT unify Norway. Norr: Jarl Rognwald (Rogvald, Raonwald, Regvald, Rouis), created Earl of Moer
1 CONT in 885. Roll: Rognwald, Earl of Maere.
1 CONT Norr: JarlRogwald (Raowald, Regvald, Rouis), Earl of Moer 885. Married
1 CONT Hilder.
1 CONT Beyond Rognvald, things get pretty confused. Norr has about 25 generations
1 CONT going backto Oden. RC doesn't agree. But some RC names coming down from RC's
1 CONT Odin agreein the upper portion. But the dates are some 250 years different.
1 CONT RC and Kraentzler agree in taking Rognvald back three more generations.
1 CONT Russell goes way back to Olaf the Sharp-eyed, King of Rerik.
