0 @N6000000002187734647@ NOTE Björn Ironside
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Björn Ironside (Old Norse: Björn Járnsíða, Swedish: Björn Järnsida) Swedish king (ca 785-800) was a legendary viking from the 8th century. He was one of the sons of Ragnar Lodbrok. He pillaged in Italy and took part in the conques
1 CONC t of Paris with his father Ragnar Lodbrok.
1 CONT
1 CONT He acquired the name Ironside because he was never wounded in battle. This invulnerability was attributed to his mother Aslaug's use of seid in order to make him impervious to iron and steel.
1 CONT
1 CONT According to Hervarar saga he inherited Sweden from his father while his brother Sigurd Snake-Eye inherited the remainder of Scandinavia.
1 CONT
1 CONT The dynasty he founded is called the House of Munsö by modern historians, because a local tradition claims that he is buried in Björnshögen at Husby on the island of Munsö. Many of his dynasty were to be named Björn.
1 CONT
1 CONT He had two sons, Refil and Erik Björnsson, and Erik succeeded him on the throne.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT See also
1 CONT Early Swedish History 
1 CONT House of Munsö 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Östen Beli Semi-legendary king of Sweden Succeeded by:
1 CONT Erik Björnsson 
