1 CONT
1 CONT Ganger Rolf, the Viking (or Rollo), was banished from Norway to the Hebrides about 867, participated in Viking attack on Bayeux in 890, where Count Berenger of Bayeux was killed, and his daughter Poppa captured and taken, 886, by 
1 CONC Rollo (now called Count of Rouen) as his "Danish" wife.  Under Treaty of St. Claire, 911, received the Duchy of Normandy from Charles III, "the Simple".
