0 @N6000000003949876699@ NOTE From: PDeloriol@aol.com (PDeloriol@aol.com) Subject: DE ROE(L)T...
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval Date: 2004-01-04 09:57:45 PST
1 CONT Someone asked about the ancestry of sir Paon/Pagan/Payen de Ruet/Roet/Roelt.
1 CONT A recent article in the Foundations Magazine of the Foundation for Medieval Genealogy suggests that this unknown Knight was a member of the ROEULX family of the Hainaut where the name is also spelt as Ruet/Roet/ Ruelt - it points 
1 CONC to a certain Gilles de Roeulx as the Pagan of English history...there is however no definite proof of his identity but the circumstantial proof seems quite compelling according to the reviewer.
1 CONT Note: I already have Payne as son of another Payne Roet, based on various people on the internet. I find a Gilles-Rigaud de Roeulx on Leo van de Pas' data files based on information in ES. Since the senior male line of Gille's eld
1 CONC er brother Eustace appears to die out with Eustace in 1288 (Eustace had a son Eustace who died before him about Dec 1287, and a daughter Marie who was his heir), I think the Roet descent indicated in the SGM post above is probably
1 CONC  through Gilles-Rigaud. Therefore I am making Payne Roet, senior, a son of that Gilles-Rigaud (at least it is pretty close to the ancestry indicated above).
